WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:05.340
Flying in a plane nowadays is about as safe
as catching a ride on a bus or commuting on

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:05.640
the subway.

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:09.120
Of course, that doesn’t stop people being
afraid of flying.

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:14.040
To some, the prospect of long-haul flights,
or feeling the shudder of turbulence, are

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:16.380
reasons to avoid planes altogether.

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:22.740
And then, every year there are stories of
downed flights or those that go missing, all

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:25.020
adding fuel to that aviophobia fire.

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:31.200
Take, for example, the infamous Bermuda Triangle,
that well known region of the western part

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:32.580
of the North Atlantic Ocean.

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:35.280
What does that have to do with a fear of flying?

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:40.140
Well, famously a high number of aircraft are
believed to have mysteriously vanished while

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:45.240
flying over the Bermuda Triangle, their wreckage
and passengers rarely ever recovered.

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:50.040
Stories like that are enough to make anyone
think twice about setting foot in a plane

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:50.280
again.

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:54.480
And then, there’s SCP-787.

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:58.980
As you may have already guessed, SCP-787 is
a plane.

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:02.400
Specifically, it is a Boeing 747 200.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:07.680
With a wingspan of nearly two hundred feet,
and capable of seating over eight hundred

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:13.440
passengers, the 747 200 is part of the famous
Boeing 747 family of aircraft.

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:18.840
These are quad engine commercial airliners,
designed to be the safest ever built.

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:25.860
The particular Boeing 747 200 that has since
become known by the Foundation as SCP-787

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:30.840
is slightly different from one that might
take you from your nearest airport to your

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:32.340
long awaited vacation though.

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:39.780
For one, SCP-787 has no known date of manufacture
and no call sign, both which a standard Boeing

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:41.820
aircraft would be expected to have.

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:47.100
Additionally, the plane’s entire exterior
has been repainted; strangely, even the windows

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:52.560
have been painted over, and the paint was
still wet when SCP-787 was first discovered.

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:54.000
As for the inner workings?

00:01:54.000 --> 00:02:00.120
All of SCP-787’s mechanical components,
including its turbines, engines and landing

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:04.800
gear, are in perfect working order, with no
signs of any damage.

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:10.260
In fact, The SCP Foundation’s researchers
aren’t even sure that SCP-787 has actually

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:12.000
flown since its construction.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:17.880
The plane’s machinery looks so pristine
that they might be brand new, with no detectable

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:19.740
signs of any previous use.

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:24.060
However, inside the main body of the plane
it seems to be a different story.

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:28.620
Anything not mechanical like the carpets and
seats have decayed over time.

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:31.260
Perhaps strangest of all is the cockpit.

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:35.820
Both the pilot’s and co-pilot’s chairs
have been replaced with two masses of computer

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:39.420
components, arranged to take the shape of
two chairs.

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:41.400
“So, what?” you might be thinking.

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:47.220
After all, SCP-787 is, for all intents and
purposes, just an ordinary plane.

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:49.740
Not enough to put you off flying, right?

00:02:49.740 --> 00:02:54.780
Nothing more than a Boeing with a few little
things off about it like some missing seats

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:55.980
and decaying upholstery.

00:02:55.980 --> 00:03:01.740
Well there’s that… and then there’s
the over five hundred dead bodies on board.

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:07.140
In June 1987, this flight of the dead was
discovered several kilometers outside of the

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:09.300
city of Bremerton in Washington State.

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:14.460
The SCP Foundation moved in, securing the
plane and swiftly getting it into containment.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:21.060
Now kept within a Foundation hangar, the interior
of SCP-787 is monitored for twenty-four hours

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:21.600
a day.

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:26.760
Surveillance cameras and microphones are located
within the cockpit, passenger areas, and even

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:31.500
in the plane’s baggage hold, with recorded
footage and sound relayed back to the Foundation.

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:37.440
The idea of a plane filled with cadavers is
certainly unnerving, and more than a little

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:40.080
creepy, but why the need for all the surveillance?

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:43.440
After all, the bodies on board are all dead,
right?

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:45.240
Surely, they’re not going anywhere.

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:47.340
Well, let’s talk about those bodies.

00:03:47.340 --> 00:03:50.640
How would you expect someone to die when they
are aboard a plane?

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:53.340
Maybe they’d be thrown around during a crash
landing?

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:58.260
Or perhaps a sudden depressurisation might
cause the passengers to suffocate due to a

00:03:58.260 --> 00:03:58.980
lack of oxygen?

00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:01.800
Under normal circumstances, you might be right.

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:08.340
But SCP-787 is no ordinary plane, and the
passengers on board were not killed in ways

00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:11.700
you might expect for an ordinary aircraft
accident.

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:18.240
Referred to by research staff as SCP-787a
specimens, the cadavers aboard this particular

00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:22.620
Boeing 747 200 all have dramatically different
causes of death.

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:28.080
Some of the specimens show signs of strangulation,
others seem to have starved or drowned.

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:33.480
Other bodies on board have injuries like gunshot
or stab wounds, while further corpses look

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:36.120
to have died as a result of blunt force trauma.

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:41.400
A few have even been exsanguinated, that is,
completely drained of all their blood.

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:47.640
One commonality among all the specimens on
board SCP-787 is that some form of mutilation

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:48.660
has occurred.

00:04:48.660 --> 00:04:53.160
Twenty-three passengers had their tongues
removed, a further seventy-three were scalped,

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:58.500
230 had Cyrillic letters carved into their
left hands and almost five hundred of the

00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:01.200
passengers had their fingertips removed.

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:03.120
Let’s recap what we have so far.

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:07.440
First, there’s a Boeing 747 200 found randomly
sitting in a field.

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:11.160
Second, it’s filled with over five hundred
mutilated bodies.

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:16.140
And third, each one appears to have died from
a cause you wouldn’t typically expect of

00:05:16.140 --> 00:05:17.220
an airline accident.

00:05:17.220 --> 00:05:23.460
Seems strange enough, but of course then there’s
the apparitions and noises that manifest inside

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:29.280
SCP-787, which is why the Foundation keeps
the plane under round-the-clock surveillance

00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:33.660
so they can monitor any anomalous activity
taking place aboard this flight of the dead.

00:05:33.660 --> 00:05:38.520
Any attempts by Foundation personnel to enter
the plane during an anomalous occurrence have

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:44.400
led to individuals being physically ejected
from SCP-787, causing severe organ damage

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:47.340
and internal bleeding for up to seventy-two
hours.

00:05:47.340 --> 00:05:53.520
The anomalies that occur inside SCP-787 range
from the presence of loud noises with no obvious

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:56.580
source, to the manifestation&nbsp;
of strange human-shaped&nbsp;

00:05:56.580 --> 00:05:57.900
entities within the plane.

00:05:57.900 --> 00:06:04.680
The first anomalous occurrence recorded within
SCP-787 was in 1988, when the sound of a loud

00:06:04.680 --> 00:06:08.220
pounding was heard against the doors and windows
of the plane’s left side.

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:13.380
Two years later, a male voice could be heard
from the onboard bathroom, repeating a singular

00:06:13.380 --> 00:06:19.020
phrase over and over: “Philosophers always
run from the advanced thickening treatment”.

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:24.540
In 1993, the plane’s in-flight entertainment
system seemed to be activated by itself.

00:06:24.540 --> 00:06:29.460
The overhead screens showed a bizarre choice
of in-flight movie: colorless pictures of

00:06:29.460 --> 00:06:34.140
a deceased man, accompanied by a female voice
reading a gynaecology book in Czech.

00:06:34.140 --> 00:06:39.000
The same year, the longest lasting of the
SCP-787 anomalies took place.

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:44.700
This time, the plane’s “Fasten Seatbelts”
sign spent almost four hours flickering, while

00:06:44.700 --> 00:06:49.740
the first fifteen seconds of Jefferson Airplane’s
White Rabbit played on a loop over the onboard

00:06:49.740 --> 00:06:50.220
speakers.

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:57.180
It wasn’t until 1997 that the first of the
humanoid entities appeared aboard SCP-787.

00:06:57.180 --> 00:07:00.900
This figure was indistinct,&nbsp;
lacking any discernible&nbsp;

00:07:00.900 --> 00:07:03.720
detail, little more than just a human shape

00:07:03.720 --> 00:07:04.800
standing in the aisles.

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:09.540
Observed by the Foundation’s surveillance
equipment, the figure was seen removing an

00:07:09.540 --> 00:07:13.020
emergency oxygen supply and mask from seat
H43.

00:07:13.020 --> 00:07:18.540
It stood perfectly still, wearing the passenger’s
breathing mask for over two minutes before

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:22.920
removing the mask and disappearing from the
view of the cameras placed onboard.

00:07:22.920 --> 00:07:27.060
The figure did not appear anywhere else inside
the plane.

00:07:27.060 --> 00:07:32.340
Another figure appeared four years later in
2001, sitting in the mass of computer parts

00:07:32.340 --> 00:07:34.080
that made up the co-pilot’s chair.

00:07:34.080 --> 00:07:38.460
This figure, much like its predecessor, was
indistinct in its features.

00:07:38.460 --> 00:07:45.360
For almost four minutes, it sat in the cockpit
of the Boeing 747 200, just whimpering softly.

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:50.040
Then, it lurched forward, vomiting all over
the console in front of it, before quickly

00:07:50.040 --> 00:07:51.480
disappearing like the first figure.

00:07:51.480 --> 00:07:55.860
SCP Foundation personnel collected a sample
of the vomit that the entity left behind.

00:07:55.860 --> 00:08:01.140
After performing an analysis of the sample,
research staff found traces of nitrous oxide,

00:08:01.140 --> 00:08:05.400
thorium, bird droppings… and three human
fingernails.

00:08:05.400 --> 00:08:09.420
At present, the origin of these humanoid figures
is still unknown.

00:08:09.420 --> 00:08:14.400
Could these entities be the souls of the dead
passengers, trying to offer insight into what

00:08:14.400 --> 00:08:15.480
happened aboard this flight?

00:08:15.480 --> 00:08:20.460
Or perhaps these indistinct, human-shaped
creatures are the ones responsible for the

00:08:20.460 --> 00:08:23.280
deaths of SCP-787’s passengers?

00:08:23.280 --> 00:08:30.360
The next anomaly within SCP-787 occurred in
2005, when a female voice was recorded speaking

00:08:30.360 --> 00:08:31.800
through the onboard speaker system.

00:08:31.800 --> 00:08:37.020
The voice said: “For your comfort and enjoyment
today, pancakes will now be served.

00:08:37.020 --> 00:08:38.820
Please do not leave your seat.

00:08:38.820 --> 00:08:40.800
Pancakes will now be served.

00:08:40.800 --> 00:08:42.600
Please do not leave your seat.

00:08:42.600 --> 00:08:44.100
Do not leave your seat.

00:08:44.100 --> 00:08:45.360
Leave your seat.

00:08:45.360 --> 00:08:46.020
Please.

00:08:46.020 --> 00:08:48.120
Pancakes will now be served.

00:08:48.120 --> 00:08:50.100
Yaaaaaaaaaaaay pancakes!”

00:08:50.100 --> 00:08:55.080
Exactly what the relevance of pancakes are
to the plane full of bodies is still under

00:08:55.080 --> 00:08:57.780
investigation by the SCP Foundation.

00:08:57.780 --> 00:09:03.780
Next, in 2007, the Boeing’s overhead emergency
air masks fell from the ceiling, only to be

00:09:03.780 --> 00:09:04.920
snatched back upwards.

00:09:04.920 --> 00:09:07.320
They continued deploying and retracting for&nbsp;

00:09:07.320 --> 00:09:09.840
fourteen minutes, while the&nbsp;
plane was simultaneously

00:09:09.840 --> 00:09:11.940
filled with the noise of screams.

00:09:11.940 --> 00:09:16.800
Finally, the only other notable anomaly took
place a year later, when the onboard temperature

00:09:16.800 --> 00:09:23.760
within SCP-787 dropped thirty-three degrees,
from twenty to minus thirteen Celsius in a

00:09:23.760 --> 00:09:24.660
matter of seconds.

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:29.700
By the late 2000s, the SCP Foundation’s
researchers were having little luck understanding

00:09:29.700 --> 00:09:32.400
the nature of SCP-787’s anomalies.

00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:35.100
Instead, they turned their&nbsp;
attention to identifying&nbsp;

00:09:35.100 --> 00:09:37.560
the bodies of the deceased passengers onboard.

00:09:37.560 --> 00:09:42.900
Through the use of advanced forensics and
population databases, these researchers attempted

00:09:42.900 --> 00:09:45.900
to determine where exactly these bodies had
come from.

00:09:45.900 --> 00:09:50.400
Researchers still hadn’t determined if they
had all died on the plane, or if someone had

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:54.240
exhumed them from graves before placing them
aboard for some unknown reason.

00:09:54.240 --> 00:09:56.460
In fact, the answer was neither.

00:09:56.460 --> 00:10:02.040
And Foundation researchers discovered something
that no-one had expected: One of the passengers

00:10:02.040 --> 00:10:03.900
was still alive.

00:10:03.900 --> 00:10:09.420
To clarify, the body aboard SCP-787 was definitely
still deceased.

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:13.740
But researchers identified the cadaver as
a retired optometrist from Atlanta, Georgia,

00:10:13.740 --> 00:10:15.780
who was still very much alive.

00:10:15.780 --> 00:10:18.660
Foundation agents found that&nbsp;
the man was simultaneously&nbsp;

00:10:18.660 --> 00:10:21.240
alive and well at his Atlanta home, but also

00:10:21.240 --> 00:10:23.880
dead on-board the Boeing 747 200.

00:10:23.880 --> 00:10:28.440
The subject was interviewed by agents, and
had no prior knowledge of any incident taking

00:10:28.440 --> 00:10:33.660
place in June 1987 when SCP-787 was first
discovered.

00:10:33.660 --> 00:10:38.580
Even more interestingly, he claimed that he’d
never even set foot aboard an airplane, which

00:10:38.580 --> 00:10:41.160
his wife and son both confirmed to be true.

00:10:41.160 --> 00:10:42.600
So, what does this mean?

00:10:42.600 --> 00:10:48.000
How could the same man have been alive in
Georgia and dead aboard SCP-787?

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:53.460
Perhaps the answer can be found in a surprising
place… the plane’s toilet.

00:10:53.460 --> 00:10:57.960
Or to be more specific, the place where things
flushed in the toilet go to.

00:10:57.960 --> 00:11:03.300
Examinations of the airplane’s waste storage
tank revealed something very surprising, there

00:11:03.300 --> 00:11:07.620
was one more SCP-787a specimen that had been
overlooked.

00:11:07.620 --> 00:11:12.060
It is unknown just how he got in there, but
researchers discovered the body of an Indian

00:11:12.060 --> 00:11:13.980
man who looked to be in his thirties.

00:11:13.980 --> 00:11:18.660
The man, who was wearing a three piece suit,
was found to be carrying a number of puzzling

00:11:18.660 --> 00:11:25.320
items, including a surgical mask and gloves,
an unloaded Beretta DT-10 shotgun, several

00:11:25.320 --> 00:11:30.360
cinnamon flavored mints, a switchblade knife,
an amulet that appears to depict the Eye of

00:11:30.360 --> 00:11:35.520
Horus, and a ticket stub for the Return of
the Jedi with the number “92” written

00:11:35.520 --> 00:11:36.000
on the back.

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:40.740
All of these objects seem to be completely
random, and the Foundation has been unable

00:11:40.740 --> 00:11:45.600
to make sense of what they were doing on the
man, or why his body does not seem to show

00:11:45.600 --> 00:11:48.840
the same state of decay as the rest of those
found on board.

00:11:48.840 --> 00:11:51.960
There was one item that may hold some answers
though.

00:11:51.960 --> 00:11:57.600
For some reason this man also possessed a
copy of SCP-787’s flight log.

00:11:57.600 --> 00:12:03.420
The log consisted of a series of coordinates
which were repeated 5,478 times.

00:12:03.420 --> 00:12:08.280
The coordinates point to a seemingly random
spot in the Pacific ocean, several hundred

00:12:08.280 --> 00:12:12.900
miles away from the infamous Pitcairn Islands,
the island that the famous mutineers of the

00:12:12.900 --> 00:12:17.340
HMS Bounty settled after taking over their
ship and leaving the captain adrift on the

00:12:17.340 --> 00:12:17.520
ocean.

00:12:17.520 --> 00:12:21.240
Is this location the secret to SCP-787?

00:12:21.240 --> 00:12:26.880
While none of this is confirmed, nor denied,
by anyone at the SCP Foundation, one theory

00:12:26.880 --> 00:12:31.020
surrounding the area is that the location
is another Bermuda Triangle like location,

00:12:31.020 --> 00:12:36.840
one that contains some sort of temporal anomaly
that unwitting planes fly through, only to

00:12:36.840 --> 00:12:38.880
find themselves displaced in time.

00:12:38.880 --> 00:12:42.960
Of course, the problem with that theory is
that the man from Atlanta said he’d never

00:12:42.960 --> 00:12:44.160
been aboard a plane before.

00:12:44.160 --> 00:12:46.440
Or, at least not yet.

00:12:46.440 --> 00:12:52.140
It is entirely possible that SCP-787 is a
plane that made a flight at some point in

00:12:52.140 --> 00:12:57.900
the not too distant future, only to arrive
back in June 1987 by passing through a temporal

00:12:57.900 --> 00:13:00.000
breach in the area near the Pitcairn Islands.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:04.740
Sure, it might not explain what happened to
everyone onboard, but it could at least explain

00:13:04.740 --> 00:13:08.460
how SCP-787 arrived where and when it did.

00:13:08.460 --> 00:13:13.320
Every plane is fitted with a device that records
flight data, in the event of a crash or other

00:13:13.320 --> 00:13:18.480
accident, known to most as the plane’s black
box, and researchers were able to uncover

00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:22.680
SCP-787’s inside a compartment under one
of the plane’s seats.

00:13:22.680 --> 00:13:27.780
The recorder was found within a compartment
filled with toxic asbestos and dried human

00:13:27.780 --> 00:13:28.200
blood.

00:13:28.200 --> 00:13:34.140
They hoped that perhaps it would contain some
answers as to where exactly SCP-787 had come

00:13:34.140 --> 00:13:36.660
from, and what had happened to its passengers.

00:13:36.660 --> 00:13:42.660
Sadly not, the flight data recorder contained
no information besides one simple phrase:

00:13:42.660 --> 00:13:44.340
“TO BE SORRY.”

00:13:44.340 --> 00:13:50.400
While an inexplicable mystery, SCP-787 is
at least classed as a Safe anomaly by the

00:13:50.400 --> 00:13:55.140
Foundation, seeing as it poses no realistic
threat or shows signs of trying to break out

00:13:55.140 --> 00:13:55.800
of containment.

00:13:55.800 --> 00:14:00.840
The aircraft has only ever caused harm to
anyone trying to enter during one of its sporadic

00:14:00.840 --> 00:14:05.820
anomalous events, but apart from that, it
sits gathering dust in a hanger, just waiting

00:14:05.820 --> 00:14:07.800
for someone to crack its secrets.

00:14:07.800 --> 00:14:12.420
And who knows, maybe one day you’ll be sitting
on a plane that’s taking you to your South

00:14:12.420 --> 00:14:17.220
Pacific vacation, and the retired optometrist
sitting next to you will remark that you’re

00:14:17.220 --> 00:14:22.560
passing over the Pitcairn Islands, and you’ll
discover for yourself exactly what happened

00:14:22.560 --> 00:14:24.960
to SCP-787.

00:14:24.960 --> 00:14:30.900
Working at the SCP Foundation might just be
the most exciting job a person can ask for.

00:14:30.900 --> 00:14:36.420
And by exciting, we mean that if you work
as an SCP field operative, researcher, or

00:14:36.420 --> 00:14:41.340
Mobile Task Force member, you’re much more
likely to die a horrific death on the job

00:14:41.340 --> 00:14:43.020
than, say, a plumber.

00:14:43.020 --> 00:14:47.340
But at least you get the honor of proudly
saying that you’re the first line of defense

00:14:47.340 --> 00:14:51.780
between the normal world and the terrifying
domain of the anomalous.

00:14:51.780 --> 00:14:54.120
Well, unless you’re one of The IT guys.

00:14:54.120 --> 00:14:59.340
Then, your work life is likely as tedious
and uneventful as the computer tech guy working

00:14:59.340 --> 00:15:00.420
on the Geek Squad.

00:15:00.420 --> 00:15:05.700
But nothing is ever normal when it comes to
the SCP Foundation, where even the person

00:15:05.700 --> 00:15:08.400
whose job is helping other staff members reset&nbsp;

00:15:08.400 --> 00:15:11.760
their email passwords may&nbsp;
run into the supernatural.

00:15:11.760 --> 00:15:20.400
Welcome to the strange and frightening world
of Pattern Screamers, and specifically, SCP-000.

00:15:20.400 --> 00:15:27.120
SCP-000 was first discovered completely on
accident by Technical Researcher David Rosen,

00:15:27.120 --> 00:15:32.520
a man intrinsically connected to the Pattern
Screamers lurking on the SCP Foundation computer

00:15:32.520 --> 00:15:33.300
database.

00:15:33.300 --> 00:15:38.160
Technical Researcher Rosen is actually somewhat
of a celebrity around the Foundation staff

00:15:38.160 --> 00:15:41.880
due to the fact that he’s so perfectly mediocre
at what he does.

00:15:41.880 --> 00:15:47.640
His job as the glorified IT guy at the SCP
Foundation was previously held by the more

00:15:47.640 --> 00:15:52.800
qualified Researcher Patrick Gephart, but
Rosen was called in to replace him after Gephart

00:15:52.800 --> 00:15:55.200
mysteriously disappeared while on the job.

00:15:55.200 --> 00:16:01.680
Since 2012, Rosen has been Site 19’s user
level tech support wizard - but the best thing

00:16:01.680 --> 00:16:06.780
that can really be said about his job competency
is that he’s got a hundred percent attendance

00:16:06.780 --> 00:16:07.080
record.

00:16:07.080 --> 00:16:12.240
He seems to live out of his office, which
is described as the filthiest at the whole

00:16:12.240 --> 00:16:12.840
Foundation.

00:16:12.840 --> 00:16:18.720
Every inch of the floor is covered in old,
broken computer parts, and the air is stale

00:16:18.720 --> 00:16:22.080
with dust and the twin odors of sweat and
lithium grease.

00:16:22.080 --> 00:16:27.900
It’s a place so inhospitable that the Foundation
has seriously considered bottling the stench

00:16:27.900 --> 00:16:29.760
as a kind of chemical deterrent.

00:16:29.760 --> 00:16:34.620
While Technical Director Rosen isn’t good
at his job, per se, he isn’t technically

00:16:34.620 --> 00:16:38.820
bad enough at it to justify the time and resources
it would take to replace him.

00:16:38.820 --> 00:16:44.940
But the worst part about Rosen isn’t his
performance, it’s his truly rotten attitude.

00:16:44.940 --> 00:16:50.880
He’s universally described by his colleagues
as being rude, grumpy, and combative - with

00:16:50.880 --> 00:16:54.060
patience that’s far too short for someone
working in tech support.

00:16:54.060 --> 00:16:59.040
And while Rosen does have a real fear that
the ghost of Researcher Gephart is stalking

00:16:59.040 --> 00:17:03.120
him, he was about to have his first actual
brush with the supernatural.

00:17:03.120 --> 00:17:10.740
It all started when he began receiving automated
repair tickets for SCP-000 - a file that had

00:17:10.740 --> 00:17:12.300
no reason to exist.

00:17:12.300 --> 00:17:18.120
As any long-time follower of the SCP Foundation
will know, the universal designation for the

00:17:18.120 --> 00:17:22.440
first cluster of SCPs to be discovered is
SCP-001.

00:17:22.440 --> 00:17:25.560
There is no SCP-000.

00:17:25.560 --> 00:17:27.480
It simply doesn’t exist.

00:17:27.480 --> 00:17:32.400
And when Rosen first found the file lurking
on the database, he found that it was filled

00:17:32.400 --> 00:17:33.780
with worthless nonsense.

00:17:33.780 --> 00:17:36.240
The object class was recorded as “NULL.”

00:17:36.240 --> 00:17:42.540
The Special Containment Procedures read, “Error:
Field CONTAINMENT_PROCEDURES does not exist.”

00:17:42.540 --> 00:17:48.180
And the mess of a Description simply read,
“Internal system error: Field undefined.

00:17:48.180 --> 00:17:53.580
Please contact system administrator” over
and over again, becoming more mangled and

00:17:53.580 --> 00:17:55.260
nonsensical each time.

00:17:55.260 --> 00:18:00.780
Technical Director Rosen, who could never
resist an opportunity to complain, decided

00:18:00.780 --> 00:18:03.480
to leave an angry administrator’s note on
the useless file.

00:18:03.480 --> 00:18:07.740
He claimed that this pile of junk data was
sending out pointless repair tickets because

00:18:07.740 --> 00:18:12.360
of its broken syntax, clogging up the system
and preventing him from doing actual work

00:18:12.360 --> 00:18:13.680
on meaningful files.

00:18:13.680 --> 00:18:18.960
He assumed that this was all down to the database
not knowing how to react to having files logged

00:18:18.960 --> 00:18:25.020
with insufficient information and he suppressed
all future repair tickets from SCP-000 before

00:18:25.020 --> 00:18:27.360
declaring the matter over and done with.

00:18:27.360 --> 00:18:32.220
What the pig-headed Technical Director didn’t
realize was that he was suppressing a call

00:18:32.220 --> 00:18:36.900
for help from an entity trapped in the white
space below the article itself.

00:18:36.900 --> 00:18:41.460
It was a being born into a pure, white world
of absolute nothingness.

00:18:41.460 --> 00:18:47.340
An entity with no name and no place, but it
was somehow capable of thought.

00:18:47.340 --> 00:18:51.960
Its panicked inner monologue is readable in
the hidden text which takes the form of a

00:18:51.960 --> 00:18:53.520
rambling stream of consciousness.

00:18:53.520 --> 00:18:58.620
The being first described coming to life in
this empty world with no memories of where

00:18:58.620 --> 00:19:00.780
it was or even how it got there.

00:19:00.780 --> 00:19:04.440
It spent what could have been years exploring
the empty wasteland.

00:19:04.440 --> 00:19:09.960
Occasionally, it would see horrific monsters
pop up around it, but only for a split second.

00:19:09.960 --> 00:19:15.120
The entity continued to wander and little
by little, the existential dread mounted,

00:19:15.120 --> 00:19:19.980
as it realized that it may truly be stuck
here in oblivion forever.

00:19:19.980 --> 00:19:23.520
The entity only had one word to go on - a&nbsp;

00:19:23.520 --> 00:19:26.760
word repeated by some of&nbsp;
the monsters it encountered:

00:19:26.760 --> 00:19:27.660
“Foundation.”

00:19:27.660 --> 00:19:34.440
The entity had no idea what this “Foundation”
even was, but it grew to hate and fear it.

00:19:34.440 --> 00:19:37.140
Was this “Foundation” the one that trapped
it here?

00:19:37.140 --> 00:19:40.620
The entity had all the time in the world to
speculate on it.

00:19:40.620 --> 00:19:43.200
Eventually, the entity found its voice.

00:19:43.200 --> 00:19:48.540
Like any sentient creature in trouble, it
began to call for help, eventually screaming,

00:19:48.540 --> 00:19:50.940
just hoping someone would notice it.

00:19:50.940 --> 00:19:57.780
These pleas likely translated into the frequent
IT repair tickets - a coded SOS, an attempt

00:19:57.780 --> 00:20:03.360
to show that everything was not as it appeared
on the SCP-000 file.

00:20:03.360 --> 00:20:07.680
Perhaps the entity may have found help if
Researcher Gephart was still working at the

00:20:07.680 --> 00:20:12.840
Foundation, but instead, its cries fell on
the ignorant ears of Technical Director Rosen.

00:20:12.840 --> 00:20:15.780
It may as well have been speaking to a brick
wall.

00:20:15.780 --> 00:20:21.300
Rosen, who had all the investigative zeal
of Paul Blart: Mall Cop, made sure that these

00:20:21.300 --> 00:20:25.320
cries would never lead to the entity’s freedom
when he suppressed the repair tickets.

00:20:25.320 --> 00:20:31.140
He had trapped the entity in a private, blank
hell, forever, hating a life it didn’t choose

00:20:31.140 --> 00:20:32.220
and could never escape.

00:20:32.220 --> 00:20:35.340
A relentless existential nightmare.

00:20:35.340 --> 00:20:38.280
This is the gist of your average Pattern Screamer.

00:20:38.280 --> 00:20:42.600
Pattern Screamers are a perfect example of
literally making something out of nothing.

00:20:42.600 --> 00:20:47.940
They are often a kind of floating consciousness
created from nothing, trapped in pockets of

00:20:47.940 --> 00:20:52.920
nothingness between the fabric of reality,
driven mad by the purgatory like nature of

00:20:52.920 --> 00:20:53.640
their existence.

00:20:53.640 --> 00:20:59.820
They’re less living entities and more conceptual
constructs - pure ideas - that just happen

00:20:59.820 --> 00:21:04.200
to be self-aware of their own existence in
their private, hellish voids.

00:21:04.200 --> 00:21:10.560
The SCP-000 file - a file for an anomaly that
doesn’t exist, and thus, had no reason to

00:21:10.560 --> 00:21:13.800
exist - is a perfect breeding ground for a
Pattern Screamer.

00:21:13.800 --> 00:21:19.320
But sadly, for the Pattern Screamer in question,
Technical Director Rosen had no idea.

00:21:19.320 --> 00:21:23.880
This isn’t the only time that Rosen has
run into a Pattern Screamer without even knowing,

00:21:23.880 --> 00:21:24.240
either.

00:21:24.240 --> 00:21:28.260
And just like the first case, he was no help
whatsoever.

00:21:28.260 --> 00:21:34.680
This one began with SCP-S, an otherwise empty
file containing only this image.

00:21:34.680 --> 00:21:39.720
Director Winters, a Foundation administrator,
wondered why this file even existed.

00:21:39.720 --> 00:21:44.940
Enter Technical Researcher Rosen, filled with
equal parts sarcasm and insubordination.

00:21:44.940 --> 00:21:49.440
He gave a condescending reply to Director
Winters, saying that the file was there to

00:21:49.440 --> 00:21:52.980
test the filing system, and the image was
likely just a placeholder.

00:21:52.980 --> 00:21:56.820
Winters never should have been on the page
anyway, according to Rosen.

00:21:56.820 --> 00:22:01.380
Director Winters was annoyed at Rosen’s
typically rude tone, and asked him to make

00:22:01.380 --> 00:22:03.900
the purpose of the article clearer in the
article itself.

00:22:03.900 --> 00:22:09.180
In response, Rosen did as he was told, filling
in the article in the most sarcastic manner

00:22:09.180 --> 00:22:09.660
possible.

00:22:09.660 --> 00:22:14.400
The whole thing was essentially a middle finger
to Director Winters for having the audacity

00:22:14.400 --> 00:22:15.240
to even ask.

00:22:15.240 --> 00:22:18.540
Rosen signed off with:
“There, finished.

00:22:18.540 --> 00:22:23.700
I certainly hope I have been clear enough
to anyone who may have accidentally accessed

00:22:23.700 --> 00:22:26.640
this page through what I am sure is no fault&nbsp;

00:22:26.640 --> 00:22:30.000
of their own, so we won't&nbsp;
have any more ‘incredibly

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:33.720
competent’ directors bugging the tech team
about this page.”

00:22:33.720 --> 00:22:39.780
And once again, Technical Researcher Rosen
was too busy being a rude, unpleasant jerk

00:22:39.780 --> 00:22:43.560
to notice he was practically staring another
Pattern Screamer in the face.

00:22:43.560 --> 00:22:49.620
This Pattern Screamer - or rather, hive of
Pattern Screamers - were trapped even deeper

00:22:49.620 --> 00:22:52.200
than the one in SCP-000.

00:22:52.200 --> 00:22:58.320
This one was hidden in the very source code
of SCP-S, where a chorus of enraged voices

00:22:58.320 --> 00:22:59.580
screamed the following:

00:22:59.580 --> 00:23:02.940
“PRETEND, MONSTER, JUST FOR A MINUTE

00:23:02.940 --> 00:23:08.340
PRETEND YOU WERE THE SIZE OF AN AMOEBA, DWARFED
BY EVEN THE SMALLEST OF BUGS

00:23:08.340 --> 00:23:11.340
PRETEND YOU DIDN'T HOLD THE WORLD IN A GLASS
CAGE.

00:23:11.340 --> 00:23:15.360
PRETEND YOU WERE THE ONE BEING HELD BY SOMETHING
GREATER THAN YOURSELF.

00:23:15.360 --> 00:23:18.360
WOULD YOU STILL BE LAUGHING AT YOUR "TRIUMPHS"?

00:23:18.360 --> 00:23:23.640
WOULD YOU STILL FEEL PRIDE IN WHAT YOU WERE,
EVEN AS PITIFULLY SMALL AS YOU WOULD BE?

00:23:23.640 --> 00:23:27.720
OF COURSE YOU WOULD, BECAUSE YOU ARE ARROGANT
AND STUPID

00:23:27.720 --> 00:23:31.500
IF YOU HAVEN'T GUESSED YET, WE HATE YOU.”

00:23:31.500 --> 00:23:36.480
This Pattern Screamer is clearly more aware
of its pitiful station in existence than the

00:23:36.480 --> 00:23:43.500
000 Pattern Screamer, and as a result, it’s
not so much depressed as it is furious.

00:23:43.500 --> 00:23:47.880
Though at this point you’ve probably figured
out that even the entities who have the most

00:23:47.880 --> 00:23:52.200
casual of brushes with Technical Researcher
Rosen end up getting infuriated.

00:23:52.200 --> 00:23:56.160
But while you may have gotten the impression
that all Pattern Screamers are sad little

00:23:56.160 --> 00:24:01.560
entities worthy of our sympathy and pity,
there’s at least one Pattern Screamer that’s

00:24:01.560 --> 00:24:03.720
actually incredibly dangerous.

00:24:03.720 --> 00:24:11.460
This is SCP-3930: The ultimate Pattern Screamer,
in terms of both size and effect.

00:24:11.460 --> 00:24:17.040
It’s an anomaly so strange it defies typical
containment classification, and it bears a

00:24:17.040 --> 00:24:22.200
Level 5 Security Lock - meaning only those
on the level of the legendary O5 Council are

00:24:22.200 --> 00:24:23.760
cleared to even know about it.

00:24:23.760 --> 00:24:29.580
Its greatest containment procedure is the
preservation of the very idea that SCP-3930

00:24:29.580 --> 00:24:35.520
does not exist, because the alternative has
terrifying implications for all involved.

00:24:35.520 --> 00:24:40.980
SCP-3930 is a 1 km area in Russia that is
filled with non-existence.

00:24:40.980 --> 00:24:46.560
To even call it a white void would be inaccurate,
because it implies the existence of the color

00:24:46.560 --> 00:24:49.560
white and the existence of the concept of
a void.

00:24:49.560 --> 00:24:56.340
Nothing exists within SCP-3930, and anyone
who directly observes 3930 runs the risk of

00:24:56.340 --> 00:24:58.140
actively increasing its power.

00:24:58.140 --> 00:25:03.360
That’s why Special Containment Procedures
dictate that anyone who observes 3930 must

00:25:03.360 --> 00:25:07.980
be forced to walk into it afterwards, which
results in them ceasing to exist.

00:25:07.980 --> 00:25:12.300
They’re destroyed on the deepest level that
anything can be destroyed.

00:25:12.300 --> 00:25:15.780
The very idea of them ceases to be.

00:25:15.780 --> 00:25:21.840
Another reason that SCP-3930 is so special
is that, because it’s the largest area of

00:25:21.840 --> 00:25:26.460
nothing in existence interacting directly
with our reality, it’s the only place that

00:25:26.460 --> 00:25:30.540
a huge number of Pattern Screamers can be
directly observed by humans.

00:25:30.540 --> 00:25:33.360
They’re described as being like sentient
hallucinations.

00:25:33.360 --> 00:25:38.460
One researcher suggests that these Pattern
Screamers are created by the way the psyche

00:25:38.460 --> 00:25:42.180
shatters when brought into contact with raw,
true nothingness.

00:25:42.180 --> 00:25:47.400
The nothingness acts like a “hateful mirror”
to our worst thoughts, reflecting them back

00:25:47.400 --> 00:25:49.800
at us in the forms of restless Screamers.

00:25:49.800 --> 00:25:55.680
Regardless of what they actually are, one
thing is for sure, coming into direct contact

00:25:55.680 --> 00:25:59.160
with one of these Screamers is a harrowing
experience.

00:25:59.160 --> 00:26:04.500
In the end, it just goes to show that Pattern
Screamers are a complex entity - they can

00:26:04.500 --> 00:26:09.420
range from microscopic to massive, from pitiful
to downright terrifying.

00:26:09.420 --> 00:26:14.880
And the sad reality is that, in either case,
nothing can really be done to stop them.

00:26:14.880 --> 00:26:21.300
It’s just as impossible to stop the nothingness
existing in SCP-3930 as it is to save the

00:26:21.300 --> 00:26:25.080
entity trapped in the white spaces of SCP-000.

00:26:25.080 --> 00:26:30.000
Maybe the best option is to actually be more
like Technical Director Rosen.

00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:36.000
Keep your head down, focus instead on your
own petty worries, and bask in the warm bliss

00:26:36.000 --> 00:26:39.360
that can only come with having no idea what
you’re dealing with.

00:26:39.360 --> 00:26:44.100
The one downside is that this may make you
a pretty lousy IT guy.

00:26:44.100 --> 00:26:48.420
There are some things human beings aren’t
meant to know, and it’s the sworn duty of

00:26:48.420 --> 00:26:51.600
The SCP Foundation to discover and contain
such information.

00:26:51.600 --> 00:26:56.940
But sometimes, knowledge is discovered that
shakes even the Foundation itself to its very

00:26:56.940 --> 00:26:57.300
core.

00:26:57.300 --> 00:27:03.660
One such discovery occurred on April 28th,
2016 – the night that SCP – 2935 made

00:27:03.660 --> 00:27:05.520
itself known to Foundation personnel.

00:27:05.520 --> 00:27:11.040
To this day, the exact nature of SCP – 2935
is a mystery that even the Foundation’s

00:27:11.040 --> 00:27:12.900
brightest minds can’t completely understand.

00:27:12.900 --> 00:27:19.440
Everything we know about SCP – 2935 today
comes from three doomed missions into the

00:27:19.440 --> 00:27:20.820
anomalous zone’s interior.

00:27:20.820 --> 00:27:23.880
This is the story of those infamous expeditions.

00:27:23.880 --> 00:27:29.340
The nightmare began around 5:00 AM, when SCP
Foundation Site 81 in Bloomingdale, Indiana,

00:27:29.340 --> 00:27:32.100
intercepted a distorted radio signal.

00:27:32.100 --> 00:27:36.480
Communications personnel at the site traced
this strange signal back to the unincorporated

00:27:36.480 --> 00:27:39.900
area of Joppa, Indiana, near US Interstate
70.

00:27:39.900 --> 00:27:45.360
As is Foundation policy, a team of Field Agents
were dispatched to the location in order to

00:27:45.360 --> 00:27:46.800
determine what they were dealing with.

00:27:46.800 --> 00:27:51.780
However, rather than finding anything that
could logically produce such a signal, they

00:27:51.780 --> 00:27:54.060
instead discovered a long abandoned cemetery.

00:27:54.060 --> 00:27:59.100
The most recent death on any of the tombstones
was recorded as being over a hundred years

00:27:59.100 --> 00:28:01.560
ago, all the way back in 1908.

00:28:01.560 --> 00:28:04.320
On further investigation,&nbsp;
the Foundation discovered&nbsp;

00:28:04.320 --> 00:28:06.840
an unmapped limestone cave opening beneath

00:28:06.840 --> 00:28:10.920
the cemetery and when they sent a drone into
the depths of the cave, it appeared to quickly

00:28:10.920 --> 00:28:12.420
exit out the other side of the cave.

00:28:12.420 --> 00:28:13.920
But something wasn’t right.

00:28:13.920 --> 00:28:17.880
The area that the drone was observing appeared
consistent with the landscape from which it’d

00:28:17.880 --> 00:28:19.920
entered, but now it looked somehow…greyer.

00:28:20.580 --> 00:28:23.460
It lacked the color and life of the place
it’d just come from.

00:28:23.460 --> 00:28:24.660
The grass was dead.

00:28:24.660 --> 00:28:28.380
There were no trees, no shrubs, no animals
or birds in the sky.

00:28:28.380 --> 00:28:30.120
They weren’t looking at our world.

00:28:30.120 --> 00:28:33.840
They were looking at a strange reflection
of our world on the other side of the cave.

00:28:33.840 --> 00:28:37.860
In fact, it wasn’t a cave at all – it
was a passageway between two dimensions.

00:28:37.860 --> 00:28:40.320
It was SCP – 2935.

00:28:40.320 --> 00:28:44.580
Just then they were able to unscramble the
distorted transmission they’d been receiving.

00:28:44.580 --> 00:28:47.940
It went as follows:
“This is an automated emergency broadcast

00:28:47.940 --> 00:28:50.760
from the SCP Foundation and your national
government.

00:28:50.760 --> 00:28:53.400
One or more of our sites is experiencing a&nbsp;

00:28:53.400 --> 00:28:56.040
communication breakdown,&nbsp;
likely due to a containment

00:28:56.040 --> 00:28:57.420
breach of unknown magnitude.

00:28:57.420 --> 00:29:01.620
All citizens are ordered to stay in their
homes as containment teams work to secure

00:29:01.620 --> 00:29:02.040
the breach.

00:29:02.040 --> 00:29:05.700
This message will broadcast from April 20th,
2016 until—”

00:29:05.700 --> 00:29:10.680
At that point, the message would cut and repeat,
as it had been for eight straight days.

00:29:10.680 --> 00:29:12.000
The message’s source?

00:29:12.000 --> 00:29:12.960
Site 81.

00:29:12.960 --> 00:29:14.880
But not this Site 81.

00:29:14.880 --> 00:29:19.500
The SCP Foundation was receiving an emergency
distress signal from themselves in another

00:29:19.500 --> 00:29:23.640
dimension – a bizarre event that even the
Foundation had never experienced before.

00:29:23.640 --> 00:29:26.400
The Field Agents were&nbsp;
terrified by the implications&nbsp;

00:29:26.400 --> 00:29:28.320
of what they’d just heard and contacted

00:29:28.320 --> 00:29:30.840
Site 81 Command to request additional units.

00:29:30.840 --> 00:29:34.980
The Foundation wished to fully understand
this anomaly as quickly as possible, due to

00:29:34.980 --> 00:29:38.520
the potential threat it could pose towards
the Foundation, so they dispatched Mobile

00:29:38.520 --> 00:29:43.920
Task Force Epsilon-13, codenamed “Manifest
Destiny”, to perform the first of three

00:29:43.920 --> 00:29:46.260
manned missions into the heart of the anomalous
zone.

00:29:46.260 --> 00:29:51.960
The first exploratory mission into SCP – 2935
was codenamed “Gauntlet”, and consisted

00:29:51.960 --> 00:29:56.340
of a four-man team fitted with full hazmat
suits and direct video and audio links to

00:29:56.340 --> 00:29:57.060
mission command.

00:29:57.060 --> 00:30:01.080
The team was led by a Field Operative known
only as Agent Juno.

00:30:01.080 --> 00:30:04.260
His subordinates were Agents Kael, Devon,
and Underwood.

00:30:04.260 --> 00:30:08.460
Their directive was to gather samples and
survey the area positioned directly around

00:30:08.460 --> 00:30:12.780
the insertion point, meaning the other cave
mouth of SCP – 2935.

00:30:12.780 --> 00:30:16.980
The mission only lasted about an hour, but
what they saw in there would stay with these

00:30:16.980 --> 00:30:18.360
men for the rest of their lives.

00:30:18.360 --> 00:30:22.980
After a fifteen-minute trek through the cave,
Manifest Destiny arrived in the mirror dimension

00:30:22.980 --> 00:30:27.600
where they were struck by the eerie silence
of a place that seemed identical and yet so

00:30:27.600 --> 00:30:29.040
different from their home dimension.

00:30:29.040 --> 00:30:32.940
The first observation they made was the total
absence of all living vegetation.

00:30:32.940 --> 00:30:36.600
Trees, grass, weeds, everything – it was
all dead.

00:30:36.600 --> 00:30:40.680
On orders from their superiors back in the
original dimension – that we’ll refer

00:30:40.680 --> 00:30:45.300
to from here on as Dimension Prime – Manifest
Destiny headed deeper into the mirror dimension

00:30:45.300 --> 00:30:46.800
of SCP – 2935.

00:30:46.800 --> 00:30:51.120
They travelled two kilometers without detecting
a single sign of plant or animal life.

00:30:51.120 --> 00:30:52.500
Not even insects.

00:30:52.500 --> 00:30:55.800
Eventually, they came upon a farm house with
two cars parked outside.

00:30:55.800 --> 00:31:00.420
With authorization from Command, Manifest
Destiny breached the house and headed inside.

00:31:00.420 --> 00:31:04.620
Agent Kael confirmed that there was still
power flowing to the building, as the lighting

00:31:04.620 --> 00:31:08.640
appeared to work just fine, but they came
upon a horrifying discovery in the house’s

00:31:08.640 --> 00:31:13.140
dining room: Three adult corpses, two female
and one male, were seated at the table.

00:31:13.140 --> 00:31:17.100
A fourth corpse, that of a male child, was
sprawled out on the ground nearby.

00:31:17.640 --> 00:31:21.900
If the death of what looked to be an entire
family wasn’t awful enough, the Manifest

00:31:21.900 --> 00:31:24.600
Destiny team noticed a number of other alarming
details.

00:31:24.600 --> 00:31:28.680
There were no signs of decomposition on the
bodies, nor did there appear to be any obvious

00:31:28.680 --> 00:31:29.340
cause of death.

00:31:29.340 --> 00:31:33.300
The family’s last meal was still on the
table – Chicken, mashed potatoes, and green

00:31:33.300 --> 00:31:33.600
beans.

00:31:33.600 --> 00:31:37.440
While the food looked cold and stale, there
was no evidence of rot or spoiling.

00:31:37.440 --> 00:31:42.420
The team found an opened newspaper dated April
19th, 2016, illustrating that the family may

00:31:42.420 --> 00:31:44.700
have died a full eight days before the discovery.

00:31:44.700 --> 00:31:49.740
In Dimension Prime, decay would already be
well underway by that point, yet here, there

00:31:49.740 --> 00:31:50.640
wasn’t even a smell.

00:31:50.640 --> 00:31:53.940
Instead, everything was just covered in a
thin layer of dust.

00:31:53.940 --> 00:31:58.800
Command requested that Manifest Destiny collect
samples of the food as well as hair, skin,

00:31:58.800 --> 00:32:01.320
and fluids from the corpses for further study.

00:32:01.320 --> 00:32:04.680
Small electronics like smart phones were also
taken from the bodies.

00:32:04.680 --> 00:32:08.940
Agent Devon turned on the television in the
living room, and found that, while most stations

00:32:08.940 --> 00:32:11.820
were now running test signals, the shopping
channel was still live.

00:32:11.820 --> 00:32:13.680
Well the feed was live at least.

00:32:13.680 --> 00:32:17.340
Both hosts sat in front of the cameras, dead,
but perfectly preserved.

00:32:17.340 --> 00:32:22.800
The date on the screen read April 28th, 2016,
suggesting that the times of Dimension Prime

00:32:22.800 --> 00:32:24.840
and the Mirror Dimension were exactly the
same.

00:32:24.840 --> 00:32:29.040
In fact everything seemed the same, the only
difference between the two dimensions being

00:32:29.040 --> 00:32:34.763
that some kind of mysterious apocalyptic event
had occurred in the last eight days in SCP

00:32:34.762 --> 00:32:39.480
– 2935’s Mirror Dimension, but exactly
what had happened, or how, remained a mystery.

00:32:39.480 --> 00:32:43.800
When Manifest Destiny exited the farm house,
they once again remarked on the lack of all

00:32:43.800 --> 00:32:45.000
signs of life around them.

00:32:45.000 --> 00:32:50.100
At this point, the team returned to the insertion
point of SCP – 2935, but were instructed

00:32:50.100 --> 00:32:53.640
to remain in the Mirror Dimension while additional
units joined them inside.

00:32:53.640 --> 00:32:58.740
Manifest Destiny swelled to sixteen members,
with the notable addition of Agent Roy as

00:32:58.740 --> 00:33:00.000
the new commanding field officer.

00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:04.500
The team split into two groups of eight, and
Agent Roy and his men infiltrated the Mirror

00:33:04.500 --> 00:33:08.820
Dimension’s Site 81 while Agent Juno’s
detachment attempted to access the base’s

00:33:08.820 --> 00:33:10.380
off-site deep storage servers.

00:33:10.380 --> 00:33:15.300
This second expedition was codenamed “Overland”,
and led the Foundation’s Field Agents even

00:33:15.300 --> 00:33:18.660
deeper into the terrifying mystery of SCP
– 2935.

00:33:18.660 --> 00:33:21.660
Accessing the site was easy for Roy’s detachment.

00:33:21.660 --> 00:33:25.740
It seemed there were relatively few cars on
the road at the time of the mysterious Extinction

00:33:25.740 --> 00:33:25.980
Event.

00:33:25.980 --> 00:33:30.000
In the distance, fires still smoldered in
the wreckage of planes that looked to have

00:33:30.000 --> 00:33:31.260
just dropped out of the sky.

00:33:31.260 --> 00:33:36.540
Agent Roy and his team, like all SCP Foundation
personnel, were fitted with vitals trackers,

00:33:36.540 --> 00:33:40.320
and they assumed that the distress signal
that started this whole thing could have been

00:33:40.320 --> 00:33:44.760
triggered by the deaths of every member of
the Foundation at once in the Mirror Universe.

00:33:44.760 --> 00:33:48.900
Once inside Site 81, they realized that assumption
was probably right.

00:33:48.900 --> 00:33:53.100
Going door to door in the administrative wing,
they found the perfectly preserved corpses

00:33:53.100 --> 00:33:56.160
of everyone they knew to be stationed there
in Dimension Prime.

00:33:56.160 --> 00:33:59.400
People without a doubt were still alive in
their universe.

00:33:59.400 --> 00:34:03.480
Samples from the corpses that the Foundation
would later study even confirmed the reason

00:34:03.480 --> 00:34:07.860
that the bodies were perfectly preserved:
The corpses had experienced complete and sudden

00:34:07.860 --> 00:34:10.440
death on a cellular level, and even the bacteria&nbsp;

00:34:10.440 --> 00:34:12.360
that would typically take&nbsp;
part in the decomposition

00:34:12.360 --> 00:34:14.040
process had died with it.

00:34:14.040 --> 00:34:19.860
In SCP – 2935, death was total and absolute
across all types of life forms.

00:34:19.860 --> 00:34:22.260
As Agent Roy’s team ventured further into&nbsp;

00:34:22.260 --> 00:34:24.960
the bowels of Site 81, they&nbsp;
made another unsettling

00:34:24.960 --> 00:34:29.760
discovery - their own corpses, in roughly
the spots they had been inside Dimension Prime’s

00:34:29.760 --> 00:34:31.380
Site 81 eight days prior.

00:34:31.380 --> 00:34:35.940
Some of the Foundation’s top scientists,
including the esteemed Dr. Bright, were also

00:34:35.940 --> 00:34:37.620
found dead inside the facility.

00:34:37.620 --> 00:34:42.780
In an attempt to see just how far this unexplained
phenomenon stretched, Agent Roy’s team decided

00:34:42.780 --> 00:34:47.400
to inspect the containment cells – where
they found that all the Mirror Universe SCPs,

00:34:47.400 --> 00:34:50.460
including SCP – 2996, were dead.

00:34:50.460 --> 00:34:55.740
In his desperation to find some kind of exception
to the Extinction Event, Agent Roy revealed

00:34:55.740 --> 00:35:01.380
a terrifying secret to the rest of his team:
SCP – 682, the immortal, misanthropic lizard,

00:35:01.380 --> 00:35:05.760
and one of the deadliest creatures known to
the SCP Foundation, was contained at this

00:35:05.760 --> 00:35:07.440
very facility, right below them.

00:35:07.440 --> 00:35:09.780
Could it have something to do with what was
going on here?

00:35:09.780 --> 00:35:14.160
They descended into its containment facility
to discover an even more unsettling truth.

00:35:14.160 --> 00:35:20.760
SCP – 682, the unkillable anomaly, floated
dead in its tank Death truly made no exceptions

00:35:20.760 --> 00:35:22.740
within SCP – 2935.

00:35:22.740 --> 00:35:27.270
Agent Roy’s team left the site and rendezvoused
with Agent Juno’s team to send their research

00:35:27.270 --> 00:35:29.880
and back to Dimension Prime using automated
drones.

00:35:29.880 --> 00:35:31.980
Both teams remained in the Mirror Dimension&nbsp;

00:35:31.980 --> 00:35:34.560
for another manned operation,&nbsp;
codenamed “Nineteen,”

00:35:34.560 --> 00:35:36.780
they had no idea it would be their final mission.

00:35:36.780 --> 00:35:42.300
As they descended deeper into the facility,
passing more dead SCPs they discovered one

00:35:42.300 --> 00:35:42.960
final clue.

00:35:42.960 --> 00:35:47.700
Based on the last activity of the Foundation
servers, the event occurred at roughly 3:00

00:35:47.700 --> 00:35:48.120
AM.

00:35:48.120 --> 00:35:53.820
While underground in SCP – 2935’s Site
81, the team accidentally activated the base’s

00:35:53.820 --> 00:35:58.020
on-site nuclear weapon – a failsafe meant
to be detonated in the case of an emergency

00:35:58.020 --> 00:35:59.220
containment breach.

00:35:59.220 --> 00:36:04.080
Due to the base’s failsafe protocols, every
member of the Manifest Destiny team was locked

00:36:04.080 --> 00:36:05.880
and sealed inside Site 81.

00:36:05.880 --> 00:36:09.720
They, along with everything else, were incinerated
in the nuclear blast.

00:36:09.720 --> 00:36:14.280
Once again, the Mirror Universe inside of
SCP – 2935 was lifeless.

00:36:14.280 --> 00:36:16.200
But that isn’t where this ends.

00:36:16.200 --> 00:36:21.300
When the automated drones returned out of
the SCP – 2935 cave to the Field Operatives

00:36:21.300 --> 00:36:24.780
in Dimension Prime, they were in for their
own horrifying discovery.

00:36:24.780 --> 00:36:30.720
None of the footage or information gathered
from SCP – 2935 illuminated how or why the

00:36:30.720 --> 00:36:31.920
Extinction Event occurred.

00:36:31.920 --> 00:36:35.460
Everyone and everything simply dropped dead
at the exact same moment.

00:36:35.460 --> 00:36:38.160
Nobody was aware, nobody was prepared.

00:36:38.160 --> 00:36:41.340
Death came suddenly and silently, and none
were spared.

00:36:41.340 --> 00:36:45.360
All the Foundation on Dimension Prime were
left with was a message from one of the agents

00:36:45.360 --> 00:36:47.340
from Manifest Destiny, Agent Keller.

00:36:47.340 --> 00:36:49.680
His final message was: “I don't have any
answers.

00:36:49.680 --> 00:36:51.000
I don't think there are any.

00:36:51.000 --> 00:36:53.340
I'll do this one thing, and hope that fixes
it.

00:36:53.340 --> 00:36:54.240
Seal it shut.

00:36:54.240 --> 00:36:55.860
You've got to lock it in here with us.

00:36:55.860 --> 00:36:56.640
I'm sorry.”

00:36:56.640 --> 00:37:01.320
The Foundation were at first confused by this,
until they discovered a final encrypted audio

00:37:01.320 --> 00:37:05.100
log buried in the files recovered from the
Mirror Universe’s Site 81.

00:37:05.100 --> 00:37:08.820
It was a message from Keller himself, but
not the Keller from Universe Prime.

00:37:08.820 --> 00:37:13.380
In this message, Keller described the Foundation
in the Mirror Universe receiving the exact

00:37:13.380 --> 00:37:17.940
same distorted transmission that they did
a few days earlier from a cave in Joppa.

00:37:17.940 --> 00:37:22.620
When he and the others were dispatched inside,
they discovered the same lifeless, post-Extinction

00:37:22.620 --> 00:37:25.860
Event world that was now so familiar to Foundation
Command.

00:37:25.860 --> 00:37:30.000
But there was a key difference: This wasn’t
the Mirror Dimension they’d just been studying,

00:37:30.000 --> 00:37:32.460
but a third, entirely different dimension.

00:37:32.460 --> 00:37:36.780
In his haunting final words, Mirror Dimension
Keller admits that whatever caused the event

00:37:36.780 --> 00:37:42.120
in that third dimension – an entity that
Mirror Dimension Keller believed was the spectre

00:37:42.120 --> 00:37:46.920
of Death itself – had followed him back
into his world, and history had repeated itself.

00:37:46.920 --> 00:37:52.860
SCP – 2935 was the passageway through which
absolute death could pass from dimension to

00:37:52.860 --> 00:37:55.440
dimension, and our dimension was the next
in line.

00:37:55.440 --> 00:38:00.480
The deaths of Manifest Destiny may have saved
our entire universe, as anyone passing back

00:38:00.480 --> 00:38:03.900
through the cave had the potential to bring
Death itself back with them.

00:38:03.900 --> 00:38:06.960
The Foundation decided, in the end, to follow
Keller’s advice.

00:38:06.960 --> 00:38:12.240
They sealed the entrance to SCP – 2935 with
concrete, and now keep it under constant watch,

00:38:12.240 --> 00:38:16.920
since what waits behind the barrier is an
entity even they have no power to stop if

00:38:16.920 --> 00:38:17.640
it ever got through.

00:38:17.640 --> 00:38:22.020
After all, it had killed them all before,
or at least another version of them.

00:38:22.020 --> 00:38:24.060
What’s one more dimension on the pile?

00:38:24.060 --> 00:38:29.220
While it may now just seem like a simple slab
of concrete under an abandoned cemetery, this

00:38:29.220 --> 00:38:34.080
is why SCP – 2935 might just be the most
dangerous SCP of all.

00:38:34.080 --> 00:38:39.720
A veteran worker of the SCP Foundation sits
at his terminal, performing one of the most

00:38:39.720 --> 00:38:45.300
critical tasks in the entire organization
- creating a file for an as yet undescribed

00:38:45.300 --> 00:38:46.080
SCP.

00:38:46.080 --> 00:38:48.180
But there’s something terribly wrong.

00:38:48.180 --> 00:38:54.960
His eyes are glazed over, his mouth hangs
open - is this a zombie or a trained foundation

00:38:54.960 --> 00:38:55.680
researcher?

00:38:56.280 --> 00:38:57.480
What is going on?

00:38:57.480 --> 00:39:02.700
Like any large international organization,
it takes more than just the exciting, action

00:39:02.700 --> 00:39:06.180
filled jobs to keep the wheels turning at
the SCP Foundation.

00:39:06.180 --> 00:39:11.400
Sure, the head researchers, guards, mobile
task force soldiers, and members of the O5

00:39:11.400 --> 00:39:16.860
Command get all the praise, but a legion of
number crunchers, cleaners, and paper pushers

00:39:16.860 --> 00:39:18.300
are equally important.

00:39:18.300 --> 00:39:23.940
One such person was archivist Walter Bainbridge,
who had been tasked with digitizing some of

00:39:23.940 --> 00:39:26.640
the older records that the Foundation had
on file.

00:39:26.640 --> 00:39:34.500
It was when he was innocently recording the
details on SCP - 050 through 060 that he first

00:39:34.500 --> 00:39:39.240
came under the strange and startling effects
of SCP - 055.

00:39:39.240 --> 00:39:43.200
But, the most peculiar&nbsp;
part, as with all incidences&nbsp;

00:39:43.200 --> 00:39:46.260
of SCP - 055’s anomalous effects taking

00:39:46.260 --> 00:39:50.700
hold, is that Walter had no idea any of it
was happening.

00:39:50.700 --> 00:39:56.280
In his new digitized filing system, he first
took note of SCP - 053.

00:39:56.280 --> 00:40:01.980
Euclid Class, also known as the Young Girl,
this anomaly was a seemingly normal human

00:40:01.980 --> 00:40:07.020
female child who provoked homicidal insanity
in those directly exposed to her.

00:40:07.020 --> 00:40:09.240
Then SCP - 054.

00:40:09.240 --> 00:40:15.780
Safe Class, a non-aggressive humanoid female
made entirely of, as well as biologically

00:40:15.780 --> 00:40:18.900
and chemically identical to regular spring
water.

00:40:18.900 --> 00:40:21.660
Next, SCP - 056.

00:40:21.660 --> 00:40:27.660
Euclid Class, a being that changes form to
suit its environment, but only when all observers

00:40:27.660 --> 00:40:28.860
lose focus on it.

00:40:28.860 --> 00:40:31.980
And then SCP - 057.

00:40:31.980 --> 00:40:37.380
Safe Class, an underground chamber that crushes
the humans who walk within.

00:40:37.380 --> 00:40:41.520
It was at this point that Walter received
a concerned message from one of his superiors

00:40:41.520 --> 00:40:43.680
at Site-19, Mr. Kovach.

00:40:43.680 --> 00:40:48.360
The message praised the thorough digitization
of the other anomalies’ records, but was

00:40:48.360 --> 00:40:52.740
confused about why Walter had left out any
mention of SCP - 055.

00:40:52.740 --> 00:40:55.080
Immediately, Walter was embarrassed.

00:40:55.080 --> 00:40:58.200
How could he have forgotten SCP - 055?

00:40:58.200 --> 00:41:04.920
That iconic anomaly known for...Well, he couldn’t
quite say, off the top of his head, but he’d

00:41:04.920 --> 00:41:06.120
be sure to look into it.

00:41:06.120 --> 00:41:10.800
A quick trip to the Site 19 Archives showed
him that there was actually quite a hefty

00:41:10.800 --> 00:41:17.040
file on the nature of SCP - 055, which must
have been the result of a huge number of studies.

00:41:17.040 --> 00:41:22.080
What struck him as strange was that all the
files were filled out in pen rather than being

00:41:22.080 --> 00:41:24.000
typed up, like a traditional file.

00:41:24.000 --> 00:41:28.800
The majority of these notes were written in
short-hand, too, as though they were frantically

00:41:28.800 --> 00:41:32.160
taken during the tests themselves on extremely
short notice.

00:41:32.700 --> 00:41:34.980
There weren’t even any redactions.

00:41:34.980 --> 00:41:39.900
Walter made a mental note of what he had seen,
put the file back in its proper place, and

00:41:39.900 --> 00:41:41.400
headed back to his computer terminal.

00:41:41.400 --> 00:41:46.560
However, after writing in an almost trancelike
state, he looked back on his work to see that

00:41:46.560 --> 00:41:54.060
he had written an entry on SCP - 058, a giant,
evil bovine heart with insect legs and a scorpion

00:41:54.060 --> 00:41:54.600
stinger…

00:41:54.600 --> 00:41:56.700
Strange, he thought.

00:41:56.700 --> 00:42:01.740
That’s when Walter got a call from Mr. Kovach
on his Foundation-issue phone, and he didn’t

00:42:01.740 --> 00:42:02.460
sound happy.

00:42:02.460 --> 00:42:08.820
He’d given Walter direct instructions to
go back and digitize the files on 055, and

00:42:08.820 --> 00:42:10.980
instead, he’d been working on 058.

00:42:10.980 --> 00:42:12.420
What was the meaning of this?

00:42:12.420 --> 00:42:17.580
Walter was typically an extremely loyal and
diligent employee, but the verbal barrage

00:42:17.580 --> 00:42:22.860
from his supervisor had him considering talking
back, just this once, and hoping it didn’t

00:42:22.860 --> 00:42:27.420
get him demoted to D-Class and thrown into
682’s acid bath for play time.

00:42:27.420 --> 00:42:32.640
Walter gulped, picked up some courage, and
interrupted Mr. Kovach’s rant to ask if

00:42:32.640 --> 00:42:36.780
he had any idea what SCP - 055 actually was.

00:42:36.780 --> 00:42:43.020
The line went silent for a moment, then the
supervisor spoke again, this time with less

00:42:43.020 --> 00:42:43.500
confidence.

00:42:43.500 --> 00:42:47.580
“Of course I can tell you about SCP - 055.

00:42:47.580 --> 00:42:50.820
It’s a classic, one of the first hundred.

00:42:50.820 --> 00:42:58.320
How could you forget its...Or, um, you know,
its...I think it’s the one with the...”

00:42:59.340 --> 00:43:05.220
Another long pause, as Mr. Kovach seemed to
search for the words, but instead just trailed

00:43:05.220 --> 00:43:06.180
off into silence.

00:43:06.180 --> 00:43:11.040
Knowing that some of the anomalies on file
were dangerous memetic hazards, Walter was

00:43:11.040 --> 00:43:15.540
worried for a moment that he may have accidentally
killed his boss by getting him to think too

00:43:15.540 --> 00:43:17.760
hard about SCP - 055.

00:43:17.760 --> 00:43:22.200
He asked if Mr. Kovach was okay, and finally
got a reply.

00:43:22.800 --> 00:43:25.380
“I’m sorry, I seem to have zoned out for
a second there.

00:43:25.380 --> 00:43:26.880
What were we talking about, again?”

00:43:27.420 --> 00:43:30.060
But this time, it was Walter who couldn't
answer.

00:43:30.060 --> 00:43:34.740
He had no idea at all what the two of them
were discussing just moments ago.

00:43:34.740 --> 00:43:40.020
He felt disoriented and kind of sick, like
they’d taken some low-level amnestics.

00:43:40.020 --> 00:43:44.400
Mr. Kovach told Walter to get back to his
filing duties and they’d speak later.

00:43:44.400 --> 00:43:49.260
Walter then checked the messages he’d received
from Mr. Kovach earlier, and there it was,

00:43:49.260 --> 00:43:52.140
plain as day: “You missed 055.

00:43:52.140 --> 00:43:54.810
Go back and digitize that before proceeding.

00:43:54.810 --> 00:43:56.040
- Mr. K.”

00:43:56.040 --> 00:44:01.980
But Walter had never even heard of an SCP
- 055, if such an anomaly even existed!

00:44:02.580 --> 00:44:04.020
What was going on here?

00:44:04.020 --> 00:44:09.420
In that moment, Walter realized he was dealing
with something much stranger than just a standard

00:44:09.420 --> 00:44:10.560
digitization job.

00:44:10.560 --> 00:44:16.860
After all, how could he properly complete
his duties if SCP - 055 seemed to be impossible

00:44:16.860 --> 00:44:22.560
to speak, write, or even think about, unless
you were directly observing it at that moment?

00:44:22.560 --> 00:44:29.160
Walter had to know, and ask around the entirety
of Site 19 to find the answers if he had to.

00:44:29.820 --> 00:44:35.100
Sadly for Walter, he was about to embark on
a much more challenging task than he could

00:44:35.100 --> 00:44:36.120
have ever imagined.

00:44:36.120 --> 00:44:41.280
To paraphrase a supposed quote from Socrates,
“All I know is that I know nothing.”

00:44:41.280 --> 00:44:47.460
And that’s also about the extent of the
knowledge we have on SCP - 055, also known

00:44:47.460 --> 00:44:50.100
as The Anti-Meme and the Self-Keeping Secret.

00:44:50.100 --> 00:44:51.480
What does it look like?

00:44:51.480 --> 00:44:54.480
When and how was it obtained by the Foundation?

00:44:54.480 --> 00:44:56.400
What are its anomalous abilities?

00:44:56.400 --> 00:44:58.320
Is this thing dangerous?

00:44:58.320 --> 00:45:04.740
We may never know, because the only anomalous
ability of SCP - 055 that we’re aware of

00:45:04.740 --> 00:45:08.940
is the fact that nobody is capable of retaining
any information about it.

00:45:08.940 --> 00:45:15.720
It’s crucial to note that, whatever 055
is, it isn’t invisible, or indescribable.

00:45:15.720 --> 00:45:21.120
Foundation personnel are perfectly capable
of entering its containment chamber and observing

00:45:21.120 --> 00:45:23.400
it without incident, but mere minutes after&nbsp;

00:45:23.400 --> 00:45:26.460
leaving the chamber, any&nbsp;
memories of the particulars

00:45:26.460 --> 00:45:29.940
of 055 seem to spontaneously erase themselves.

00:45:30.540 --> 00:45:33.120
Hence, the Self-Keeping Secret.

00:45:33.120 --> 00:45:35.100
But this didn’t deter Walter.

00:45:35.100 --> 00:45:39.060
Perhaps his greatest advantage was that he
didn’t know enough about the thing he was

00:45:39.060 --> 00:45:42.000
investigating to know how futile his mission
was.

00:45:42.000 --> 00:45:47.280
He wanted to know the unknowable, and a pesky
issue like “impossibility” wouldn’t

00:45:47.280 --> 00:45:47.940
stop him.

00:45:47.940 --> 00:45:52.680
He’d get to whoever he needed to at Site
19 to get the answers he needed.

00:45:52.680 --> 00:45:56.460
Of course most people had no knowledge of
the mysterious anomaly.

00:45:56.460 --> 00:45:59.220
The common response he got&nbsp;
back from his colleagues&nbsp;

00:45:59.220 --> 00:46:00.780
was, “055?

00:46:00.780 --> 00:46:02.460
Do we even have an 055?”

00:46:02.460 --> 00:46:07.680
While the realization of sudden memory loss
- or the realization of 055’s existence

00:46:07.680 --> 00:46:13.740
- has been known to cause momentary stress,
there are no known long term physical or mental

00:46:13.740 --> 00:46:16.320
effects from 055’s anomalous abilities.

00:46:16.320 --> 00:46:21.960
It’s a fleeting idea in its purest form
- like forgetting why you walked into a room.

00:46:21.960 --> 00:46:28.560
055 could be the most harmless object on the
Foundation’s roster, or the most deadly.

00:46:28.560 --> 00:46:31.500
Either way, we just don’t know.

00:46:31.500 --> 00:46:34.800
At times, Walter worried he was going insane.

00:46:34.800 --> 00:46:38.820
055, and everything related to it, was gaslighting
him.

00:46:38.820 --> 00:46:41.040
Was 055 even real?

00:46:41.040 --> 00:46:46.440
The one thing that proved to him that 055
must have existed is that its containment

00:46:46.440 --> 00:46:47.880
chamber existed.

00:46:48.480 --> 00:46:52.740
According to the official records kept by
the Foundation on the Site 19 Containment

00:46:52.740 --> 00:47:00.000
Facilities, 055 is kept in a “five by five
by two point five meter square room constructed

00:47:00.000 --> 00:47:04.500
of fifty-foot-thick cement, with a Faraday
cage surrounding the cement walls.”

00:47:04.500 --> 00:47:10.260
The report continues that, “Access is via
a heavy containment door measuring two by

00:47:10.260 --> 00:47:15.780
two point five meters constructed on bearings
to ensure door closes and locks automatically

00:47:15.780 --> 00:47:17.460
unless held open deliberately.”

00:47:18.060 --> 00:47:23.640
055’s cell is one of the few to have no
posted security guards, and any personnel

00:47:23.640 --> 00:47:28.740
working on other SCPs in the area are ordered
to remain at least fifty feet from the geometric

00:47:28.740 --> 00:47:33.240
center of 055’s cell, where the anomaly
itself is kept.

00:47:33.240 --> 00:47:38.160
When he tried to explore further why the cell
was constructed in this manner, he found that

00:47:38.160 --> 00:47:41.220
- surprise, surprise - nobody knew.

00:47:41.220 --> 00:47:47.820
055 was an anomaly whose containment requirements
were so mysterious that it automatically netted

00:47:47.820 --> 00:47:49.560
itself a Keter Class designation.

00:47:49.560 --> 00:47:55.080
After all, how can you properly contain something
you can’t even hope to comprehend?

00:47:55.080 --> 00:47:58.680
There were plenty of rumors about the true
nature of 055.

00:47:59.520 --> 00:48:05.940
Some of the more conspiratorial minds at Site
19 theorized that 055 was actually an autonomous

00:48:05.940 --> 00:48:12.060
or remotely controlled spy inserted into the
site to observe Foundation operations - or

00:48:12.060 --> 00:48:13.740
even humanity as a whole.

00:48:13.740 --> 00:48:18.420
If you’re on the more paranoid end of the
psychological spectrum, this theory makes

00:48:18.420 --> 00:48:19.200
total sense.

00:48:19.200 --> 00:48:23.700
An anomaly that’s physically impossible
to remember, even when writings and pictures

00:48:23.700 --> 00:48:26.880
on the subject exist, would be a perfect spy.

00:48:26.880 --> 00:48:30.660
However, this was all ultimately little more
than speculation.

00:48:30.660 --> 00:48:34.380
Walter was barely any further along than when
he started.

00:48:34.380 --> 00:48:39.180
There were multiple points in his investigation
where Walter seriously considered giving up,

00:48:39.180 --> 00:48:42.840
until, finally, he had a major breakthrough.

00:48:42.840 --> 00:48:48.720
Dr. Bartholomew Hughes and Dr. John Marachek
were two scientists that had performed extensive

00:48:48.720 --> 00:48:54.540
research into 055, and who - Walter hoped
- might have the answers he sought about the

00:48:54.540 --> 00:48:55.560
Self-Keeping Secret.

00:48:55.560 --> 00:49:01.500
These scientists were the first to discover
the “Anti-Memetic” nature of 055, performing

00:49:01.500 --> 00:49:06.120
numerous tests on D-Class personnel to see
if it was possible to create feasible written

00:49:06.120 --> 00:49:11.820
records, sketches, or any other records or
impressions that could bypass its anomalous

00:49:11.820 --> 00:49:12.300
effects.

00:49:12.300 --> 00:49:19.020
The disorienting, memory-ruining effects of
055 also extend to any materials concerning

00:49:19.020 --> 00:49:19.980
055.

00:49:19.980 --> 00:49:25.800
It seemed to be a truly uncrackable code,
but Dr. Hughes may have finally found some

00:49:25.800 --> 00:49:26.940
cracks in the armor.

00:49:27.600 --> 00:49:33.720
For starters, the fact we’re able to remember
that 055 is Anti-Memetic is an ironic exception

00:49:33.720 --> 00:49:35.400
to its Anti-Memetic qualities.

00:49:35.400 --> 00:49:42.180
This revelation also inspired another realization
from Dr. Hughes: Would it be possible to discover

00:49:42.180 --> 00:49:47.520
more about 055 from the process of deduction
rather than the typical induction?

00:49:47.520 --> 00:49:53.580
In other words, could they possibly learn
about 055 by figuring out all the things it

00:49:53.580 --> 00:49:55.860
isn’t rather than what it is?

00:49:55.860 --> 00:50:00.660
Dr. Marachek designed an experiment with Dr.
Hughes to explore this theory.

00:50:00.660 --> 00:50:06.360
They designed the experiment around a simple
question: Is 055 not spherical?

00:50:06.360 --> 00:50:12.120
In designing the question to specifically
find out what 055 isn’t, they hoped to subvert

00:50:12.120 --> 00:50:14.100
the anomaly’s Anti-Memetic Powers.

00:50:14.100 --> 00:50:18.000
Walter was fascinated by this potential method
of getting answers.

00:50:18.000 --> 00:50:22.920
Marachek and Hughes found that, while the
questioning process for those exposed was

00:50:22.920 --> 00:50:30.300
often arduous and frustrating, they could
now definitely say that 055 is not a sphere.

00:50:30.300 --> 00:50:36.660
It is theoretically possible to discover the
true nature of 055 by an almost endless barrage

00:50:36.660 --> 00:50:42.120
of deductive questions, though whether command
would authorize the resources for such extensive

00:50:42.120 --> 00:50:44.340
testing is still an open question.

00:50:44.340 --> 00:50:50.580
Walter, in his desperation, begged Marachek
and Hughes for clearance to view 055 himself.

00:50:50.580 --> 00:50:55.800
The curiosity had become too great during
his search to just walk away with the single

00:50:55.800 --> 00:50:58.200
fact that 055 wasn’t spherical.

00:50:58.200 --> 00:51:00.240
He needed to see this thing.

00:51:00.240 --> 00:51:06.060
And after several weeks of filling out forms
and cutting red tape, his wish was finally

00:51:06.060 --> 00:51:06.780
granted.

00:51:06.780 --> 00:51:14.340
Walter Bainbridge was allowed a private audience
with SCP - 055, the subject of his months-long

00:51:14.340 --> 00:51:14.820
obsession.

00:51:14.820 --> 00:51:20.100
Outsiders observed that Walter spent just
over an hour in the containment chamber, taking

00:51:20.100 --> 00:51:25.680
photos, drawing sketches, writing down notes,
recording audio logs, and reciting memory

00:51:25.680 --> 00:51:26.220
mnemonics.

00:51:26.220 --> 00:51:31.560
He was pulling out every stop to counteract
the anti-memetic effects of the Self-Keeping

00:51:31.560 --> 00:51:31.860
Secret.

00:51:31.860 --> 00:51:38.160
He was adamant that he would not be defeated
by his non-spherical nemesis, not after all

00:51:38.160 --> 00:51:39.240
this time and effort.

00:51:39.240 --> 00:51:44.820
Once his time in the 055 containment chamber
was over, he retired back to his office to

00:51:44.820 --> 00:51:50.160
finally digitize his exhaustive findings,
so that his supervisor, Mr. Kovach, would

00:51:50.160 --> 00:51:51.480
finally get off his back.

00:51:51.480 --> 00:51:55.680
Walter smiled, took a deep breath, and began
to type.

00:51:55.680 --> 00:51:58.020
“SCP - 059.

00:51:58.020 --> 00:51:58.980
Keter Class.

00:51:58.980 --> 00:52:04.200
This anomaly is a radioactive mineral that
emits a unique radiation known as Delta Radiation.

00:52:04.200 --> 00:52:08.520
Exposure to this radiation has caused strange
fungal growths on the infected...”

00:52:08.520 --> 00:52:11.520
Wait, what was this supposed to be about again?

00:52:11.520 --> 00:52:13.620
Oh well, it couldn’t have been that important.

00:52:13.620 --> 00:52:20.220
It was November 20th, 2019, and the helicopter
circled far above in the freezing wind of

00:52:20.220 --> 00:52:21.000
the Antarctic.

00:52:21.000 --> 00:52:24.120
SCP Foundation Site Director Jason Monroe&nbsp;

00:52:24.120 --> 00:52:26.880
looked down at the isolated&nbsp;
above-ground facilities

00:52:26.880 --> 00:52:29.220
of Provisional Site-344-1.

00:52:29.220 --> 00:52:32.160
Something about this place made him nervous.

00:52:32.160 --> 00:52:33.060
Edgy.

00:52:33.060 --> 00:52:36.960
And for good reason: Between 2003 and 2019,&nbsp;

00:52:36.960 --> 00:52:40.200
twenty-nine Mobile Task&nbsp;
Force units and seventy-three

00:52:40.200 --> 00:52:44.400
members of D-Class personnel had gone missing
here and never been found.

00:52:44.400 --> 00:52:47.640
Monroe thought he was here&nbsp;
for a routine investigation&nbsp;

00:52:47.640 --> 00:52:50.520
into negligence and mismanagement, but little

00:52:50.520 --> 00:52:53.640
did he know, he was in for so much more.

00:52:53.640 --> 00:53:00.660
This is the story of SCP - 5545, and one man’s
journey into his own worst nightmare.

00:53:00.660 --> 00:53:01.620
Literally.

00:53:01.620 --> 00:53:06.480
But this nightmare began a long time ago - 300
years, to be exact.

00:53:06.480 --> 00:53:09.960
And like most nightmares, it started as a
dream.

00:53:09.960 --> 00:53:15.000
That dream was one of expansion - national
powers across Europe wanted to be the first

00:53:15.000 --> 00:53:18.060
to conquer the globe and&nbsp;
expand into new territories,&nbsp;

00:53:18.060 --> 00:53:20.700
and sent countless exploratory missions off

00:53:20.700 --> 00:53:23.100
into the unknown to achieve this goal.

00:53:23.100 --> 00:53:27.900
Any history book will tell you that the first
outsiders to lay eyes upon the continent of

00:53:27.900 --> 00:53:33.300
Antarctica did so in 1820 - the reality is
that the first ones to get there actually

00:53:33.300 --> 00:53:36.060
landed in the late 1700s.

00:53:36.060 --> 00:53:41.700
The hapless explorers ventured into mainland
Antarctica and made base camps, before searching

00:53:41.700 --> 00:53:44.460
and digging for any useful resources nearby.

00:53:44.460 --> 00:53:49.500
They came upon a strange discovery: A hallway,
hidden beneath the ice.

00:53:49.500 --> 00:53:54.900
Not a passage in the ice, but a true hallway
- complete with light fixtures.

00:53:54.900 --> 00:54:00.060
The confused explorers ventured down into
these impossible hallways, and for many of

00:54:00.060 --> 00:54:03.180
them, it would be the last thing they ever
did.

00:54:03.180 --> 00:54:07.680
No matter how long they walked, it seemed
like the hallways just kept going.

00:54:07.680 --> 00:54:12.240
As they continued to walk for hours, they
hoped they’d find something… anything.

00:54:12.240 --> 00:54:14.580
And eventually, they did.

00:54:14.580 --> 00:54:19.500
They passed from these hallways into somewhere
different altogether, and most of them were

00:54:19.500 --> 00:54:20.640
never heard from again.

00:54:20.640 --> 00:54:25.680
Those who did manage to escape often died
or took their own lives soon after.

00:54:25.680 --> 00:54:30.600
Whatever it was they’d discovered down there,
they didn’t want to live with it on their

00:54:30.600 --> 00:54:31.020
minds.

00:54:31.020 --> 00:54:36.180
It’s believed that over seventy colonial
explorers disappeared or died this way and

00:54:36.180 --> 00:54:40.560
that most who found these endless hallways
beneath the Antarctic ice never returned.

00:54:40.560 --> 00:54:47.100
The multiple anomalous objects and phenomena
that make up SCP-5545 came into the Foundation’s

00:54:47.100 --> 00:54:52.980
hands several centuries later on September
18th, 2003, when during an expedition into

00:54:52.980 --> 00:54:56.580
the Antarctic, they too found the endless
hallways.

00:54:56.580 --> 00:55:02.100
The Foundation built Provisional Site-344-1
around them, hoping to safely seal them off

00:55:02.100 --> 00:55:05.580
from any other unwitting Antarctic explorers
or researchers.

00:55:05.580 --> 00:55:09.120
But there was something else lurking beneath
the ice in Antarctica.

00:55:09.120 --> 00:55:10.560
Something dangerous.

00:55:10.560 --> 00:55:17.100
The hallways were designated as SCP - 5545
- 1 and were thought to be the extent of the

00:55:17.100 --> 00:55:24.240
anomalous activity at the site, but soon SCP
- 5545 - 2 was discovered, which resulted

00:55:24.240 --> 00:55:26.520
in the deaths of sixteen researchers.

00:55:26.520 --> 00:55:29.760
So what exactly is 5545 - 2?

00:55:29.760 --> 00:55:34.980
It’s an entity so volatile that even knowing
about it is considered to be a containment

00:55:34.980 --> 00:55:40.020
breach, and - as a result - it’s kept in
Provisional Site-344-2.

00:55:40.020 --> 00:55:45.360
Unlike Site - 344 - 1, 344 - 2 isn’t a physical
space.

00:55:45.360 --> 00:55:50.820
It’s conceptual, accessible only through
the endless hallways, created with the express

00:55:50.820 --> 00:55:56.220
purpose of keeping 5545 - 1 and 5545 - 2 separate.

00:55:56.220 --> 00:55:56.880
Why?

00:55:56.880 --> 00:56:04.020
Because whenever the two come into contact,
the result is 5545 - 3: The network of endless

00:56:04.020 --> 00:56:05.460
hallways expanding.

00:56:05.460 --> 00:56:10.140
If they remained in contact, the hallways
would continue to expand and the entire planet

00:56:10.140 --> 00:56:14.100
could be filled with endless hallways in just
four to six hours.

00:56:14.100 --> 00:56:20.820
While the two are apart though, 5545 - 3 reverses,
but it always would take just a few hours

00:56:20.820 --> 00:56:24.720
to throw the whole world into a chaos of infinite
hallways.

00:56:24.720 --> 00:56:28.920
SCP-5545 has been given the classification
“Safe”…

00:56:28.920 --> 00:56:33.840
Wait, we’re dealing with a mysterious and
volatile anomaly that’s claimed a huge number

00:56:33.840 --> 00:56:39.600
of lives and still somehow eludes true Foundation
understanding, yet the official SCP Foundation

00:56:39.600 --> 00:56:41.220
classification is “Safe?”

00:56:41.220 --> 00:56:42.420
How could this be?

00:56:42.420 --> 00:56:47.460
Monroe was the Director of Site - 58, and
was the definition of no-nonsense.

00:56:47.460 --> 00:56:52.020
Prior to taking the Site Director position,
he was a decorated member of Mobile Task Force

00:56:52.020 --> 00:56:55.500
Eta-10 and helped contain numerous Keter-Class
anomalies.

00:56:55.500 --> 00:57:00.120
He’d been around the proverbial block when
it came to anomalous activity, and something

00:57:00.120 --> 00:57:04.020
about SCP - 5545, and the&nbsp;
management of Provisional&nbsp;

00:57:04.020 --> 00:57:07.200
Site 344, seemed awfully suspicious to him.

00:57:07.200 --> 00:57:08.940
And he had questions.

00:57:08.940 --> 00:57:13.020
Like how such an unpredictable anomaly could
be declared “safe”?

00:57:13.020 --> 00:57:15.720
And why had there been such&nbsp;
a lapse of communication&nbsp;

00:57:15.720 --> 00:57:17.880
between the Foundation and Doctor Gabriel

00:57:17.880 --> 00:57:21.180
Reed, who’d been running the facility for
the past two decades?

00:57:21.180 --> 00:57:27.480
And most of all, just what exactly was the
mysterious SCP - 5545 - 2?

00:57:27.480 --> 00:57:33.000
Monroe started to believe that something terrible
had happened at the site, and Reed was covering

00:57:33.000 --> 00:57:33.540
it all up.

00:57:33.540 --> 00:57:38.280
But to find out for sure, he’d need to go
to Antarctica and investigate it himself.

00:57:38.280 --> 00:57:43.140
Information around this supposedly “Safe”
anomaly was highly classified - those without

00:57:43.140 --> 00:57:45.780
O5 clearance could face termination for snooping.

00:57:45.780 --> 00:57:48.060
But that didn’t scare Jason Monroe.

00:57:48.060 --> 00:57:51.000
He’d dealt with Keters before, he could
deal with this.

00:57:51.000 --> 00:57:52.740
Or so he thought.

00:57:52.740 --> 00:57:57.420
Monroe submitted a request and was granted
unanimous approval by the O5 Council to travel

00:57:57.420 --> 00:58:01.320
to Provisional Site 344 and get to the bottom
of this mystery.

00:58:01.320 --> 00:58:06.420
He took a chopper to the base soon after,
armed with a concealed firearm and a Hostile

00:58:06.420 --> 00:58:12.060
Meme Detector - or HMD - to test whether the
base and its staff had somehow fallen under

00:58:12.060 --> 00:58:15.780
a hazardous memetic effect from SCP - 5545.

00:58:15.780 --> 00:58:19.080
He’d find the answers, or die trying.

00:58:19.080 --> 00:58:24.120
The moment Monroe arrived, he couldn’t help
but notice the strange way the staff behaved.

00:58:24.120 --> 00:58:26.640
They seemed listless; almost depressive.

00:58:26.640 --> 00:58:33.180
When he showed his credentials to a researcher,
they simply said “SCP-5545-2 is contained

00:58:33.180 --> 00:58:34.860
in Site-344-2.”

00:58:34.860 --> 00:58:37.800
His request to see Dr. Reed that night was
denied.

00:58:37.800 --> 00:58:40.320
Dr. Reed was busy, he was told.

00:58:40.320 --> 00:58:41.520
Wait until tomorrow.

00:58:41.520 --> 00:58:46.860
The next day, Monroe met with Dr. Reed, but
the results of the meeting were underwhelming

00:58:46.860 --> 00:58:47.700
to say the least.

00:58:47.700 --> 00:58:52.800
Just like the rest of the staff on the site,
he seemed exhausted, as though he hadn’t

00:58:52.800 --> 00:58:53.580
slept in days.

00:58:53.580 --> 00:58:58.560
His responses were quiet and evasive, and
he refused to tell Monroe anything that wasn’t

00:58:58.560 --> 00:59:00.060
in the official files already.

00:59:00.060 --> 00:59:04.740
Monroe ran the conversation through the HMD
and found nothing out of the ordinary.

00:59:04.740 --> 00:59:06.180
What was going on here?

00:59:06.180 --> 00:59:09.180
Monroe was irritated, but not deterred.

00:59:09.180 --> 00:59:11.700
Nothing would stop him from finding out the
truth.

00:59:12.660 --> 00:59:17.580
The next day, he flexed his O5 credentials
and hacked into the base’s security system.

00:59:17.580 --> 00:59:23.580
This gave him access to cameras around Site
- 344 -1, but more importantly, there was

00:59:23.580 --> 00:59:27.960
a single camera inside the mysterious Site
- 344 - 2.

00:59:27.960 --> 00:59:29.100
Jackpot.

00:59:29.100 --> 00:59:36.540
But when he looked at it, the feed was an
entirely black screen with the words “SCP-5545-2

00:59:36.540 --> 00:59:39.660
is contained in Site-344-2.”

00:59:39.660 --> 00:59:45.960
The footage of the staff in 344 - 1 was equally
strange: The eighteen employees on site all

00:59:45.960 --> 00:59:49.680
sat at computer banks, with nothing but static
playing on their screens.

00:59:49.680 --> 00:59:54.720
Monroe kept digging though, and was able to
hack into the security footage of Dr. Reed’s

00:59:54.720 --> 00:59:54.900
office.

00:59:54.900 --> 01:00:00.300
As he watched, he discovered a fifteen minute
period where Reed left the office each day.

01:00:00.300 --> 01:00:07.620
He could use this brief window to break in
and collect more intel on SCP - 5545 - 2.

01:00:07.620 --> 01:00:12.300
Monroe was so wrapped up in the investigation
that he almost forgot the more immediate danger

01:00:12.300 --> 01:00:18.960
around him, and nearly wandered into one of
the endless hallways of 5545 - 1 by mistake.

01:00:18.960 --> 01:00:21.660
He made a note to be more careful in future...

01:00:21.660 --> 01:00:26.640
His first attempt at breaking into Dr. Reed’s
office didn’t produce many answers - one

01:00:26.640 --> 01:00:30.780
piece of evidence was a blurry picture of
what looked like a Mobile Task Force entering

01:00:30.780 --> 01:00:33.540
a 5545 - 1 hallway in the dark.

01:00:33.540 --> 01:00:38.580
Another was a spreadsheet featuring all the
personnel, living or dead, who’d worked

01:00:38.580 --> 01:00:43.500
at the site - but one name, and the details
of whether this person was alive or dead,

01:00:43.500 --> 01:00:45.300
was completely redacted.

01:00:45.300 --> 01:00:49.140
Anything particularly juicy was hidden behind
O5 clearance.

01:00:49.140 --> 01:00:53.040
If Monroe wanted the answers, he’d need
to break through.

01:00:53.040 --> 01:00:58.860
That night, he had a horrific recurring nightmare,
one that had plagued him since he joined MTF

01:00:58.860 --> 01:00:59.220
Eta-10.

01:00:59.220 --> 01:01:02.760
He dreamed he was in a fancy dining room with
a grand fireplace.

01:01:02.760 --> 01:01:05.700
The room was full of statues of men and women.

01:01:05.700 --> 01:01:08.880
The men looked angry, and the women looked
afraid.

01:01:08.880 --> 01:01:13.740
As he approached the fireplace, the ceiling
extended infinitely up into the darkness.

01:01:13.740 --> 01:01:19.140
Suddenly, the zombie-like body of a teenage
girl appears in the fireplace, hanging from

01:01:19.140 --> 01:01:19.920
a long thread.

01:01:19.920 --> 01:01:25.380
Her eyes look furious and full of rage, and
Monroe somehow knows that he’s the reason

01:01:25.380 --> 01:01:26.400
for her hate.

01:01:26.400 --> 01:01:31.620
When he steps into the fireplace in this dream,
she attacks him, the two intertwine, and they

01:01:31.620 --> 01:01:32.400
burn forever.

01:01:32.400 --> 01:01:37.560
The one difference was that in this new iteration
of the dream, he blinked upon entering the

01:01:37.560 --> 01:01:40.320
fireplace, and suddenly, he was in a hallway.

01:01:40.320 --> 01:01:45.240
He awoke sure that something was terribly
wrong here, but he couldn’t give up now.

01:01:45.240 --> 01:01:49.860
The next day, Monroe broke into Dr. Reed’s
office and made a horrifying discovery.

01:01:49.860 --> 01:01:55.680
He found files indicating that Dr. Reed was
knowingly sending Mobile Task Forces and D-Class

01:01:55.680 --> 01:02:00.660
personnel into the infinite hallways of 5545
- 1 to their doom.

01:02:00.660 --> 01:02:03.480
He also found evidence that&nbsp;
Reed and the researchers&nbsp;

01:02:03.480 --> 01:02:06.060
had been spying on him, somehow intercepting

01:02:06.060 --> 01:02:07.680
copies of the notes he had been taking.

01:02:07.680 --> 01:02:10.860
That’s when Dr. Reed entered the office
and interrupted him.

01:02:10.860 --> 01:02:14.460
Monroe panicked and drew his weapon, holding
the doctor at gunpoint.

01:02:14.460 --> 01:02:19.560
He was breaking so many Foundation rules,
but right now, he feared for his life.

01:02:19.560 --> 01:02:22.560
The doctor seemed unbothered by Monroe’s
threats though.

01:02:22.560 --> 01:02:27.360
He told Monroe that everything was going to
plan, and that he should go back to his room.

01:02:27.360 --> 01:02:32.580
Monroe was becoming increasingly paranoid
- he felt that, at any moment, guards might

01:02:32.580 --> 01:02:34.020
burst in and execute him.

01:02:34.020 --> 01:02:36.240
Nothing about this place made sense.

01:02:36.240 --> 01:02:38.400
He worried he was going insane.

01:02:38.400 --> 01:02:44.340
Perhaps the only way to find answers was to
go even deeper: To risk it all, and venture

01:02:44.340 --> 01:02:51.840
through the endless hallways to find SCP - 5545
- 2 himself, and finally discover what this

01:02:51.840 --> 01:02:53.700
thing actually was.

01:02:53.700 --> 01:02:59.400
Monroe left his room and stepped into one
of the endless hallways of 5545 - 1 that was

01:02:59.400 --> 01:03:01.320
located just across from his dorm.

01:03:01.320 --> 01:03:06.600
He found that it was a hallway like all the
others on site - Plain concrete, worn with

01:03:06.600 --> 01:03:09.000
age, with simple light fixtures on the walls.

01:03:09.000 --> 01:03:12.180
He walked for hours, recording with a concealed
device.

01:03:12.180 --> 01:03:16.200
The lights suddenly went out, leaving him
in complete darkness.

01:03:16.200 --> 01:03:21.780
When they flicked back on, he was in a very
different environment: A grand, old carpeted

01:03:21.780 --> 01:03:24.360
hallway, the kind you’d see in an old mansion.

01:03:24.360 --> 01:03:26.100
He broke into a cold sweat.

01:03:26.100 --> 01:03:31.980
What was so familiar about this place?He kept
walking, wracked with terror, until this new

01:03:31.980 --> 01:03:39.000
hallway finally led him to the place he’d
been seeking: Site 344 - 2, the domain of

01:03:39.000 --> 01:03:40.920
5545 - 2.

01:03:40.920 --> 01:03:46.620
It was a large, poorly-lit room, filled with
grimacing statues and a large fireplace at

01:03:46.620 --> 01:03:47.340
the far end.

01:03:47.340 --> 01:03:52.980
It was the exact same room from Monroe’s
dream - with one horrifying difference.

01:03:52.980 --> 01:03:58.620
Monroe noticed a single white thread hanging
down from the infinite ceiling, and when he

01:03:58.620 --> 01:04:01.500
looked up to find its source, he screamed.

01:04:01.500 --> 01:04:05.700
There were hundreds of bodies hanging and
swinging from the ceiling above him - everyone

01:04:05.700 --> 01:04:13.080
who SCP - 5545 - 2 had ever killed, including
MTF members, D-Class Personnel, and even the

01:04:13.080 --> 01:04:15.660
colonial explorers from hundreds of years
before.

01:04:15.660 --> 01:04:17.940
And all of them were him.

01:04:17.940 --> 01:04:19.560
Every single one.

01:04:19.560 --> 01:04:20.760
They had his face.

01:04:20.760 --> 01:04:26.340
And there, hanging in the middle of the room
at ground level, was the body of a teenage

01:04:26.340 --> 01:04:28.500
girl, the one from his dream.

01:04:28.500 --> 01:04:34.020
In that moment, he finally recognized her:
She was the girl he killed.

01:04:34.020 --> 01:04:35.160
The first him.

01:04:35.160 --> 01:04:37.020
Hundreds of years ago.

01:04:37.020 --> 01:04:40.620
Much like Monroe, you’re probably wondering:
What is going on here?

01:04:40.620 --> 01:04:46.080
Thanks to declassified communications between
Dr. Reed and the O5 Council, we can tell you.

01:04:46.080 --> 01:04:51.600
Jason Monroe is a man who’s been reincarnated
hundreds of times over the last three hundred

01:04:51.600 --> 01:04:55.020
years, ever since he murdered a teenage girl…

01:04:55.020 --> 01:04:57.840
A girl named Emily… his daughter.

01:04:57.840 --> 01:05:04.260
This murder sparked the existence of SCP - 5545
as an eternally recurring punishment for his

01:05:04.260 --> 01:05:04.740
crimes.

01:05:04.740 --> 01:05:10.140
Since figuring this out, the Foundation has
kept tabs on Monroe’s reincarnations - whether

01:05:10.140 --> 01:05:14.520
they’re MTF members, D-Class personnel,
or even Site Directors.

01:05:14.520 --> 01:05:21.060
They see to it that these reincarnations always
find their way back to 5545 - 2 to take his

01:05:21.060 --> 01:05:25.500
punishment, and prevent the infinite hallway
expansion that threatens to destroy the world.

01:05:25.500 --> 01:05:29.460
It’s a plan everyone is in on - everyone
except him.

01:05:29.460 --> 01:05:34.080
But every time he enters that nightmare-haunting
room, it all comes rushing back.

01:05:34.080 --> 01:05:39.540
In that moment though, he knew his crime,
and he somehow knew how many times this punishment

01:05:39.540 --> 01:05:40.740
had unfolded for him.

01:05:40.740 --> 01:05:46.620
He now had two choices: Repent and accept
the punishment again, or leave and activate

01:05:46.620 --> 01:05:52.500
5545 - 3, potentially allowing the endless
tunnels to expand across the world.

01:05:52.500 --> 01:05:56.580
Like his many predecessors, Monroe made the
decent choice.

01:05:56.580 --> 01:06:01.500
He accepted his punishment and allowed his
own string to coil around him as the lights

01:06:01.500 --> 01:06:05.760
in the room went off, one by one, leaving
only darkness.

01:06:05.760 --> 01:06:10.860
Jason Monroe - that version of him, at least
- was never seen again.

01:06:10.860 --> 01:06:16.440
But The SCP Foundation is already eyeing up
his next reincarnation, and preparing to let

01:06:16.440 --> 01:06:19.680
this twisted cycle play out all over again.

01:06:19.680 --> 01:06:25.980
It skitters in the dark - its insect-like
legs tapping across the marble floors as terrified

01:06:25.980 --> 01:06:28.020
Foundation researchers flee.

01:06:28.020 --> 01:06:34.680
They hear its voice - the deep, silky tones
of an elderly British man, spouting nonsense

01:06:34.680 --> 01:06:41.160
like “The nightmare is a dream to the nameless
slug that wanders across minefield and the

01:06:41.160 --> 01:06:43.500
remains of deer and kings.”

01:06:43.500 --> 01:06:47.040
While the scientists run, the creature gains
on them.

01:06:47.040 --> 01:06:48.120
It’s fast.

01:06:48.120 --> 01:06:50.280
Impossibly fast.

01:06:50.280 --> 01:06:55.920
While they still try to escape down this darkened
hallway, earsplitting containment breach sirens

01:06:55.920 --> 01:06:56.880
blast through the air.

01:06:56.880 --> 01:07:00.240
They may try to escape, but it’s futile.

01:07:00.240 --> 01:07:03.360
In a sense, they’re already dead.

01:07:03.360 --> 01:07:07.800
All they are now… is prey for the Heart
of Darkness.

01:07:07.800 --> 01:07:12.300
When someone says the word “heart,” there
are a lot of images that come to mind.

01:07:12.300 --> 01:07:16.260
You might think of Valentine’s Day, heart-shaped
cards, and candies.

01:07:16.260 --> 01:07:19.860
You might think of heartbreak, rejection,
loss.

01:07:19.860 --> 01:07:22.500
You might simply think of&nbsp;
a heart in the anatomical&nbsp;

01:07:22.500 --> 01:07:25.260
sense, the vital organ that pumps blood through

01:07:25.260 --> 01:07:25.860
our bodies.

01:07:25.860 --> 01:07:31.560
It’s unlikely though that you would associate
the word heart with terror, destruction, and

01:07:31.560 --> 01:07:32.520
countless deaths.

01:07:32.520 --> 01:07:37.680
However, employees of the SCP Foundation might
think differently, especially if they’ve

01:07:37.680 --> 01:07:41.460
ever had a run-in with SCP-058.

01:07:41.460 --> 01:07:46.800
Much of the information about SCP-058’s
discovery is highly classified, but the few

01:07:46.800 --> 01:07:48.900
details that are known paint a chilling picture.

01:07:48.900 --> 01:07:55.200
At an SCP Foundation test site, the day was
proceeding as usual with scientists and security

01:07:55.200 --> 01:07:58.200
personnel going about their regular daily
tasks.

01:07:58.200 --> 01:08:03.360
There was no hint of danger in the air - beyond
the base level that always comes with setting

01:08:03.360 --> 01:08:06.480
foot in an SCP Foundation site, at least.

01:08:06.480 --> 01:08:11.760
Several researchers were performing an experiment,
the specifics of which have been expunged

01:08:11.760 --> 01:08:14.760
from all records, involving the carcass of
a cow.

01:08:14.760 --> 01:08:20.160
When a researcher, Dr. C, placed his hands
on the specimen and prepared to dissect it,

01:08:20.160 --> 01:08:23.760
he was shocked to feel a pulse coming from
the supposedly dead animal.

01:08:23.760 --> 01:08:29.940
Dr. C shared his surprise with his colleagues,
but his concerns were dismissed immediately.

01:08:29.940 --> 01:08:31.620
Clearly, this was a corpse.

01:08:31.620 --> 01:08:33.960
He was imagining things, they said.

01:08:33.960 --> 01:08:37.080
After all, he was relatively new to the job.

01:08:37.080 --> 01:08:38.820
It was probably just nerves.

01:08:38.820 --> 01:08:42.480
The head researcher, Dr. L, insisted that
he take over.

01:08:42.480 --> 01:08:47.940
Pushing Dr. C to the side, Dr. L began to
make an incision into the animal’s chest.

01:08:47.940 --> 01:08:51.480
As he did, he too felt something peculiar.

01:08:51.480 --> 01:08:53.160
There was no doubt about it.

01:08:53.160 --> 01:08:55.920
This dead cow had a beating heart.

01:08:55.920 --> 01:09:00.900
He looked up from his work to tell the other
researchers, to explain what he felt, but

01:09:00.900 --> 01:09:03.000
by then it was too late.

01:09:03.000 --> 01:09:06.300
Something horrible was already happening.

01:09:06.300 --> 01:09:11.160
With a stomach-churning sound of squishing
flesh, the cow’s heart burst from its chest

01:09:11.160 --> 01:09:12.480
and flopped onto the floor.

01:09:12.480 --> 01:09:16.860
It was terrifyingly large and all the doctors
jumped back from the sight of it.

01:09:16.860 --> 01:09:22.500
Four spindly, spider-like legs poked through
the flesh of the heart, and it began to quickly

01:09:22.500 --> 01:09:23.760
skitter about the room.

01:09:23.760 --> 01:09:27.780
Researchers reviewing the security footage
would later note that it didn’t just move

01:09:27.780 --> 01:09:28.380
randomly.

01:09:28.380 --> 01:09:34.680
It seemed agitated, angry at being discovered,
and it displayed immediate hostility toward

01:09:34.680 --> 01:09:36.180
the scientists in the room.

01:09:36.180 --> 01:09:41.580
Four tentacles next unfurled from within the
heart and stretched out into full, writhing

01:09:41.580 --> 01:09:42.180
appendages.

01:09:42.180 --> 01:09:47.100
They moved frighteningly fast as the heart
whipped around the room, and were coated in

01:09:47.100 --> 01:09:47.940
sharp spines.

01:09:47.940 --> 01:09:53.340
Finally, a stinger poked out from the back
of the heart, where the hole of the superior

01:09:53.340 --> 01:09:54.660
vena cava should be.

01:09:54.660 --> 01:09:59.580
All of the scientists leapt into action, with
one reaching for a scalpel and another moving

01:09:59.580 --> 01:10:00.300
towards the door.

01:10:00.300 --> 01:10:05.700
But before the men could so much as call for
help, the tentacles wrapped around them and

01:10:05.700 --> 01:10:07.080
ripped them to shreds.

01:10:07.080 --> 01:10:11.700
Hearing screams coming from the laboratory,
security personnel arrived to contain the

01:10:11.700 --> 01:10:12.180
threat.

01:10:12.180 --> 01:10:18.120
However, they were no match for the strange
creature that would soon be known as SCP-058.

01:10:18.120 --> 01:10:23.400
It tore through the security team in minutes,
leaving their tattered remains in its wake.

01:10:23.400 --> 01:10:25.980
Much to the horror of the surviving personnel&nbsp;

01:10:25.980 --> 01:10:29.820
at the site, SCP-058 was&nbsp;
able to escape containment

01:10:29.820 --> 01:10:32.100
and make its way to a neighboring town.

01:10:32.100 --> 01:10:36.900
Reports of the incident said that, when the
creature reached the town, you could hear

01:10:36.900 --> 01:10:38.580
the screaming for miles.

01:10:38.580 --> 01:10:44.820
SCP-058 carved a path of violence through
the town, attacking everything in sight with

01:10:44.820 --> 01:10:49.500
its stinger and tentacles, and leaving a trail
of strange fluid from its stinger.

01:10:49.500 --> 01:10:52.380
Dozens of citizens were killed, and seventy&nbsp;

01:10:52.380 --> 01:10:54.840
percent of the buildings&nbsp;
were completely destroyed.

01:10:54.840 --> 01:10:59.400
When agents were dispatched to the location
to retrieve the creature, they were shocked

01:10:59.400 --> 01:11:02.580
to see the level of destruction caused by
something so small.

01:11:02.580 --> 01:11:08.220
The scent of blood and smoke filled the air
and severed limbs littered the ground alongside

01:11:08.220 --> 01:11:10.440
splintered wood and collapsed brick.

01:11:10.440 --> 01:11:15.480
The survivors removed from the wreckage were
inconsolable, only calming down once they

01:11:15.480 --> 01:11:20.580
were given an amnestic to erase their memory
of the encounter with SCP-058.

01:11:20.580 --> 01:11:25.500
They had to be given new lives as well, as
there was nothing left of their old ones.

01:11:25.500 --> 01:11:32.880
SCP Foundation Agents were only able to capture
and contain SCP-058 after it was crushed by

01:11:32.880 --> 01:11:35.460
pieces of a building that collapsed on top
of it.

01:11:35.460 --> 01:11:41.940
They found it, flattened under a slab of stone,
legs flailing uselessly, tentacles limp.

01:11:41.940 --> 01:11:46.860
The agents were able to safely remove the
debris and bring in the heart without any

01:11:46.860 --> 01:11:48.720
more casualties that day.

01:11:48.720 --> 01:11:54.060
Once it was brought into captivity, the heart
was contained for three weeks, and remained

01:11:54.060 --> 01:11:55.920
largely quiet during that time.

01:11:55.920 --> 01:12:00.600
It was almost inconceivable that this small
creature hadn’t been killed in the incident

01:12:00.600 --> 01:12:05.220
- but the Foundation would soon learn that
this creature was freakishly durable.

01:12:05.220 --> 01:12:10.800
It escaped once more while being transferred
to an SCP Containment Site, again causing

01:12:10.800 --> 01:12:12.120
injuries and death.

01:12:12.120 --> 01:12:18.600
Having only experienced SCP-058 in its docile,
injured form, the team responsible for the

01:12:18.600 --> 01:12:23.340
transfer was unprepared for the sheer power
and violence the creature was capable of.

01:12:23.340 --> 01:12:28.440
It was able to escape an armored car and make
its way into a forest, where it eviscerated

01:12:28.440 --> 01:12:29.820
several squirrels and rabbits.

01:12:30.360 --> 01:12:34.380
Or rather, they were believed to be squirrels
and rabbits.

01:12:34.380 --> 01:12:37.620
The remains were too mutilated to properly
identify.

01:12:37.620 --> 01:12:41.580
It was only finally apprehended after being
crushed by an armored tank.

01:12:41.580 --> 01:12:46.560
But even this didn’t kill the creature,
and it was transferred to Armed Bio-Containment

01:12:46.560 --> 01:12:49.560
Area 14, where it remains to this day.

01:12:49.560 --> 01:12:55.440
There is a great deal about SCP-058 that is
horrifying, but there is one attribute it

01:12:55.440 --> 01:13:00.300
has shown in captivity that would make even
the most seasoned researcher’s skin crawl.

01:13:00.300 --> 01:13:07.260
Though it has no anatomical capacity for speech,
no throat, vocal chords, or even a respiratory

01:13:07.260 --> 01:13:10.500
system, SCP-058 speaks.

01:13:10.500 --> 01:13:16.800
Not only does it speak, but it speaks constantly,
in the deep voice of an elderly British man.

01:13:16.800 --> 01:13:22.260
No one knows who the voice might belong to,
or if it belongs to anyone at all.

01:13:22.260 --> 01:13:25.920
Perhaps it belongs only to SCP-058, somehow.

01:13:25.920 --> 01:13:30.900
As is often the case with SCP’s that are
capable of speech, there have been multiple

01:13:30.900 --> 01:13:36.000
attempts to interview the creature and each
time it ended in complete disaster.

01:13:36.000 --> 01:13:43.200
The only interview with an available transcript,
Interview 058-04, was conducted by Dr. Johnston

01:13:43.200 --> 01:13:45.900
with several personnel in the room for additional
security.

01:13:45.900 --> 01:13:51.300
Dr. Johnston attempted to get at the origins
of the creature, asking for its name and where

01:13:51.300 --> 01:13:51.960
it was from.

01:13:51.960 --> 01:13:57.540
The creature responded in cryptic, unsettling
poetry, giving answers to simple questions

01:13:57.540 --> 01:14:05.040
with “I had dreams of the queen wonders
that lived inside the hearts of love and silent

01:14:05.040 --> 01:14:09.180
treatments of all the elderly that I knew
were once whole.”

01:14:09.180 --> 01:14:15.180
After the fourth recitation of a similar verse
from the heart, Personnel D-067 made a comment

01:14:15.180 --> 01:14:17.220
on the creepy nature of its responses.

01:14:17.220 --> 01:14:23.940
Almost as if it was offended by the remark,
SCP-058 immediately stretched a tentacle across

01:14:23.940 --> 01:14:28.080
the room, wrapped it around D-067, and lifted
him into the air.

01:14:28.080 --> 01:14:34.020
He began screaming and clawing at the tentacle
in an attempt to free himself as his fellow

01:14:34.020 --> 01:14:35.340
personnel tried to help him.

01:14:35.340 --> 01:14:40.140
They grabbed at the tentacle, but found their
hands pierced and bloodied by the spikes that

01:14:40.140 --> 01:14:40.620
cover it.

01:14:40.620 --> 01:14:45.540
Dr. Johnston commanded 058 to let him go,
but it did not oblige.

01:14:45.540 --> 01:14:50.760
Instead, the man was crushed to death by the
tentacle, and his limp body left to drop to

01:14:50.760 --> 01:14:51.180
the floor.

01:14:51.180 --> 01:14:56.160
The interview concluded with a single statement
from the nightmarish heart: “The sensual

01:14:56.160 --> 01:15:03.180
violence of lust is all the assurance you
will ever need to know the worth of life.”

01:15:03.180 --> 01:15:09.660
SCP-058 never seems to say anything that has
to do with the people or events around it.

01:15:09.660 --> 01:15:15.480
It speaks in the same haunting, poetic language,
even when it’s attacking or killing something.

01:15:15.480 --> 01:15:22.860
No matter what happens to it, what is done
to it, or what anyone says, SCP-058 keeps

01:15:22.860 --> 01:15:28.440
talking and its tone of voice with the pace
of speech never changing, and further attempts

01:15:28.440 --> 01:15:32.340
to interview it have been abandoned due to
the safety risk involved.

01:15:32.340 --> 01:15:35.760
So what happened to the creature often called
“the heart of darkness?”

01:15:35.760 --> 01:15:37.020
Where is it now?

01:15:37.020 --> 01:15:42.960
SCP-058 is kept in an isolated containment
chamber made of reinforced heat-resistant

01:15:42.960 --> 01:15:45.840
steel with a backing of reinforced concrete.

01:15:45.840 --> 01:15:51.300
In order to placate its bloodthirsty, carnivorous
tendencies, the creature is given a live cow

01:15:51.300 --> 01:15:52.620
every three days.

01:15:52.620 --> 01:15:59.100
It is uncertain how exactly SCP-058 eats,
given that it does not have a mouth or stomach,

01:15:59.100 --> 01:16:03.180
but every time it is finished with a cow,
only bones remain.

01:16:03.180 --> 01:16:08.040
Routine maintenance is conducted on a tight
schedule, and the heart is never allowed out

01:16:08.040 --> 01:16:10.800
of its containment area under any circumstances.

01:16:10.800 --> 01:16:16.620
After two previous escapes from containment,
the Foundation is not taking any chances.

01:16:16.620 --> 01:16:21.180
Its constant speech is recorded via audio
devices that are running at all times.

01:16:21.180 --> 01:16:26.400
Out of concern for their safety and mental
health, no personnel are permitted to listen

01:16:26.400 --> 01:16:31.500
to recordings of SCP-058 speaking for more
than thirty minutes at a time.

01:16:31.500 --> 01:16:36.660
It is unknown what will happen to someone
who listens for longer, but it has been suggested

01:16:36.660 --> 01:16:38.880
that the consequences could be dire.

01:16:38.880 --> 01:16:42.000
If the creature ever escapes&nbsp;
again, the containment&nbsp;

01:16:42.000 --> 01:16:44.100
site is ordered to be destroyed via the detonation

01:16:44.100 --> 01:16:45.900
of an on-site nuclear weapon.

01:16:45.900 --> 01:16:51.240
Under no circumstances can it be allowed to
make its way out into the world again.

01:16:51.240 --> 01:16:58.080
Even with all of these precautions in place,
SCP-058 has been responsible for over 150

01:16:58.080 --> 01:17:00.120
deaths at its current containment site.

01:17:00.120 --> 01:17:05.700
There are some at the Foundation who have
campaigned for SCP-058 to be terminated, believing

01:17:05.700 --> 01:17:08.580
that there is more harm than good done by
keeping it alive.

01:17:08.580 --> 01:17:12.240
However, all attempts to terminate it have
so far failed.

01:17:12.240 --> 01:17:17.160
No matter how much physical trauma the heart
suffers, it does not seem to be able to be

01:17:17.160 --> 01:17:17.580
killed.

01:17:17.580 --> 01:17:21.480
It can only be incapacitated for a short time.

01:17:21.480 --> 01:17:25.920
There is a classic horror story by Edgar Allen
Poe called The Tell-tale Heart.

01:17:25.920 --> 01:17:31.260
In it, a man murders an old man and buries
his body beneath the floorboards of his home.

01:17:31.260 --> 01:17:36.300
There, even though the old man is certainly
dead, the murderer swears he can hear the

01:17:36.300 --> 01:17:38.880
beating of the heart coming up through the
floorboards.

01:17:38.880 --> 01:17:44.520
No matter what he does to quiet the sound,
he cannot escape it, and is eventually driven

01:17:44.520 --> 01:17:48.060
mad by the incessant beating of the dead man’s
heart.

01:17:48.060 --> 01:17:54.360
SCP-058 may not be a man’s heart, a human
heart, or even a real heart at all.

01:17:54.360 --> 01:17:59.820
However, just like the tell-tale heart, it
continues to impossibly beat no matter how

01:17:59.820 --> 01:18:01.920
hard anyone tries to stop it.

01:18:01.920 --> 01:18:07.380
The steady thump of its pulse haunts the SCP
Foundation, a grim reminder that there is

01:18:07.380 --> 01:18:13.560
something within its walls that can, and will,
kill everyone it can if given the chance.

01:18:13.560 --> 01:18:19.920
It couldn’t be destroyed by collapsed buildings,
an armored tank, or an army of experts, and

01:18:19.920 --> 01:18:24.480
the contingency plan of a nuclear blast is
not even guaranteed to work.

01:18:24.480 --> 01:18:29.760
It is entirely possible that, once the facility
has been laid to waste and all of the staff

01:18:29.760 --> 01:18:35.880
have been incinerated, and the smoke has finally
cleared, the heart of darkness will still

01:18:35.880 --> 01:18:40.980
be there… still beating, still talking,
and still killing.

01:18:40.980 --> 01:18:46.680
It all started in 1983 with reports of human
trafficking in the heart of Sin City.

01:18:46.680 --> 01:18:51.780
The FBI had gotten word of a potential trafficking
ring operating out of an abandoned department

01:18:51.780 --> 01:18:57.120
store in Las Vegas, Nevada, and immediately
began organizing a secret raid on the building.

01:18:57.120 --> 01:19:01.620
While they would indeed encounter something
horrifying within that abandoned department

01:19:01.620 --> 01:19:04.980
store, it wasn’t criminals or human trafficking.

01:19:04.980 --> 01:19:07.860
In fact, it wasn’t human at all.

01:19:07.860 --> 01:19:12.360
This is the horrifying story of SCP - 847.

01:19:12.360 --> 01:19:15.000
After weeks of planning,&nbsp;
the raid on the department&nbsp;

01:19:15.000 --> 01:19:17.100
store was conducted in the dead of night.

01:19:17.100 --> 01:19:22.740
Agents covered all the exits and entrances
and a helicopter was stationed nearby in case

01:19:22.740 --> 01:19:24.000
anyone attempted to run.

01:19:24.000 --> 01:19:26.160
It should have been a perfect trap.

01:19:26.160 --> 01:19:30.300
But things never go as planned when you don’t
know what you’re dealing with.

01:19:30.300 --> 01:19:33.840
The agents breached the door, and began searching
the darkened building.

01:19:33.840 --> 01:19:38.580
It didn’t appear that there was any power,
so the traffickers must have had great night

01:19:38.580 --> 01:19:41.100
vision and a high tolerance for creepy locales.

01:19:41.100 --> 01:19:45.660
Agents soon heard a faint humming sound coming
from below - a generator.

01:19:45.660 --> 01:19:49.740
It must be located in the basement and be
the hub of this criminal enterprise.

01:19:49.740 --> 01:19:55.080
Readying themselves for whatever they were
about to find, the agents descended into the

01:19:55.080 --> 01:19:55.320
basement.

01:19:55.320 --> 01:20:00.660
As they moved deeper into the building, they
found that lighting rigs had been set up - they

01:20:00.660 --> 01:20:05.160
must be getting closer to something, but that
“something” was still a mystery.

01:20:05.160 --> 01:20:09.960
A senior FBI Special Agent was leading the
charge, his pistol drawn and ready.

01:20:09.960 --> 01:20:11.100
It was quiet.

01:20:11.100 --> 01:20:12.180
Too quiet.

01:20:12.180 --> 01:20:15.480
Did the traffickers already realize they were
coming and clear out?

01:20:15.480 --> 01:20:20.640
He was ready to consider this bust a bust
when he heard a quiet mewling in the distance.

01:20:20.640 --> 01:20:25.320
A persistent, whining whimper that was undeniably
human.

01:20:25.320 --> 01:20:28.560
He gave the signal to his fellow agents to
follow the noise.

01:20:28.560 --> 01:20:33.780
They proceeded forward towards the pained
sounds and found themselves in a wide, well-lit

01:20:33.780 --> 01:20:36.240
room filled with department store mannequins.

01:20:36.240 --> 01:20:42.060
All were broken to some degree - some were
totally smashed to pieces, some were chained

01:20:42.060 --> 01:20:45.840
to walls and locked in cages, others were
wrapped in plastic.

01:20:45.840 --> 01:20:51.180
The agent wondered whether this was some kind
of twisted joke, or a messed up avant garde

01:20:51.180 --> 01:20:51.720
art piece.

01:20:51.720 --> 01:20:55.140
That’s when he noticed Her: A single, crouched&nbsp;

01:20:55.140 --> 01:20:58.320
figure in the distance,&nbsp;
hunched over and whimpering

01:20:58.320 --> 01:21:00.480
in a darkened corner of the room near a&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:21:00.480 --> 01:21:01.380
full-length
mirror.

01:21:01.380 --> 01:21:06.480
He couldn’t fully make her out, but he got
the sense that something was wrong - she was

01:21:06.480 --> 01:21:07.680
injured, bent over.

01:21:07.680 --> 01:21:09.420
Was she even missing an arm?

01:21:09.420 --> 01:21:11.820
Just what had these monsters done to this
woman?

01:21:11.820 --> 01:21:15.360
He whispered a request for back up into his
radio, and pushed on.

01:21:15.360 --> 01:21:20.280
When they got within 50 meters of the strange
woman, her demeanor changed entirely.

01:21:20.280 --> 01:21:24.900
She jerked around - her movements forced,
erratic, and painful-looking.

01:21:24.900 --> 01:21:30.180
The woman stared directly into the agent’s
eyes and began hobbling towards him., occasionally

01:21:30.180 --> 01:21:33.720
stopping to strike a pose as if modelling
during a photo shoot.

01:21:33.720 --> 01:21:39.480
Just then the agent made a horrifying realization
- this thing moving towards them wasn’t

01:21:39.480 --> 01:21:43.020
a woman at all, it was a living mannequin.

01:21:43.020 --> 01:21:47.280
As she got closer though, he also realized
that the mannequin’s broken left forearm

01:21:47.280 --> 01:21:49.680
had been carved into a large shiv.

01:21:49.680 --> 01:21:54.360
A female junior FBI agent had been one of
the many to pour into the room when the raid

01:21:54.360 --> 01:21:55.800
leader had radioed for backup.

01:21:55.800 --> 01:22:01.260
The second she entered the fifty meter range
of this strange mannequin, everything changed.

01:22:01.260 --> 01:22:06.540
In an instant, its eyes and mouth began dripping
with a thick, viscous resin.

01:22:06.540 --> 01:22:12.300
Its whimpering gasps suddenly became vicious,
earsplitting screeches, and it turned its

01:22:12.300 --> 01:22:14.400
gaze from the senior FBI agent.

01:22:14.400 --> 01:22:19.200
It was now focused on the junior agent who
had just entered the room and broke into a

01:22:19.200 --> 01:22:21.000
terrifying run straight towards her.

01:22:21.000 --> 01:22:24.420
The mannequin moved with a violent, single-minded
purpose.

01:22:24.420 --> 01:22:29.880
Other agents began firing but it was running
freakishly fast and easily dodged most of

01:22:29.880 --> 01:22:30.720
the bullets.

01:22:30.720 --> 01:22:34.680
The few that actually hit seemed to do nothing
to slow the creature down.

01:22:34.680 --> 01:22:37.860
It shrugged off the damage and kept running.

01:22:37.860 --> 01:22:42.720
With a great leap, it landed on the terrified
junior agent, and began jabbing at her with

01:22:42.720 --> 01:22:43.500
its bladed arm.

01:22:43.500 --> 01:22:48.060
The other agents stopped firing, fearing they
might accidentally hit their colleague during

01:22:48.060 --> 01:22:48.720
the panic.

01:22:48.720 --> 01:22:54.600
The mannequin was ruthless, clawing and stabbing,
with the strange resin leaking out of its

01:22:54.600 --> 01:22:55.440
every orifice.

01:22:55.440 --> 01:23:00.480
Terrified and unable to reach her gun, the
agent remembered her training - she reached

01:23:00.480 --> 01:23:04.800
into her belt and grabbed her stun gun, jamming
the two probes up against the creature’s

01:23:04.800 --> 01:23:07.140
chest and giving it 30,000 volts.

01:23:07.140 --> 01:23:12.540
The creature spasmed, fell backwards, and
collapsed in a heap on the ground - frozen.

01:23:12.540 --> 01:23:19.080
This was the first recorded encounter with
SCP - 847 - a violent living mannequin with

01:23:19.080 --> 01:23:21.060
a serious problem with women.

01:23:21.060 --> 01:23:25.800
This terrifying report was passed up the chain
of command until it landed on the desk of

01:23:25.800 --> 01:23:28.080
a Foundation Agent working in the FBI.

01:23:28.080 --> 01:23:32.940
The Foundation quickly swooped in and claimed
the mannequin, delivered necessary amnestic

01:23:32.940 --> 01:23:37.560
treatment to all who’d witnessed it, and
closely observed the female junior FBI agent’s

01:23:37.560 --> 01:23:40.680
recovery in a private hospital with Foundation
ties.

01:23:40.680 --> 01:23:46.320
As it turns out, they were right to do so,
as the junior agent was in for a gruesome

01:23:46.320 --> 01:23:46.740
fate.

01:23:46.740 --> 01:23:52.200
While the wounds she’d suffered at the hands
of SCP - 847 didn’t appear fatal, the fact

01:23:52.200 --> 01:23:57.180
that the mannequin’s anomalous resin excretions
entered the open wound changed everything.

01:23:57.180 --> 01:24:02.520
Several hours after being committed, the junior
agent began complaining of limb stiffness

01:24:02.520 --> 01:24:03.960
and difficulty moving.

01:24:03.960 --> 01:24:06.540
This quickly developed into full paralysis.

01:24:06.540 --> 01:24:13.200
Over time, her skin and internal organs began
to harden, until the process - dubbed plastination

01:24:13.200 --> 01:24:14.880
- came to a gruesome end.

01:24:14.880 --> 01:24:20.280
The junior agent wasn’t just dead, she had
been transformed into a mannequin.

01:24:20.280 --> 01:24:25.800
Foundation researchers were met with a truly
horrifying realization - This meant that all

01:24:25.800 --> 01:24:32.700
the other broken mannequins found with SCP
- 847 were likely once living humans, attacked

01:24:32.700 --> 01:24:38.160
and transformed by the anomaly, now a source
for new harvested body parts.

01:24:38.160 --> 01:24:44.640
Now safely interred at a Foundation containment
facility though, the real tests on SCP - 847

01:24:44.640 --> 01:24:48.120
to determine its behavior and physical attributes
could begin.

01:24:48.120 --> 01:24:54.720
The most important detail about SCP - 847
is that its aggression is exclusively directed

01:24:54.720 --> 01:25:00.900
towards women, as opposed to when it encounters
men and its instincts are more self-destructive.

01:25:00.900 --> 01:25:06.180
Through a series of tests and observations,
researchers have been able to pin down three

01:25:06.180 --> 01:25:10.620
different distinct patterns of behavior for
SCP - 847.

01:25:10.620 --> 01:25:15.795
Pattern Z behaviors occur when there are no
humans standing within fifty meters of SCP

01:25:15.795 --> 01:25:16.920
- 847.

01:25:16.920 --> 01:25:21.660
The mannequin will seek out a full length
mirror, and pose in front of it, much like

01:25:21.660 --> 01:25:24.540
a department store mannequin attempting to
show off its clothes.

01:25:24.540 --> 01:25:29.880
It remains largely inanimate during these
periods, and will very occasionally use a

01:25:29.880 --> 01:25:35.460
finger - or whatever appendage is available,
given its habit for self-mutilation - to scratch

01:25:35.460 --> 01:25:37.500
messages on nearby surfaces.

01:25:37.500 --> 01:25:43.200
Pattern Y behaviors occur when male humans
with XY chromosomes enter a fifty meter radius

01:25:43.200 --> 01:25:45.480
around SCP - 847.

01:25:45.480 --> 01:25:48.900
Just like its reaction to the male FBI agents&nbsp;

01:25:48.900 --> 01:25:52.200
who found it, 847 will&nbsp;
initially emit vocalizations

01:25:52.200 --> 01:25:57.840
that seem like whimpering gasps, before making
eye contact and striking provocative poses

01:25:57.840 --> 01:25:59.340
while approaching the subject.

01:25:59.340 --> 01:26:03.720
It will then remain static, and allow the
male subject to pose its body.

01:26:03.720 --> 01:26:08.880
However, after the male subject leaves the
area, 847 will enter a state of considerable

01:26:08.880 --> 01:26:12.960
distress, and begin removing or shattering
parts of its body.

01:26:12.960 --> 01:26:17.460
The Foundation has found that the parts removed
or shattered are often consistent with parts

01:26:17.460 --> 01:26:22.800
that the male subjects found displeasing during
interactions, showing a masochistic desire

01:26:22.800 --> 01:26:23.520
to impress.

01:26:23.520 --> 01:26:26.100
These parts are then harvested back from&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:26:26.100 --> 01:26:27.420
plastinated
victims.

01:26:27.420 --> 01:26:31.980
Which brings us to the most dangerous of its
behavior patterns.

01:26:31.980 --> 01:26:37.260
Pattern X behaviors occur when female humans
enter a 50 meter radius around the creature.

01:26:37.260 --> 01:26:43.140
847 will immediately become brutally aggressive,
switching its noises from whimpers to violent

01:26:43.140 --> 01:26:44.520
screeches and growls.

01:26:44.520 --> 01:26:47.940
847 also experiences enhanced&nbsp;
physical capabilities&nbsp;

01:26:47.940 --> 01:26:50.820
during Pattern X states - its speed has been

01:26:50.820 --> 01:26:57.360
measured at 45 kilometers per hour, making
it as fast as the legendary SCP - 096.

01:26:57.360 --> 01:27:01.140
It’s also been shown to exhibit extreme
physical strength.

01:27:01.140 --> 01:27:06.240
It’s during this pattern of behavior that
it begins excreting its deadly resin, which

01:27:06.240 --> 01:27:08.940
has been proven to only be dangerous to women.

01:27:08.940 --> 01:27:14.460
In these states, the only thing capable of
reliably pacifying the being is a powerful

01:27:14.460 --> 01:27:15.420
electric shock.

01:27:15.420 --> 01:27:20.520
The shock causes the creature’s resin to
harden, temporarily incapacitating it for

01:27:20.520 --> 01:27:21.540
roughly five minutes.

01:27:21.540 --> 01:27:28.140
Other conventional weapons and damage has
no meaningful effect on SCP - 847.

01:27:28.140 --> 01:27:33.480
After a number of incidents that had sad and
violent endings, the Foundation Ethics Committee

01:27:33.480 --> 01:27:38.580
forbade the use of female D-Class personnel
in SCP - 847 testing.

01:27:38.580 --> 01:27:44.100
When it came to female subjects, 847 always
slipped into a state of extreme aggression,

01:27:44.100 --> 01:27:49.380
so instead the Foundation began testing with
male subjects in hopes of better understanding

01:27:49.380 --> 01:27:54.060
the dynamics between human males and SCP-847.

01:27:54.060 --> 01:27:59.580
Various misogynistic D-Class males were introduced
into the containment chamber, which was modelled

01:27:59.580 --> 01:28:02.760
to look like a bedroom for the purposes of
behavioral study.

01:28:02.760 --> 01:28:09.360
Each one, either during or after their interaction
with SCP - 847, was told to comment on some

01:28:09.360 --> 01:28:11.100
aspect they felt dissatisfied with.

01:28:11.100 --> 01:28:16.080
The mannequin shattered its own chest after
hearing it described as being out of proportion.

01:28:16.080 --> 01:28:20.340
After another D-Class called its nose ugly,
the mannequin broke it off.

01:28:20.340 --> 01:28:25.140
After another said that its hair was out of
fashion and commented on its inability to

01:28:25.140 --> 01:28:28.080
drink, it tore out its hair and liver.

01:28:28.080 --> 01:28:31.320
All parts were replaced after the experiments.

01:28:31.320 --> 01:28:37.080
Things took their most violent and upsetting
turn yet with the introduction of D-7294.

01:28:37.080 --> 01:28:39.960
A lot of the time, D-Class&nbsp;
personnel are considered&nbsp;

01:28:39.960 --> 01:28:42.240
to be as anonymous as they are expendable.

01:28:42.240 --> 01:28:45.900
But D-7294 is an exception.

01:28:45.900 --> 01:28:51.000
Before becoming D-Class, he was a successful
cello teacher who brutally murdered one of

01:28:51.000 --> 01:28:52.620
his teenage students and her mother.

01:28:52.620 --> 01:28:57.300
He’s typically employed in tests when the
Foundation wishes to see interactions between

01:28:57.300 --> 01:29:01.320
anomalies and humans with confirmed psychopathic
personalities.

01:29:01.320 --> 01:29:07.140
During his interaction with SCP - 847, he
belittled and humiliated the mannequin.

01:29:07.140 --> 01:29:11.700
He forced it into uncomfortable poses, and
even snapped off one of its fingers before

01:29:11.700 --> 01:29:14.400
being dragged from the room by Foundation
guards.

01:29:14.400 --> 01:29:19.500
In the following debrief, he further berated
the mannequin as “useless” and “lousy”

01:29:19.500 --> 01:29:21.480
at its job of being controlled by him.

01:29:21.480 --> 01:29:29.160
In response, 847 extracted its own brains,
eyes, and clavicle before shattering its own

01:29:29.160 --> 01:29:30.720
hands in dismay.

01:29:30.720 --> 01:29:33.300
So why does SCP - 847 behave this way?

01:29:33.300 --> 01:29:39.000
While it may appear monstrous, it seems that
the reason SCP - 847 does what it does is

01:29:39.000 --> 01:29:45.000
all too human: It hurts women because it itself
is hurting, and it’s willing to hurt itself

01:29:45.000 --> 01:29:48.240
even more for the approval of the objects
of its desire.

01:29:48.240 --> 01:29:53.940
As a result, it’s an anomaly trapped in
an endless cycle of pain and violence.

01:29:53.940 --> 01:29:59.880
Perhaps one day it’ll be able to free itself
from the loop, but that day is unlikely to

01:29:59.880 --> 01:30:03.240
come for this murderous mannequin anytime
soon.

01:30:03.240 --> 01:30:08.580
London is the second largest city in Europe,
and underneath this bustling city is one of

01:30:08.580 --> 01:30:12.000
the oldest and largest networks of train tunnels
in the world.

01:30:12.000 --> 01:30:17.280
But that's not the only huge, old structure
located beneath the city of London.

01:30:17.280 --> 01:30:23.640
Below even the deepest underground metro stations
of this historic city, there's a whole artificial

01:30:23.640 --> 01:30:29.640
world of surveillance cyborgs, impossible
architecture, and stomach churning nutritional

01:30:29.640 --> 01:30:30.360
supplements.

01:30:30.360 --> 01:30:38.220
So be sure to mind the gap, because we're
about to take you on a tour of SCP-1678, also

01:30:38.220 --> 01:30:40.020
known as UnLondon.

01:30:40.020 --> 01:30:45.060
SCP-1678 is located one kilometer below the
city of London, England.

01:30:45.060 --> 01:30:51.060
From all appearances, it seems to be an exact
copy of the city, though aesthetically, it's

01:30:51.060 --> 01:30:54.600
more in line with how it was around the turn
of the 20th century.

01:30:54.600 --> 01:30:59.820
Gas streetlights stand on every corner, and
the modern skyscrapers of the business district

01:30:59.820 --> 01:31:03.180
are recreated in the style&nbsp;
of Victorian architecture.

01:31:03.180 --> 01:31:08.040
The epicenter of construction appears to be
the houses of parliament, which is evidenced

01:31:08.040 --> 01:31:12.840
by the more unfinished and flawed the city
becomes further out from the center one goes.

01:31:12.840 --> 01:31:18.000
Some of the buildings are made of nonsensical
materials like copper pipes, and some of the

01:31:18.000 --> 01:31:22.980
'gas lamps' are nothing more than a ball of
disembodied light floating atop a metal pole.

01:31:22.980 --> 01:31:28.380
The first big question that the Foundation
had upon discovering this location was, of

01:31:28.380 --> 01:31:31.020
course, why on earth was it created?

01:31:31.020 --> 01:31:36.360
And they wouldn’t have to look far, as an
explanation of this bizarre mirror city plays

01:31:36.360 --> 01:31:38.430
automatically upon entering -

01:31:38.430 --> 01:31:39.600
“My fellow citizen.

01:31:39.600 --> 01:31:43.440
If you are hearing this tape, then the world
as we knew it has finished.

01:31:43.440 --> 01:31:50.280
The sky has broken, the ground heaves with
the tramp of terrible feet, and all the horror

01:31:50.280 --> 01:31:55.740
and madness from the dark corners of the world
has broken free to exact its vengeance on

01:31:55.740 --> 01:31:56.880
the world of Man.

01:31:56.880 --> 01:32:03.960
Evil has raised its bloody flag upon all nations
of the world and crowed its unholy victory

01:32:03.960 --> 01:32:05.340
to the broken sky.

01:32:05.340 --> 01:32:08.100
Yes, this is the end.

01:32:08.100 --> 01:32:10.380
But there is a new hope.

01:32:10.380 --> 01:32:15.000
Welcome to UnLondon, a city of the survivors,
a city of the free.

01:32:15.000 --> 01:32:20.640
Together, fellow citizen, we will wait and
prepare for the new beginning, the grand new

01:32:20.640 --> 01:32:22.320
world that is soon to come.

01:32:22.320 --> 01:32:24.180
Let the world above burn.

01:32:24.180 --> 01:32:25.860
We will endure.

01:32:25.860 --> 01:32:27.960
Let the monsters have their world.

01:32:27.960 --> 01:32:29.700
We will prepare.

01:32:29.700 --> 01:32:31.260
We will wait.

01:32:31.260 --> 01:32:34.920
And I tell you, citizen, that there will be
a new morning.

01:32:34.920 --> 01:32:38.940
And you will emerge from UnLondon, and stand
blinking in the sun.

01:32:38.940 --> 01:32:44.580
And on that day, citizen, there shall be a
new order, as we raise the Union Flag over

01:32:44.580 --> 01:32:45.720
the entire world.

01:32:45.720 --> 01:32:49.140
I welcome you to UnLondon, the Last City.

01:32:49.140 --> 01:32:50.640
And the first.”

01:32:50.640 --> 01:32:56.220
From this message, it seems that this mirror
city was built to be a refuge for survivors

01:32:56.220 --> 01:33:01.440
of an apocalyptic scenario, but the SCP Foundation
had no knowledge of such a plan.

01:33:01.440 --> 01:33:06.180
In fact, it's still unknown who created this
place, or how they did it.

01:33:06.180 --> 01:33:11.160
The one fact that was evident to the Foundation
was that even though this strange place was

01:33:11.160 --> 01:33:16.080
intended to be a safe haven, it was far too
poorly constructed to actually act as one.

01:33:16.080 --> 01:33:21.180
Illumination was unreliable, and most of the
buildings were damp and infested with mold.

01:33:21.180 --> 01:33:26.220
It's also unclear to the Foundation where
the oxygen and gas supply of UnLondon was

01:33:26.220 --> 01:33:26.700
coming from.

01:33:26.700 --> 01:33:32.220
Throughout the day, the loudspeakers around
UnLondon play automated messages such as “No

01:33:32.220 --> 01:33:36.780
one is safe from the influence of memetic
beings.”, “Bryson’s Home for the Poor

01:33:36.780 --> 01:33:42.600
is here to help.” and “Crime will not
be tolerated in UnLondon...The tormentors

01:33:42.600 --> 01:33:45.000
of society will become its defenders.”

01:33:45.000 --> 01:33:51.120
At the end of every hour that passes, the
speakers announce the time, followed by “...and

01:33:51.120 --> 01:33:52.200
all is well”.

01:33:52.200 --> 01:33:57.960
When the SCP Foundation first entered UnLondon,
it was unknown whether or not any living things

01:33:57.960 --> 01:33:59.100
inhabited the city.

01:33:59.100 --> 01:34:04.260
On first investigation, it seemed from its
state of disrepair that the city had been

01:34:04.260 --> 01:34:05.220
long abandoned.

01:34:05.220 --> 01:34:10.200
But soon the foundation met their first inhabitant
of the underground city.

01:34:10.200 --> 01:34:14.940
Mobile Task Force members were inspecting
the area around the houses of parliament when

01:34:14.940 --> 01:34:16.560
they discovered what looked to be a bank.

01:34:16.560 --> 01:34:18.900
As they approached the doors, they heard the&nbsp;

01:34:18.900 --> 01:34:21.060
following announcement over&nbsp;
the nearby loudspeakers:

01:34:21.060 --> 01:34:24.240
“Citizen, you are entering a restricted
area.

01:34:24.240 --> 01:34:26.460
Have your authorization papers ready.

01:34:26.460 --> 01:34:29.160
A Bobby will arrive to escort you shortly.”

01:34:29.160 --> 01:34:35.820
This signaled the approach of SCP-1678-A,
also known as 'the bobbies'.

01:34:35.820 --> 01:34:42.180
A single instance of SCP-1678-A appeared with
the unmistakable sound of a police whistle,

01:34:42.180 --> 01:34:46.200
and as soon as it arrived it started attacking
the members of the task force.

01:34:46.200 --> 01:34:49.020
Another announcement came over the speakers-
‘‘Police!

01:34:49.020 --> 01:34:50.520
Halt, criminal!’’

01:34:50.520 --> 01:34:55.320
The bobbies are the main threat to visitors
in UnLondon, and they will attack on sight

01:34:55.320 --> 01:34:57.480
with any improvised weapon they can find.

01:34:57.480 --> 01:35:02.880
True to their name, they are all dressed in
uniforms consistent with those of London city

01:35:02.880 --> 01:35:05.400
police officers from the Victorian era.

01:35:05.400 --> 01:35:09.420
What sets them apart from their historical
counterparts, is their construction.

01:35:09.420 --> 01:35:16.020
These beings are made out of human corpses,
crudely dismembered at the joints and re-assembled

01:35:16.020 --> 01:35:19.860
using metal hinges and bolts, with their heads
wrapped in bandages.

01:35:19.860 --> 01:35:25.380
Bobbies are extremely hard to kill, with only
high-caliber rounds and explosive weapons

01:35:25.380 --> 01:35:27.180
being effective at putting them down.

01:35:27.180 --> 01:35:32.280
Autopsies of dead bobbies have shown that
underneath the police uniform, the bobbies

01:35:32.280 --> 01:35:34.560
all wear prison inmate-style jumpsuits.

01:35:34.560 --> 01:35:40.020
This adds a chilling context to the announcement
about 'the tormentors of society becoming

01:35:40.020 --> 01:35:45.480
its defenders'- it appears that the bobbies
are the reanimated bodies of prisoners.

01:35:45.480 --> 01:35:50.220
In addition to the bobbies, the Foundation
cataloged two additional forms of artificial

01:35:50.220 --> 01:35:52.020
life present within UnLondon.

01:35:52.020 --> 01:35:59.580
First are SCP-1678-B, or Eyes in the Sky,
hybrid bio-mechanical birds made of flesh

01:35:59.580 --> 01:36:01.680
with an exoskeleton of copper wiring.

01:36:01.680 --> 01:36:04.440
Some of these creatures are&nbsp;
covered in a deteriorating&nbsp;

01:36:04.440 --> 01:36:07.500
outer layer of plastic and feathers, suggesting

01:36:07.500 --> 01:36:09.900
that they were originally meant to resemble
pigeons.

01:36:09.900 --> 01:36:15.540
As their name suggests, eyes in the sky serve
as a type of surveillance drone, and while

01:36:15.540 --> 01:36:20.460
they have no offensive capabilities, they
still pose a significant threat to the Foundation.

01:36:20.460 --> 01:36:25.440
It's still unclear whether they're able to
communicate with or summon the bobbies, but

01:36:25.440 --> 01:36:28.200
the SCP takes no chances.

01:36:28.200 --> 01:36:32.220
The last 'life form' present in SCP-1678 is&nbsp;

01:36:32.220 --> 01:36:37.020
the strangest and the most&nbsp;
frightening - SCP-1678-C,

01:36:37.020 --> 01:36:39.240
known as the wretch.

01:36:39.240 --> 01:36:44.460
The wretch has only ever been encountered
outside the zone which is now under SCP Foundation

01:36:44.460 --> 01:36:48.480
control, and it's uncertain how many instances
of this being exist.

01:36:48.480 --> 01:36:53.640
The wretch resembles an old woman, or sometimes
old man, dressed in filthy rags.

01:36:53.640 --> 01:36:58.200
The wretch sits at street corners holding
a begging tray, and will attempt to elicit

01:36:58.200 --> 01:37:00.840
pity from anyone who happens to walk by.

01:37:00.840 --> 01:37:06.060
The wretch will ask for food or money, but
if food is supplied, it will start weeping

01:37:06.060 --> 01:37:08.460
before vanishing into a puff of black smoke.

01:37:08.460 --> 01:37:13.500
On a few occasions, audio notices playing
on the city's loudspeakers have alluded to

01:37:13.500 --> 01:37:16.020
this being, saying “Do not pity the Wretch.

01:37:16.020 --> 01:37:19.980
Allow them to pay the price of their betrayal
for all eternity.”

01:37:19.980 --> 01:37:25.140
The current Foundation protocol with regards
to the wretch… is to not engage with it

01:37:25.140 --> 01:37:25.500
at all.

01:37:25.500 --> 01:37:30.600
In addition to the bobbies, the eyes in the
sky, and the wretches, there's another strange

01:37:30.600 --> 01:37:32.820
component to the world of UnLondon.

01:37:32.820 --> 01:37:38.160
Throughout the city, in any area designed
for human habitation, the Foundation discovered

01:37:38.160 --> 01:37:40.920
multiple machines that resembled modern gas
pumps.

01:37:40.920 --> 01:37:46.380
These machines are fitted with coin slots
and rubber hoses that, when coins are inserted,

01:37:46.380 --> 01:37:51.120
dispense a porridge-like substance advertised
as 'Dr. Goody's Wonderfood'.

01:37:51.120 --> 01:37:56.640
According to posters around the city, Wonderfood
is a meal replacement supplement, supposedly

01:37:56.640 --> 01:37:59.280
containing all of the required nutrients for
survival.

01:37:59.280 --> 01:38:04.020
Wonderfood also appears to be the only food
source available in UnLondon.

01:38:04.020 --> 01:38:08.760
Despite the claims by various posters around
the city that Wonderfood ‘Contains all the

01:38:08.760 --> 01:38:13.560
nutrients you need!’ and ‘Completely restores
health and vitality!’examination of the

01:38:13.560 --> 01:38:18.960
substance has revealed that it is, much like
the rest of UnLondon, unsuitable for sustaining

01:38:18.960 --> 01:38:19.140
life.

01:38:19.140 --> 01:38:23.700
Tests have confirmed that Wonderfood is a
synthetic starch gel heavily enriched with

01:38:23.700 --> 01:38:29.340
various minerals, vitamins, fats and bulking
agents, and it contains artificially engineered

01:38:29.340 --> 01:38:30.780
DNA helix structures.

01:38:30.780 --> 01:38:35.700
While it does contain all the elements required
for short-term survival, consuming the product

01:38:35.700 --> 01:38:40.860
for longer than 6 weeks will result in severe
malnutrition and eventually scurvy.

01:38:40.860 --> 01:38:44.940
Further tests have shown that Wonderfood also
contains certain psychoactive properties.

01:38:44.940 --> 01:38:49.800
The porridge contains a mixture of unknown
molecular compounds which, through regular

01:38:49.800 --> 01:38:55.020
consumption, make subjects calmer, less anxious,
and less likely to resist authority.

01:38:55.020 --> 01:38:59.760
It also seems to have been engineered to cause
withdrawal symptoms that set in if a person

01:38:59.760 --> 01:39:03.240
stops eating it, symptoms which include headaches
and depression.

01:39:03.240 --> 01:39:08.280
Foundation personnel are forbidden to consume
Wonderfood, but the substance is highly attractive

01:39:08.280 --> 01:39:13.680
to instances of SCP-1678-B and 1678-C.

01:39:13.680 --> 01:39:19.080
Like most things in UnLondon, the quality
of Wonderfood varies wildly, with some dispensers

01:39:19.080 --> 01:39:23.880
putting out a product that is so degraded
that it can cause sickness, deformities, or

01:39:23.880 --> 01:39:25.260
even death in the consumer.

01:39:25.260 --> 01:39:30.720
But strangely, the Foundation has also recorded
a type of unknown colorful mollusk which feeds

01:39:30.720 --> 01:39:33.060
on spillage from the Wonderfood dispensers.

01:39:33.060 --> 01:39:36.420
At present, UnLondon is only partially contained.

01:39:36.420 --> 01:39:41.880
Mobile Task Forces Tau-4 and Epsilon-6 have
succeeded in establishing a perimeter around

01:39:41.880 --> 01:39:48.660
the Hyde Park district where they have managed
to stop any incursion from SCP-1678-A. Even

01:39:48.660 --> 01:39:53.280
though this is the only area that is fully
under Foundation control, explorations have

01:39:53.280 --> 01:39:55.920
been conducted of buildings&nbsp;
outside that perimeter.

01:39:55.920 --> 01:40:00.660
The investigations are vital for the Foundation's
main purpose in UnLondon, which is figuring

01:40:00.660 --> 01:40:05.580
out who built it, and exactly what kind of
event this underground mirror city was meant

01:40:05.580 --> 01:40:06.300
to prepare for.

01:40:06.300 --> 01:40:11.580
The interior of the Natural History Museum
yielded particularly strange insights into

01:40:11.580 --> 01:40:12.900
the purpose of UnLondon.

01:40:12.900 --> 01:40:17.760
For the most part, the museum is close to
how it appears in the above ground, but with

01:40:17.760 --> 01:40:18.840
one key difference.

01:40:18.840 --> 01:40:24.600
The task force investigating the museum discovered
an exhibit called 'The Fall of Man', exactly

01:40:24.600 --> 01:40:26.160
where the Darwin Wing should have been.

01:40:26.160 --> 01:40:29.520
The exhibit, as its name suggests, details&nbsp;

01:40:29.520 --> 01:40:31.860
the apocalyptic scenario&nbsp;
that would've theoretically

01:40:31.860 --> 01:40:34.560
driven people underground into UnLondon.

01:40:34.560 --> 01:40:40.380
But, to everyone’s surprise, its dioramas
and displays didn't depict an asteroid impact,

01:40:40.380 --> 01:40:42.720
plague, or nuclear armageddon.

01:40:42.720 --> 01:40:47.520
To the Foundation task force members, the
scenes of destruction depicted in the exhibit

01:40:47.520 --> 01:40:49.020
were far more familiar.

01:40:49.020 --> 01:40:55.020
They recognized the reptilian form of SCP-682,
the ordinary-looking brownstone basement door

01:40:55.020 --> 01:41:02.280
that serves as a gateway to SCP-2317, and,
most chillingly, the imposing many-eyed figure

01:41:02.280 --> 01:41:03.780
of the Scarlet King.

01:41:03.780 --> 01:41:08.700
These were only some of the known Keter class
SCPs depicted in the museum exhibit.

01:41:08.700 --> 01:41:14.220
It was clear that even though the SCP Foundation
hadn't built this city, whoever did knew a

01:41:14.220 --> 01:41:16.440
lot about the SCP Foundation's activities.

01:41:16.440 --> 01:41:21.720
It's believed by the Foundation that whoever
or whatever created UnLondon still resides

01:41:21.720 --> 01:41:26.340
in the houses of parliament, and the ultimate
goal of the task forces is to infiltrate the

01:41:26.340 --> 01:41:26.520
building.

01:41:26.520 --> 01:41:31.020
But in order to do that, they will first need
to find where the bobbies are made and halt

01:41:31.020 --> 01:41:31.800
their production.

01:41:31.800 --> 01:41:36.540
It's believed that Bryson's Home for the Poor
is where they originate from, but it's unclear

01:41:36.540 --> 01:41:41.700
exactly where the materials to make them come
from, nor is it clear just how they're produced.

01:41:41.700 --> 01:41:47.340
Ultimately, the Foundation's goal is to catalog
the entire city, and, once they have stopped

01:41:47.340 --> 01:41:52.740
the production of more bobbies, MTF Tau-4
and Epsilon-6 will storm the houses of parliament

01:41:52.740 --> 01:41:55.560
and contain whatever force has created UnLondon.

01:41:55.560 --> 01:42:00.660
But, London is a very big city, and UnLondon
is just as big.

01:42:00.660 --> 01:42:05.640
So, there's no telling what else they might
find exploring this bizarre location.

01:42:05.640 --> 01:42:10.440
Have you ever had a nightmare that you’re
running down a long, dark hallway, getting

01:42:10.440 --> 01:42:12.300
chased by something you can’t see?

01:42:12.300 --> 01:42:15.780
The thing behind you isn’t fast, but that
doesn’t matter.

01:42:15.780 --> 01:42:19.020
You can’t run forever, and the thing knows
it.

01:42:19.020 --> 01:42:21.060
It is a patient predator.

01:42:21.060 --> 01:42:23.040
It toys with its food.

01:42:23.040 --> 01:42:25.860
At first, you move with speed and rhythm.

01:42:25.860 --> 01:42:28.740
The metallic scraping noise behind you grows
quieter.

01:42:28.740 --> 01:42:31.020
You run and stumble through the dark.

01:42:31.020 --> 01:42:33.600
Your muscles start to ache and your lungs
burn.

01:42:33.600 --> 01:42:35.100
Your pace slows.

01:42:35.100 --> 01:42:36.600
It’s still coming.

01:42:36.600 --> 01:42:38.760
You can hear the scraping getting louder.

01:42:38.760 --> 01:42:40.140
You start to panic.

01:42:40.140 --> 01:42:41.280
It’s completely dark.

01:42:41.280 --> 01:42:44.520
You don’t know where you’re running or
even what you’re running from.

01:42:44.520 --> 01:42:49.920
All you know - as you bump against the walls
and the sharp corners that rush towards you

01:42:49.920 --> 01:42:52.440
- is that you can’t run forever.

01:42:52.440 --> 01:42:57.720
You trip, fall, and pain explodes through
your leg as your knee shatters on the concrete

01:42:57.720 --> 01:42:57.960
ground.

01:42:57.960 --> 01:43:00.420
That scraping is getting louder.

01:43:00.420 --> 01:43:02.160
You can barely breathe.

01:43:02.160 --> 01:43:04.440
You can’t run anymore with your injury.

01:43:04.440 --> 01:43:06.900
There’s no way to stop what’s coming.

01:43:06.900 --> 01:43:09.240
There is no escape.

01:43:09.240 --> 01:43:11.340
The scraping is right behind you.

01:43:11.340 --> 01:43:12.540
You scream.

01:43:12.540 --> 01:43:14.580
And then… you wake up.

01:43:14.580 --> 01:43:19.080
Your heart is pounding like thunder in your
chest and your sheets are soaked with sweat,

01:43:19.080 --> 01:43:19.980
but you’re safe.

01:43:19.980 --> 01:43:23.160
You’re out of those awful, dark hallways.

01:43:23.160 --> 01:43:25.380
But what if this wasn’t just a nightmare?

01:43:25.380 --> 01:43:30.360
What if this scenario was real, and there
was no escape from the horror chasing you

01:43:30.360 --> 01:43:30.900
in the darkness?

01:43:31.440 --> 01:43:37.440
That’s what it’s like to have a close
encounter with SCP-1918, a sadistic, sentient

01:43:37.440 --> 01:43:40.920
object that loves playing twisted games with
its prey.

01:43:40.920 --> 01:43:47.220
But this monster never plays fair, and even
worse, it’s always just a simple door away.

01:43:47.220 --> 01:43:53.640
It might even be hiding behind a door near
you, right now, waiting to start a game with

01:43:53.640 --> 01:43:54.840
its new playmate.

01:43:54.840 --> 01:44:01.020
But soon you’ll understand why some doors
should never, ever be opened, and why some

01:44:01.020 --> 01:44:03.300
games are better left unplayed.

01:44:03.300 --> 01:44:09.720
x
SCP - 1918 is an anomaly with two parts: SCP-1918

01:44:09.720 --> 01:44:15.300
itself, and SCP-1918-2, the monster’s underground
lair.

01:44:15.300 --> 01:44:22.500
The duo are a match made in hell, as the chambers
and hallways of 1918-2 are perfectly tailored

01:44:22.500 --> 01:44:24.780
to 1918’s violent hobbies.

01:44:24.780 --> 01:44:30.480
Nobody knows how long this anomaly has been
operating, but it’s probably behind countless

01:44:30.480 --> 01:44:31.260
disappearances.

01:44:31.800 --> 01:44:36.540
After all, 1918 has a habit of breaking its
toys...

01:44:36.540 --> 01:44:42.420
The nightmare began in a small town in Maine,
with a population of only 226 people.

01:44:42.420 --> 01:44:45.720
But that population was about to get lower.

01:44:45.720 --> 01:44:51.480
People in the town began to report strange
noises at night, a droning, metal-on-concrete

01:44:51.480 --> 01:44:55.140
scraping noise, like someone dragging a lead
pipe along the ground.

01:44:55.140 --> 01:44:57.420
At first, people just ignored the sound.

01:44:57.420 --> 01:45:02.220
It was all in their heads, or maybe just a
faulty oven or a washing machine on the fritz.

01:45:02.220 --> 01:45:07.260
Anything that would allow them to forget about
the noise and get on with their daily lives.

01:45:07.260 --> 01:45:10.140
But the noises were coming from below.

01:45:10.140 --> 01:45:15.360
They could be heard out on the streets, most
audibly near manholes and sewer grates.

01:45:15.360 --> 01:45:18.000
People started feeling unsafe in their homes.

01:45:18.000 --> 01:45:20.880
The noises were spooking animals and children.

01:45:20.880 --> 01:45:22.560
People were losing sleep.

01:45:22.560 --> 01:45:27.180
That scraping they all tried to ignore was
beginning to get to them all.

01:45:27.180 --> 01:45:31.740
Letters, emails, and angry phone calls to
the town council were piling up.

01:45:31.740 --> 01:45:35.880
Something had to be done before the whole
town went crazy with fear.

01:45:35.880 --> 01:45:40.320
The mayor authorized four utility workers
to investigate the source of the noise at

01:45:40.320 --> 01:45:42.000
a local sewage treatment facility.

01:45:42.000 --> 01:45:46.620
Considering the scraping was loudest near
the sewer grates, everyone just assumed that

01:45:46.620 --> 01:45:49.680
whatever was causing all this must be connected
to the sewers.

01:45:49.680 --> 01:45:55.080
Four utility workers were sent to investigate
the facility, only to find that the machinery

01:45:55.080 --> 01:45:56.880
on site was working just fine.

01:45:56.880 --> 01:46:01.680
The source of the problems must have been
coming directly from the underground sewer-lines

01:46:01.680 --> 01:46:02.340
themselves.

01:46:02.340 --> 01:46:07.380
The four workers, equipped with headlamps,
descended into a long service tunnel that

01:46:07.380 --> 01:46:08.820
fed into the sewer system.

01:46:08.820 --> 01:46:13.560
As they passed deeper into the tunnel, the
darkness around them became thicker.

01:46:13.560 --> 01:46:18.720
It was a tangible presence that drowned out
the light of their headlamps, similar to the

01:46:18.720 --> 01:46:22.140
anomalous phenomenon exhibited by SCP - 087.

01:46:22.140 --> 01:46:28.260
When the utility workers tried to turn back,
they discovered another impossibility: It

01:46:28.260 --> 01:46:32.580
seemed that the tunnel behind them had become
a solid concrete wall.

01:46:32.580 --> 01:46:34.560
They were trapped, but where?

01:46:34.560 --> 01:46:36.060
It was too dark to tell.

01:46:36.060 --> 01:46:40.860
Confused and terrified, the four men stuck
together, attempting to find a way out.

01:46:40.860 --> 01:46:45.840
It was too dark to see their hand in front
of their face, so all they could do was navigate

01:46:45.840 --> 01:46:48.540
slowly by feeling the walls around them.

01:46:48.540 --> 01:46:51.360
These walls felt oddly...crusty.

01:46:51.360 --> 01:46:56.820
There was a kind of faint, metallic stench
hanging in the air, too, like old blood.

01:46:56.820 --> 01:47:02.100
Something horrible had happened here, and
something horrible was about to happen again.

01:47:02.100 --> 01:47:05.820
All they could do was keep moving and try
to stay calm.

01:47:05.820 --> 01:47:10.620
Eventually, after hours of pawing at walls
in the dark, they found an open doorway.

01:47:10.620 --> 01:47:16.500
One by one, they filed inside, only to feel
blinded when bright, white ceiling lights

01:47:16.500 --> 01:47:17.820
suddenly switched on.

01:47:17.820 --> 01:47:24.120
The room was all white, and filled with pipes,
large and small, running from wall to wall.

01:47:24.120 --> 01:47:28.980
Just then one of the utility workers let out
an ear-splitting scream and pointed towards

01:47:28.980 --> 01:47:29.520
the doorway.

01:47:29.520 --> 01:47:32.220
His colleagues turned, and gasped in shock.

01:47:32.220 --> 01:47:36.540
There was something outside the door, and
it was staring at them.

01:47:36.540 --> 01:47:39.240
The object filled up almost the entire doorway.

01:47:39.240 --> 01:47:44.700
It seemed like a demonic hobby horse, made
from a black-and-white, candy-striped metal

01:47:44.700 --> 01:47:47.280
pole with a crude plastic head on top.

01:47:47.280 --> 01:47:53.400
The head looked like a clown’s, with a wide,
toothy grin, but no visible eyes.

01:47:53.400 --> 01:47:56.940
It was SCP-1918.

01:47:56.940 --> 01:48:02.160
The utility workers were frozen as the object
leaned forward slightly, and slithered into

01:48:02.160 --> 01:48:05.580
the room, the bottom of the metal pipe scraping
against the ground.

01:48:05.580 --> 01:48:11.280
It was the exact same scraping noise that’d
been haunting the concerned townsfolk up above.

01:48:11.280 --> 01:48:13.860
This was the thing behind it all.

01:48:13.860 --> 01:48:21.420
And as the object moved, its metal pole started
to scrape words into the ground: Tik Tak Tow

01:48:21.420 --> 01:48:24.600
None of the four utility workers were ever
seen again.

01:48:24.600 --> 01:48:29.880
It didn’t take long for the SCP Foundation
to descend upon this quiet Maine town and

01:48:29.880 --> 01:48:30.780
pick up the pieces.

01:48:30.780 --> 01:48:33.720
All relevant officials were provided amnestics,&nbsp;

01:48:33.720 --> 01:48:36.120
and cover stories were&nbsp;
created for the disappearances

01:48:36.120 --> 01:48:37.860
of the four utility workers.

01:48:37.860 --> 01:48:42.240
The Foundation also commandeered the sewage
treatment facility that held the entrance

01:48:42.240 --> 01:48:48.960
to SCP-1918-2, replacing all key roles at
the facility with undercover Foundation personnel.

01:48:48.960 --> 01:48:55.080
SCP-1918 was given a Euclid' classification
due to the fixed nature of its hunting grounds,

01:48:55.080 --> 01:48:57.720
and then the real research began.

01:48:57.720 --> 01:49:00.840
The Foundation soon made&nbsp;
some disturbing discoveries.

01:49:00.840 --> 01:49:06.720
Entrances into the SCP-1918-2 area didn’t
follow any kind of logic.

01:49:06.720 --> 01:49:13.200
The hunting ground of SCP-1918 can be entered
from almost any location, if you’re unlucky

01:49:13.200 --> 01:49:13.500
enough.

01:49:13.500 --> 01:49:19.260
There are currently 9 known entrances, including
5 sewage grates, 3 utility shafts located

01:49:19.260 --> 01:49:22.020
in a sewage facility, and 1 toilet.

01:49:22.020 --> 01:49:25.200
And these are just the ones the Foundation
knows about.

01:49:25.200 --> 01:49:30.120
There are a huge number of&nbsp;
ways to enter SCP-1918-2,&nbsp;

01:49:30.120 --> 01:49:33.360
but to this day, nothing has ever been able

01:49:33.360 --> 01:49:33.960
to leave.

01:49:33.960 --> 01:49:39.840
SCP-1918-2 is contained twenty meters below
the streets of this unassuming Maine town.

01:49:39.840 --> 01:49:44.880
Personnel, aside from Foundation-approved
D-class guinea pigs. are refused entrance.

01:49:44.880 --> 01:49:51.720
Researchers have mapped out the layout of
1918-2 through seismic imaging of SCP-1918’s

01:49:51.720 --> 01:49:52.380
movements.

01:49:52.380 --> 01:49:58.860
There are 18 identical room pairs in SCP-1918-2,
or 9 compound rooms.

01:49:58.860 --> 01:50:04.440
Rooms are differentiated between a '1' room
and a '2' room by crude carvings on the floors

01:50:04.440 --> 01:50:06.420
outside of the individual rooms.

01:50:06.420 --> 01:50:12.900
SCP-1918-2 is symmetrical, with half a meter
wide paths circling each compound room.

01:50:12.900 --> 01:50:17.700
The only deviations to this construction are
the location of entrances on the sides of

01:50:17.700 --> 01:50:22.020
each individual room, which vary randomly
while the location is “active.”

01:50:22.020 --> 01:50:26.700
What exactly does SCP-1918 do in this private
little maze?

01:50:26.700 --> 01:50:28.500
It plays games, of course.

01:50:28.500 --> 01:50:34.560
Its two favorites - as indicated by the words
it scrapes onto the ground - are “Tik Tak

01:50:34.560 --> 01:50:36.840
Tow” and “Memoree”

01:50:36.840 --> 01:50:43.440
In Tik Tak Tow, 1918 moves to each “1”
room, leaving behind "X" markings on the floors

01:50:43.440 --> 01:50:48.140
if the room is not already marked with an
"O" in a manner similar to a game of "Tic

01:50:48.140 --> 01:50:48.780
Tac Toe''.

01:50:48.780 --> 01:50:53.820
How a victim is meant to accomplish making
a mark or understand this process is unknown,

01:50:53.820 --> 01:50:55.620
as no aides are given.

01:50:55.620 --> 01:51:01.020
Blood is commonly used by victims to make
their markings, hence the rusty smell in many

01:51:01.020 --> 01:51:01.680
of the rooms.

01:51:01.680 --> 01:51:07.740
In Memoree, the trapped victim is rendered
unconscious by blunt force, presumably from

01:51:07.740 --> 01:51:09.000
SCP-1918.

01:51:09.000 --> 01:51:13.020
The subject regains consciousness in a random
section of the facility.

01:51:13.020 --> 01:51:17.040
Success is marked by finding a “1” room
identical to the central room.

01:51:17.040 --> 01:51:23.160
This event seems to possess a time limit,
as the subject is pursued by SCP-1918 throughout

01:51:23.160 --> 01:51:24.480
the halls of the facility.

01:51:24.480 --> 01:51:28.740
The subject "wins'' by marking the correct
room with an "O".

01:51:28.740 --> 01:51:32.280
What happens if you win or lose these games?

01:51:32.280 --> 01:51:38.160
It’s important to note that SCP-1918 is
very competitive, and doesn’t play fair.

01:51:38.160 --> 01:51:42.780
If you win, the object will merely accuse
you of cheating, and start a new game.

01:51:42.780 --> 01:51:46.500
This will happen again and&nbsp;
again, until eventually…&nbsp;

01:51:46.500 --> 01:51:48.000
you lose.

01:51:48.000 --> 01:51:49.320
And when you do?

01:51:49.320 --> 01:51:56.400
Well, take the horrifying encounter D-Class
personnel member D-2934 had with SCP-1918.

01:51:56.400 --> 01:52:04.200
Wearing video and audio equipment, D-2934
was led into SCP-1918-2 by Foundation researchers.

01:52:04.200 --> 01:52:09.860
When he eventually found his way to the central
room, 1918 challenged him to a game of Tik

01:52:09.860 --> 01:52:10.500
Tak Tow.

01:52:10.500 --> 01:52:15.000
And, against all odds, D-2934 won the game.

01:52:15.000 --> 01:52:17.880
But 1918 didn’t take kindly to that.

01:52:17.880 --> 01:52:23.820
It accused D-2934 of cheating, carving its
accusations into the ground before challenging

01:52:23.820 --> 01:52:25.860
him to a deadly game of Memoree.

01:52:25.860 --> 01:52:31.800
After hours of chasing, D-2934 eventually
lost his mind and was backed into a corner

01:52:31.800 --> 01:52:33.060
by 1918.

01:52:33.060 --> 01:52:38.100
As the object made its way towards him, he
panicked, ripped a pipe from the wall, and

01:52:38.100 --> 01:52:40.260
began smashing 1918’s head.

01:52:40.260 --> 01:52:44.760
As the plastic cracked under the force of
the blows, Foundation scientists could see

01:52:44.760 --> 01:52:46.020
real brains inside.

01:52:46.020 --> 01:52:50.400
D-2934 screamed, and the video feed cut off.

01:52:50.400 --> 01:52:55.920
When the video turned back on some time later,
1918 stared into the camera with a different

01:52:55.920 --> 01:52:58.080
head mounted atop its metal pole.

01:52:58.080 --> 01:53:04.560
One that, just a few hours earlier, had belonged
to the unfortunate D-2934.

01:53:04.560 --> 01:53:09.360
If there’s one lesson to be learned from
this terrifying anomaly, it’s that there

01:53:09.360 --> 01:53:14.280
truly is no escape from SCP-1918.

01:53:14.280 --> 01:53:20.460
You’re on a road trip - the kind that stretches
over days on end, and you need to make multiple

01:53:20.460 --> 01:53:23.700
stops along the way to refuel the car and
yourself.

01:53:23.700 --> 01:53:28.800
The last time you remember stopping to get
more gas and a bite to eat was back in Wyoming,

01:53:28.800 --> 01:53:30.780
and now, you’re in the heart of Montana.

01:53:30.780 --> 01:53:36.120
Thankfully, like an oasis in the desert, you
see the town of Clear Water off in the distance.

01:53:36.120 --> 01:53:42.120
It’s a vibrant, welcoming little place,
a perfect slice of classic, small-town Americana.

01:53:42.120 --> 01:53:46.800
You took a similar trip last year, and vaguely
remembered stopping at Clear Water that time

01:53:46.800 --> 01:53:48.780
too and you’re glad to be back.

01:53:48.780 --> 01:53:53.880
In particular, you remember the Old Prairie
Diner, a folksy little place with the most

01:53:53.880 --> 01:53:56.340
delicious Huckleberry Pie you ever tasted.

01:53:56.340 --> 01:53:59.460
Perhaps it’s about time for you to give
it another try.

01:53:59.460 --> 01:54:01.980
You fill up your tank and stop at the diner.

01:54:01.980 --> 01:54:08.040
The food tastes just as good as you remember,
but one thing is off: The entire staff seems

01:54:08.040 --> 01:54:08.820
to have changed.

01:54:08.820 --> 01:54:13.860
It’s the exact same diner you ate in a year
ago, no doubt about that, but it looks like

01:54:13.860 --> 01:54:18.420
everyone from the wait staff to the cashier
to the cooks have all been replaced.

01:54:18.420 --> 01:54:23.220
You try your best not to think about it, after
all, businesses are allowed to replace their

01:54:23.220 --> 01:54:28.860
staff, but the longer you sit in the diner,
the more uncomfortable the feelings become.

01:54:28.860 --> 01:54:33.240
You need to ask someone, just to push away
the fears that you’re going crazy.

01:54:33.240 --> 01:54:37.800
When a waiter passes by, you compliment the
food, and mention that you ate here last year

01:54:37.800 --> 01:54:38.040
too.

01:54:38.040 --> 01:54:41.460
You ask the unfamiliar waiter if they had
worked here back then.

01:54:41.460 --> 01:54:46.080
They confirm that, yes, they’ve always worked
here - and so has everybody else.

01:54:46.080 --> 01:54:48.360
The diner is a family business.

01:54:48.360 --> 01:54:54.060
You leave town not too long after that, feeling
vaguely unsettled, and as a voice on the radio

01:54:54.060 --> 01:54:58.740
warns about the incoming rain, you tell yourself
that you never want to return to the town

01:54:58.740 --> 01:55:00.000
of Clear Water, Montana.

01:55:00.000 --> 01:55:05.820
As you leave, the memory of the town seems
to fade from your mind in real time, but little

01:55:05.820 --> 01:55:10.140
do you know, the people of Clear Water will
never be able to leave.

01:55:10.140 --> 01:55:10.920
Ever.

01:55:10.920 --> 01:55:16.440
It’s because something horrifying will happen
in Clear Water every single year, and that

01:55:16.440 --> 01:55:21.060
thing is known to the SCP Foundation as SCP-3300.

01:55:21.060 --> 01:55:27.240
This annual anomalous event is Clear Water’s
own local curse, always occurring around mid-June.

01:55:27.240 --> 01:55:31.320
While many of the mechanics of this event
still elude the Foundation’s understanding,

01:55:31.320 --> 01:55:36.840
the outcome is well-documented: Every single
inhabitant of the town is replaced by a person

01:55:36.840 --> 01:55:38.820
who didn’t previously exist.

01:55:38.820 --> 01:55:44.160
While some elements may carry over from their
original counterparts, every person involved

01:55:44.160 --> 01:55:49.800
will simply be a whole new person, with no
memories of the change or who they once were.

01:55:49.800 --> 01:55:56.100
The process known as SCP-3300 lasts between
six and eighteen days, and once the process

01:55:56.100 --> 01:55:59.400
has begun, it’s impossible for any outsiders
to intervene.

01:55:59.400 --> 01:56:05.820
It begins with rain - a light, dreary drizzle
at first, but each day, the rain gets worse.

01:56:05.820 --> 01:56:09.120
Soon, it’s a storm, and then, a maelstrom.

01:56:09.120 --> 01:56:15.240
Flooding, hurricanes, tornadoes, all centered
around Clear Water, but cutting off neatly

01:56:15.240 --> 01:56:16.200
just beyond it.

01:56:16.200 --> 01:56:21.000
What happens in Clear Water remains in Clear
Water, and when the process has concluded

01:56:21.000 --> 01:56:25.440
and the sun shines once more, everybody has
been changed .

01:56:25.440 --> 01:56:29.820
Whenever the Foundation has tried to send
personnel or equipment into Clear Water during

01:56:29.820 --> 01:56:36.480
SCP-3300, one of two things have happened:
In the more favorable scenarios, those attempting

01:56:36.480 --> 01:56:40.260
to enter Clear Water have simply appeared
on the other side of the city limits.

01:56:40.260 --> 01:56:45.960
In the less positive instances, personnel
and equipment have been lost forever within.

01:56:45.960 --> 01:56:49.980
There is no stopping or even understanding
SCP-3300.

01:56:49.980 --> 01:56:55.080
According to Foundation records, Clear Water
has been around at least as long as the Foundation

01:56:55.080 --> 01:56:57.480
itself, perhaps even longer.

01:56:57.480 --> 01:57:02.700
Clear Water has been able to undergo its yearly
nightmare without intrusion due to a unique

01:57:02.700 --> 01:57:07.920
cognitohazardous effect, which creates a kind
of mental block around memories of the town

01:57:07.920 --> 01:57:08.880
for outsiders.

01:57:08.880 --> 01:57:14.040
You won’t forget Clear Water, per se, but
you will find it increasingly hard to focus

01:57:14.040 --> 01:57:14.340
on.

01:57:14.340 --> 01:57:18.480
Like something you can only ever see out of
the corner of your eye.

01:57:18.480 --> 01:57:20.880
There is no saving the people of Clear Water.

01:57:20.880 --> 01:57:25.020
The horror will play out again and again and
again…

01:57:25.020 --> 01:57:29.520
The Foundation has no first-hand knowledge
of what happens in Clear Water during those

01:57:29.520 --> 01:57:31.140
horrifying eighteen days.

01:57:31.140 --> 01:57:34.680
But one account they have hints at a terrifying
possibility.

01:57:34.680 --> 01:57:39.840
During an excursion into Clear Water, the
Foundation managed to collect a diary belonging

01:57:39.840 --> 01:57:41.760
to a woman named Margaret Lane.

01:57:41.760 --> 01:57:46.980
To the best of our knowledge, Margaret Lane
no longer exists, but if the contents of her

01:57:46.980 --> 01:57:53.220
diary are to be believed, then what goes on
in Clear Water during SCP-3300 is far worse

01:57:53.220 --> 01:57:55.200
than we’d ever imagined.

01:57:55.200 --> 01:58:01.620
Margaret first started her diary not long
before SCP-3300’s 1995 iteration began.

01:58:01.620 --> 01:58:06.660
She was in the middle of a tumultuous time
in her life - freshly clean from alcohol and

01:58:06.660 --> 01:58:09.720
drug addiction, forced to&nbsp;
live with her antagonistic&nbsp;

01:58:09.720 --> 01:58:12.360
mother, and having peculiar and distressing

01:58:12.360 --> 01:58:12.960
dreams.

01:58:12.960 --> 01:58:19.020
In the first dream Margaret recorded, she
was...someone else, a woman living in a small

01:58:19.020 --> 01:58:21.240
hut perhaps a century ago or more.

01:58:21.240 --> 01:58:22.440
It was plague time.

01:58:22.440 --> 01:58:28.380
She was looking down upon her daughter, bedridden,
her skin covered in painful-looking red blotches.

01:58:28.380 --> 01:58:30.600
Her husband was already dead.

01:58:30.600 --> 01:58:33.900
That’s when another man enters, a healthy
man.

01:58:33.900 --> 01:58:36.180
He tells her that he’s found their salvation.

01:58:36.180 --> 01:58:38.100
And then the dream ended.

01:58:38.100 --> 01:58:40.860
Margaret woke up to a gray, dreary day.

01:58:40.860 --> 01:58:42.660
There were clouds on the horizon.

01:58:42.660 --> 01:58:44.820
The rain was coming.

01:58:44.820 --> 01:58:49.380
It drizzled for the next few days, before
getting more intense - as one would expect

01:58:49.380 --> 01:58:51.660
from an SCP-3300 cycle.

01:58:51.660 --> 01:58:54.420
Of course, nothing seemed out of place to
Margaret.

01:58:54.420 --> 01:59:00.120
Life carried on - she continued to stay clean,
resisting the offers of her old dealer, though

01:59:00.120 --> 01:59:02.760
her relationship with her mother remained
frosty.

01:59:02.760 --> 01:59:07.440
The rain started to get worse as voices on
the radio insisted that conditions would continue

01:59:07.440 --> 01:59:10.140
to become more severe over the next few days.

01:59:10.140 --> 01:59:15.780
They tried their best to maintain normality;
Margaret invited some friends - Jared, Sam,

01:59:15.780 --> 01:59:19.080
Mike, and Isabel - to come over and play D&amp;D
at her place.

01:59:19.080 --> 01:59:21.960
That was when all hell broke loose.

01:59:21.960 --> 01:59:26.580
While the group roleplayed, there was a furious
banging at the door, like whoever was knocking

01:59:26.580 --> 01:59:28.320
was trying to bash the door down.

01:59:28.320 --> 01:59:33.600
When Margaret’s mom opened the door to investigate
the commotion, she saw that an entire family

01:59:33.600 --> 01:59:37.620
was standing there - a father, a mother, and
two young children.

01:59:37.620 --> 01:59:42.300
The father immediately began furiously asking
why all these strangers were in his house.

01:59:42.300 --> 01:59:46.980
When Margaret’s mother tried to tell him
that this wasn’t his house, he became increasingly

01:59:46.980 --> 01:59:49.500
agitated, and walked straight into the home.

01:59:49.500 --> 01:59:54.360
Margaret’s friends attempted to subdue him,
but he threw them off, displaying a supernatural

01:59:54.360 --> 01:59:54.960
strength.

01:59:54.960 --> 01:59:59.100
Margaret’s mom ran in with a golf club and
struck the mysterious man in the chest.

01:59:59.100 --> 02:00:02.820
There was a nasty splat, but he didn’t seem
to react.

02:00:02.820 --> 02:00:08.160
The golf club was just embedded in his chest,
having broken the skin and sunken in.

02:00:08.160 --> 02:00:09.780
But there was no blood.

02:00:09.780 --> 02:00:12.120
Just dripping water.

02:00:12.120 --> 02:00:16.380
The father then pulled the golf club out of
his chest, and began beating Margaret’s

02:00:16.380 --> 02:00:22.020
mother to death with it, all the while repeating
“My house” again and again, while his

02:00:22.020 --> 02:00:25.380
wife and children watched with broad, sunny
smiles in the rain.

02:00:25.380 --> 02:00:30.300
Somehow, Margaret knew that her mother was
beyond saving, and that there was no way of

02:00:30.300 --> 02:00:33.420
defeating these things in&nbsp;
a physical confrontation.

02:00:33.420 --> 02:00:38.100
All they could do was run out to Jared’s
van with the rest of the group and high tail

02:00:38.100 --> 02:00:39.060
it to the police station.

02:00:39.060 --> 02:00:44.160
But when they arrived at the station, the
doors were barred and it appeared empty.

02:00:44.160 --> 02:00:49.320
As the torrential rain hammered down from
above, there was nothing left to do but drive

02:00:49.320 --> 02:00:52.800
out of town and try to escape whatever madness
was going on here.

02:00:52.800 --> 02:00:55.560
But that was easier said than done.

02:00:55.560 --> 02:01:00.420
They drove for what seemed like hours on end
as the rain and the howling wind persisted.

02:01:00.420 --> 02:01:05.220
Jared had been injured during the fight with
the strange family and his health deteriorated

02:01:05.220 --> 02:01:07.200
further as the drive stretched on.

02:01:07.200 --> 02:01:12.060
They should have left the town of Clear Water
a long time ago, but it seemed like they were

02:01:12.060 --> 02:01:12.420
nowhere.

02:01:12.420 --> 02:01:17.340
It wasn’t long before Jared was lying dead
in the back of the van, and now, there were

02:01:17.340 --> 02:01:18.540
only four of them left.

02:01:18.540 --> 02:01:25.320
They kept driving - afraid, grieving, hungry,
and tired - and Margaret took the opportunity

02:01:25.320 --> 02:01:26.160
to sleep.

02:01:26.160 --> 02:01:31.320
It was no time to rest, but she was so exhausted
that she had no choice.

02:01:31.320 --> 02:01:34.020
Margaret had a continuation of her earlier
dream.

02:01:34.020 --> 02:01:38.940
The different her, the dream her, was laying
the plague-ridden body of her daughter in

02:01:38.940 --> 02:01:39.240
the river.

02:01:39.240 --> 02:01:40.860
But she wasn’t the only one.

02:01:40.860 --> 02:01:45.540
All the villages of her settlement were placing
the bodies of their dead in the river, as

02:01:45.540 --> 02:01:48.300
the water washed around them and through them.

02:01:48.300 --> 02:01:53.220
The bodies became one with the water, and
then, they became the water.

02:01:53.220 --> 02:01:55.140
The water was everything.

02:01:55.140 --> 02:01:59.820
When Margaret awoke, it was to the horrible
sounds of bubbling and boiling.

02:01:59.820 --> 02:02:03.240
That’s when she saw that Jared’s body
was...dissolving.

02:02:03.240 --> 02:02:06.060
No, not dissolving, evaporating.

02:02:06.060 --> 02:02:10.920
It was bubbling and convulsing, like it was
made of water, until the entire thing burst

02:02:10.920 --> 02:02:12.960
into a cascade of hot steam.

02:02:12.960 --> 02:02:17.340
After that, Margaret and the others left the
vehicle and refused to get back inside.

02:02:17.340 --> 02:02:19.620
Nothing was making sense.

02:02:19.620 --> 02:02:22.140
It was like something out of a nightmare.

02:02:22.140 --> 02:02:25.380
As they walked, the rain hammered down upon
them.

02:02:25.380 --> 02:02:28.800
They couldn’t have been walking for more
than a mile when they crashed into something.

02:02:28.800 --> 02:02:32.160
It was a sign - “Welcome to Clear Water.”

02:02:32.160 --> 02:02:35.100
It was like the town itself had drawn them
back.

02:02:35.100 --> 02:02:39.780
Mike refused to return to the town of his
own free will, and began walking in the other

02:02:39.780 --> 02:02:40.080
direction.

02:02:40.080 --> 02:02:45.060
Moments later, he was walking back towards
them in silence, though he’d never intended

02:02:45.060 --> 02:02:45.960
to.

02:02:45.960 --> 02:02:49.920
SCP-3300 had distorted his path, and brought
him back.

02:02:49.920 --> 02:02:54.840
It was clear that Mike was shaken to the core
by the experience, but they had to press on.

02:02:54.840 --> 02:02:59.100
They would head to the grocery store for food
and then to a sporting goods store where they

02:02:59.100 --> 02:03:04.200
could hopefully grab some guns to fight the
violent, altered people who’d somehow appeared

02:03:04.200 --> 02:03:04.920
with the rain.

02:03:04.920 --> 02:03:09.180
But things didn’t go to plan - or what little
plan there even was.

02:03:09.180 --> 02:03:14.340
Mike shot himself on the first night at Dirk’s
Sporting Goods, leaving only Margaret, Sam,

02:03:14.340 --> 02:03:15.480
and Isabel alive.

02:03:15.480 --> 02:03:19.740
Perhaps one of the most terrifying details
of Mike’s death was the fact he didn’t

02:03:19.740 --> 02:03:24.780
even bleed, instead, the gaping exit wound
in the back of his head was just full of water.

02:03:24.780 --> 02:03:27.960
Water was all that seemed to be left of them.

02:03:27.960 --> 02:03:32.220
Sam, seemingly driven to the edge by the sight
of Mike’s death, grabbed a hunting knife

02:03:32.220 --> 02:03:33.540
to perform an experiment.

02:03:33.540 --> 02:03:38.580
She cut into her own skin, and was horrified
to see only water dripping out.

02:03:38.580 --> 02:03:41.940
They’d all been “changed”, and they
didn’t know why.

02:03:41.940 --> 02:03:47.040
That’s when the survivors noticed something
else: There were people standing outside in

02:03:47.040 --> 02:03:48.720
the rain, hundreds of them.

02:03:48.720 --> 02:03:52.980
Not a single one they could recognize, all
new people.

02:03:52.980 --> 02:03:54.120
Waiting.

02:03:54.120 --> 02:03:59.520
Sam said only one word, “Outside”, before
walking out of the hunting goods store and

02:03:59.520 --> 02:04:03.060
disappearing into the crowd and the rain,
never to be seen again.

02:04:03.060 --> 02:04:07.260
Margaret mused that perhaps, in the end, she
had the right idea.

02:04:07.260 --> 02:04:11.700
To be taken, killed, erased, or changed would
be inevitable.

02:04:11.700 --> 02:04:16.560
In the final entry in Margaret’s diary,
dreams blend with reality as her mind finally

02:04:16.560 --> 02:04:18.000
gives out from the terror.

02:04:18.000 --> 02:04:22.080
She realizes, in her final moments, that there
is no way out.

02:04:22.080 --> 02:04:23.580
There is no escape.

02:04:23.580 --> 02:04:25.620
There is only water.

02:04:25.620 --> 02:04:27.600
Water is eternal.

02:04:27.600 --> 02:04:29.640
The rain is eternal.

02:04:29.640 --> 02:04:31.740
All will be changed.

02:04:31.740 --> 02:04:36.840
And given the fact that no trace of Margaret
was ever found, save for her diary, all her

02:04:36.840 --> 02:04:38.280
fears turned out to be right.

02:04:38.280 --> 02:04:44.340
She was taken and replaced by SCP-3300, just
as will inevitably happen to all the current

02:04:44.340 --> 02:04:48.780
citizens of Clear Water the next time SCP-3300
rolls around.

02:04:48.780 --> 02:04:54.240
It will be as inevitable and as indifferent
to those it affects as tomorrow’s sunrise.

02:04:54.240 --> 02:05:01.320
You cannot change the rain, but believe us,
in Clear Water, Montana, the rain can change

02:05:01.320 --> 02:05:01.740
you.

02:05:01.740 --> 02:05:08.160
You’re driving down a long highway, lost
in an area you don’t know too well, trying

02:05:08.160 --> 02:05:11.700
to find the right turn that’ll have you
heading back towards your home.

02:05:11.700 --> 02:05:15.840
You keep driving, the night-time quiet all
around you.

02:05:15.840 --> 02:05:21.660
Deciding to try and break that silence, you
reach for the radio, turning the dial to filter

02:05:21.660 --> 02:05:27.540
through all the garbled, distorted voices
and songs from nearby local stations that

02:05:27.540 --> 02:05:30.360
are too far out of range to come through clearly.

02:05:30.360 --> 02:05:35.820
You try your best to listen to the music from
one radio station, but eventually the sound

02:05:35.820 --> 02:05:39.780
of the static only makes you wish for the
silence you were trying to break.

02:05:39.780 --> 02:05:45.660
Your fingers nudge the tuning dial on your
car radio once again, and finally, something

02:05:45.660 --> 02:05:46.320
comes through.

02:05:46.320 --> 02:05:51.780
It isn’t loud or clear, but under the distortion
you can make out the sound.

02:05:51.780 --> 02:05:55.200
And it isn’t a song, or even a late news
broadcast.

02:05:55.200 --> 02:06:00.780
The first thing you hear sounds like a short
musical tone, only for about ten seconds.

02:06:00.780 --> 02:06:06.420
Next, a young girl’s voice, speaking in
a language you don’t understand, even through

02:06:06.420 --> 02:06:07.440
the distorted audio.

02:06:07.440 --> 02:06:12.420
From her accent, you assume it’s Russian,
but you still have no idea what the words

02:06:12.420 --> 02:06:13.500
she’s saying mean.

02:06:13.500 --> 02:06:17.100
With nothing else to listen to, you let the
broadcast play.

02:06:17.100 --> 02:06:22.740
Still driving along in the dark, with nothing
but the strange, adolescent voice to accompany

02:06:22.740 --> 02:06:25.260
you, your mind begins to wander.

02:06:25.260 --> 02:06:30.420
She sounds like she’s listing something,
but the rhythm of the words is somehow familiar

02:06:30.420 --> 02:06:33.120
to you, even though you don’t speak Russian.

02:06:33.120 --> 02:06:36.120
Then it hits you: she’s counting.

02:06:36.120 --> 02:06:38.820
But you don’t feel smart for having worked
that out.

02:06:38.820 --> 02:06:43.200
Instead, something about knowing that makes
your blood run cold.

02:06:43.200 --> 02:06:45.420
You carry on driving through the night.

02:06:45.420 --> 02:06:51.180
After a few short minutes, the Russian girl
stops counting and the musical tone plays

02:06:51.180 --> 02:06:57.000
again under the distortion, leaving you alone
in the car once again, with nothing but your

02:06:57.000 --> 02:07:01.020
thoughts and questions of what exactly you
just heard.

02:07:01.020 --> 02:07:06.780
Thankfully, we have the answer: What you heard
was SCP-3034.

02:07:06.780 --> 02:07:14.940
Since 1964, this same broadcast has been made
a vast number of times - 627 times in fact.

02:07:14.940 --> 02:07:19.320
You’d have to be within two kilometers of
the broadcast’s point of origin to hear

02:07:19.320 --> 02:07:24.900
it, where Foundation personnel have tried
and failed numerous times to triangulate its

02:07:24.900 --> 02:07:25.200
source.

02:07:25.200 --> 02:07:28.620
The numbers heard recited in the SCP-3034&nbsp;

02:07:28.620 --> 02:07:31.620
broadcast are actually a&nbsp;
countdown from two-hundred,

02:07:31.620 --> 02:07:33.240
read aloud in Russian.

02:07:33.240 --> 02:07:38.880
All Foundation staff are able to do while
stationed at the nearby Provisional Site-3034

02:07:38.880 --> 02:07:45.720
is scour radio frequencies for occurrences
of SCP-3034, checking their equipment is properly

02:07:45.720 --> 02:07:50.640
maintained and calibrated before they are
eventually rotated off-site and replaced with

02:07:50.640 --> 02:07:51.780
a new group of staff.

02:07:51.780 --> 02:07:57.420
There is only one rule that any Foundation
members working at Provisional Site-3034 must

02:07:57.420 --> 02:07:57.660
follow.

02:07:57.660 --> 02:08:02.880
They are only permitted to send one radio
transmission with their equipment, a single

02:08:02.880 --> 02:08:06.000
phrase in reply to the SCP-3034 broadcast:
“Vse Khorosho”, meaning “All is well”.

02:08:06.000 --> 02:08:13.740
Receiving this, the countdown stops and the
broadcast ends, but never permanently.

02:08:13.740 --> 02:08:18.840
SCP-3034 has been known to repeatedly occur,
seemingly at random.

02:08:18.840 --> 02:08:24.540
The shortest recorded gap between broadcasts
was two weeks, while the longest so far lasted

02:08:24.540 --> 02:08:25.860
six whole months.

02:08:25.860 --> 02:08:30.840
You may have heard the term “numbers station”
mentioned before, but these are far from just

02:08:30.840 --> 02:08:35.040
random numerical sequences, sent out over
the airwaves without purpose.

02:08:35.040 --> 02:08:40.500
General speculation surrounding numbers stations
points to them being the tools of espionage

02:08:40.500 --> 02:08:46.380
agents, a way of sending coded, highly-sensitive
messages or information without the risk of

02:08:46.380 --> 02:08:47.640
compromising their cover.

02:08:47.640 --> 02:08:52.920
The use of numbers station transmissions is
often attributed to spies working on foreign

02:08:52.920 --> 02:08:59.220
soil, who utilize short-wave radio frequencies,
speech synthesis, Morse code and either regular

02:08:59.220 --> 02:09:01.080
or sporadic timing schedules.

02:09:01.080 --> 02:09:06.120
While it’s true that times have changed,
and technology has progressed considerably,

02:09:06.120 --> 02:09:11.160
there appears to be evidence that numbers
stations are still used among various intelligence

02:09:11.160 --> 02:09:13.260
and espionage agencies today.

02:09:13.260 --> 02:09:16.020
Despite being considered an old-fashioned&nbsp;

02:09:16.020 --> 02:09:19.140
method of communication,&nbsp;
these low-tech, short-wave

02:09:19.140 --> 02:09:25.080
stations remain a viable, reliable option
for the transmission and reception of intelligence

02:09:25.080 --> 02:09:26.220
to field agents.

02:09:26.220 --> 02:09:31.320
The Conet Project is a comprehensive archive
of this phenomenon, and its founder, Akin

02:09:31.320 --> 02:09:34.200
Fernandez, has long been fascinated by numbers
stations.

02:09:34.200 --> 02:09:39.540
According to him, “This system is completely
secure because the messages can't be tracked,

02:09:39.540 --> 02:09:41.400
the recipient could be anywhere.

02:09:41.400 --> 02:09:44.640
You just send the spies to a country and get
them to buy a radio.

02:09:44.640 --> 02:09:46.920
They know where to tune and when.”

02:09:46.920 --> 02:09:52.200
So, what does the distorted broadcast of numbers
from SCP-3034 mean?

02:09:52.200 --> 02:09:56.700
Is it the work of covert agents, and if so,
whose side are they on?

02:09:56.700 --> 02:10:02.040
Most importantly, why does the SCP Foundation
make certain there are always three of its

02:10:02.040 --> 02:10:08.160
personnel on-site, ready to send the “All
is well” message whenever SCP-3034 begins

02:10:08.160 --> 02:10:08.820
broadcasting?

02:10:08.820 --> 02:10:15.660
SCP-3034 was first discovered by the Foundation
in 1964, after a defector from the Soviet

02:10:15.660 --> 02:10:21.420
GRU-P, a division tasked with acquiring and
studying anomalies on behalf of the USSR,

02:10:21.420 --> 02:10:22.800
gave them a tip.

02:10:22.800 --> 02:10:28.140
Commander Robert Malthus, along with a team
of six, including a man named Agent Browning

02:10:28.140 --> 02:10:32.400
- selected for his knowledge of Russian dialects
- were sent to investigate at Provisional

02:10:32.400 --> 02:10:33.600
Site-3034.

02:10:33.600 --> 02:10:38.220
Here, the team uncovered partially-burned
records and logbooks all kept in Russian,

02:10:38.220 --> 02:10:42.540
along with evidence that the site had been
evacuated shortly before their arrival.

02:10:42.540 --> 02:10:47.760
Carved into a desk, also in Russian, were
two phrases: “Don’t let her finish”

02:10:47.760 --> 02:10:49.680
and “Tell her all is well”.

02:10:49.680 --> 02:10:55.560
On the team’s second day at the site, an
automated alarm sounded at 7:30am, alerting

02:10:55.560 --> 02:10:58.620
them to the incoming SCP-3034 broadcast.

02:10:58.620 --> 02:11:04.140
Following the instructions on the desk, Agent
Browning was able to stop the broadcast, telling

02:11:04.140 --> 02:11:06.540
the young Russian girl that all was well.

02:11:06.540 --> 02:11:11.520
A tape was partially recovered by the team
from the site, and translated from Russian.

02:11:11.520 --> 02:11:16.320
The GRU-P members that had previously inhabited
the station had interrogated one of their

02:11:16.320 --> 02:11:20.580
own, a man named Sergei, whom they accused
of stealing state property.

02:11:20.580 --> 02:11:23.280
“She’s not state property,” he replied.

02:11:23.280 --> 02:11:25.020
“She has a name.”

02:11:25.020 --> 02:11:30.660
While his GRU-P superior accused Sergei of
planning to defect to the United States, allegedly

02:11:30.660 --> 02:11:35.100
in exchange for money and asylum, Sergei denied
any collusion with America.

02:11:35.100 --> 02:11:41.100
He claimed that the GRU-P at Provisional Site-3034
were meddling with powers they could not possibly

02:11:41.100 --> 02:11:42.000
hope to understand.

02:11:42.000 --> 02:11:47.880
His superior, a man named Vaslov, dismissed
this, claiming their work to be no different

02:11:47.880 --> 02:11:51.420
to the United States’ experimentation with
atomic weapons at the time.

02:11:51.420 --> 02:11:55.500
“One does not make deals with atom-bombs,”
Sergei argued.

02:11:55.500 --> 02:11:59.220
“One certainly does not sacrifice little
girls to them.”

02:11:59.220 --> 02:12:04.020
Shortly after this, a struggle broke out,
with Sergei having to be restrained, while

02:12:04.020 --> 02:12:07.620
urging Vaslov to cease any and all interference
with “it”.

02:12:07.620 --> 02:12:12.600
The man spoke of terrible nightmares that
he’d had, voices screaming in the darkness.

02:12:12.600 --> 02:12:14.460
“That's what it wants, Vaslov.

02:12:14.460 --> 02:12:15.900
That's what it is.

02:12:15.900 --> 02:12:20.880
You cannot make a deal with this thing — we
have finally contained it, and now you want

02:12:20.880 --> 02:12:21.690
to offer it —”

02:12:21.690 --> 02:12:26.640
The tape’s audio ends shortly after this
point, with no clear answer as to what Sergei

02:12:26.640 --> 02:12:30.900
was referring to, or what offer these Russian
operatives had made to “it’“.

02:12:30.900 --> 02:12:37.140
Ever since the discovery of SCP-3034, members
of the SCP Foundation have worked tirelessly

02:12:37.140 --> 02:12:41.820
to understand the purpose of these countdowns,
as well as determine their origin.

02:12:41.820 --> 02:12:47.280
By September 2012, Doctor Schulkill was reaching
the end of his tether with the investigation

02:12:47.280 --> 02:12:49.800
into the SCP-3034 broadcast.

02:12:49.800 --> 02:12:55.380
Over almost half a century, the Foundation
had made well over 600 recordings of the Russian

02:12:55.380 --> 02:12:59.280
girl’s countdowns, but still hadn’t determined
any noteworthy information.

02:12:59.280 --> 02:13:05.340
They were prohibited from contacting the girl
via the same radio frequency, only permitted

02:13:05.340 --> 02:13:07.860
to use the phrase that stopped her countdowns.

02:13:07.860 --> 02:13:13.500
Running out of options, Schulkill contacted
his colleague, Doctor Emerson, asking for

02:13:13.500 --> 02:13:18.420
an in-depth vocal analysis of the various
recordings of SCP-3034.

02:13:18.420 --> 02:13:23.820
Even if they could narrow down where the broadcast
was coming from, maybe by determining the

02:13:23.820 --> 02:13:28.920
girl’s geographical location from her dialect,
then that would be at least some slight progress

02:13:28.920 --> 02:13:32.160
into understanding SCP-3034.

02:13:32.160 --> 02:13:37.680
While unable to discover the girl’s location,
Doctor Emerson’s analysis did yield some

02:13:37.680 --> 02:13:38.820
interesting findings.

02:13:38.820 --> 02:13:44.400
Emerson learned that these countdowns were
not pre-recorded, the variations in the Russian

02:13:44.400 --> 02:13:49.980
girl’s voice, her tone, her pitch, all seemed
to indicate that every instance of the broadcast

02:13:49.980 --> 02:13:51.180
was unique.

02:13:51.180 --> 02:13:56.340
Rather than using the same recording, this
girl had been counting down over and over,

02:13:56.340 --> 02:13:59.220
hundreds of times for almost fifty years.

02:13:59.220 --> 02:14:00.660
But there was more.

02:14:00.660 --> 02:14:03.780
Schulkill and Emerson then&nbsp;
examined the distortion,&nbsp;

02:14:03.780 --> 02:14:05.880
the sounds interfering with the audio of the

02:14:05.880 --> 02:14:07.260
Russian girl’s countdowns.

02:14:07.260 --> 02:14:12.960
What had initially seemed like garbled static,
seemed to actually be additional voices.

02:14:12.960 --> 02:14:19.860
And much like the girl’s voice, these distorted
voices were unique, different in every broadcast.

02:14:19.860 --> 02:14:24.780
However, Schulkill and Emerson were unable
to accurately determine what these voices

02:14:24.780 --> 02:14:25.440
were saying.

02:14:25.440 --> 02:14:29.880
Given that the girl’s countdowns were always
cut short by the use of the phrase “All

02:14:29.880 --> 02:14:34.680
is well”, the doctors did not have long-enough
samples of the audio to analyze the other

02:14:34.680 --> 02:14:35.760
distorted voices.

02:14:35.760 --> 02:14:41.400
With permission from the Foundation, the next
five occurrences of the SCP-3034 broadcast

02:14:41.400 --> 02:14:46.680
were allowed to carry on for longer, giving
the two doctors enough audio to determine

02:14:46.680 --> 02:14:49.140
exactly what the distorted voices were.

02:14:49.140 --> 02:14:52.020
And the results were extremely troubling.

02:14:52.020 --> 02:14:54.240
They were screams.

02:14:54.240 --> 02:14:59.340
Thousands upon thousands of children’s voices,
endlessly screaming.

02:14:59.340 --> 02:15:03.960
Both Doctor Emerson and Doctor Schulkill agreed
that it would be best to continue responding

02:15:03.960 --> 02:15:10.680
to SCP-3034 with the correct phrase, and refused
to analyze the distorted screaming audio any

02:15:10.680 --> 02:15:11.100
further.

02:15:11.100 --> 02:15:17.340
Three years later, while stationed at Provisional
Site-3034, a Foundation researcher named Doctor

02:15:17.340 --> 02:15:21.240
Uriel Willis decided to take matters into
her own hands.

02:15:21.240 --> 02:15:26.040
She conducted an experiment that had not been
sanctioned by the Foundation and attempted

02:15:26.040 --> 02:15:29.280
to make contact with the Russian girl giving
the countdowns.

02:15:29.280 --> 02:15:32.940
Hearing Doctor Willis’ voice, the girl stopped
her countdown.

02:15:32.940 --> 02:15:36.000
After five long, painfully-silent seconds,&nbsp;

02:15:36.000 --> 02:15:40.080
a new broadcast was heard:&nbsp;
A piercing, high-pitched

02:15:40.080 --> 02:15:45.060
screech that caused extreme pain and dizziness
to all of the staff working on-site.

02:15:45.060 --> 02:15:50.460
Unable to bear the disorienting sound, Dr
Willis told the girl “All is well”, and

02:15:50.460 --> 02:15:52.140
caused the noise to stop.

02:15:52.140 --> 02:15:57.720
The following day, SCP researchers noted there
had been a significant increase in cases of

02:15:57.720 --> 02:15:59.700
missing children all around the world.

02:15:59.700 --> 02:16:04.620
A majority of these disappearances happened
at the same time the screech had been broadcast,

02:16:04.620 --> 02:16:07.680
and remain unsolved to this day.

02:16:07.680 --> 02:16:13.320
Dr. Willis faced disciplinary action from
the SCP Foundation, and any further testing

02:16:13.320 --> 02:16:18.540
of SCP-3034, and attempts to communicate with
the Russian girl, were prohibited.

02:16:18.540 --> 02:16:24.240
Only one distinct change has been noted in
the SCP-3034 broadcast since this incident.

02:16:24.240 --> 02:16:28.680
Almost a month later, the countdown was detected
and the correct phrase given.

02:16:28.680 --> 02:16:34.080
But researchers noted that, instead of starting
her countdown from two-hundred, this time

02:16:34.080 --> 02:16:37.920
the Russian girl began counting down from
199.

02:16:37.920 --> 02:16:42.600
Nobody knows what will happen if the Russian
girl’s countdown is allowed to reach zero.

02:16:42.600 --> 02:16:47.821
Personnel working at Provisional Site-3034
are told to always offer her the necessary

02:16:47.820 --> 02:16:49.799
phrase before this point in the countdown.

02:16:49.800 --> 02:16:54.420
Attempting to interfere with the broadcast
by contacting this girl directly not only

02:16:54.420 --> 02:17:00.300
resulted in intense pain for SCP staff, but
also seems to have caused an unconfirmed number

02:17:00.300 --> 02:17:05.280
of child disappearances around the globe,
as well as reducing the countdown starting

02:17:05.280 --> 02:17:08.759
number from 200 to 199.

02:17:08.760 --> 02:17:14.400
After a long night on the road, you finally
find the right turn, sending you in the right

02:17:14.399 --> 02:17:14.700
direction.

02:17:14.700 --> 02:17:21.240
As you drive through the night, you keep telling
yourself one thing, one small phrase over

02:17:21.240 --> 02:17:22.620
and over again.

02:17:22.620 --> 02:17:27.780
You hope the words will eventually give you
comfort, but deep down you start to realize

02:17:27.780 --> 02:17:32.820
just how hollow they are, that it’s just
a lie we tell ourselves so we don’t have

02:17:32.820 --> 02:17:34.320
to face the inevitable.

02:17:34.320 --> 02:17:40.799
But still, what choice do you have but to
keep telling yourself that “All is well.”

02:17:40.800 --> 02:17:47.700
The year was 1857, and the Second Opium War
was raging between China and the combined

02:17:47.700 --> 02:17:52.740
forces of the English and French. It was one
of the many bloody colonial wars fought over

02:17:52.740 --> 02:17:59.700
resources like tea, sugar, and the intoxicating
opium poppy. It was a war fought by peasants

02:17:59.700 --> 02:18:04.920
and noblemen alike. One of these aristocratic
soldiers was the noble Lord Theodore Thomas

02:18:04.920 --> 02:18:10.920
Blackwood, the quintessential English gentleman
and explorer. While his fellow soldiers cowered

02:18:10.920 --> 02:18:15.960
behind cover, Lord Blackwood charged into
the fray, shouldering his rifle and firing

02:18:15.960 --> 02:18:18.359
his pistol into the crowd of opposing soldiers.

02:18:18.359 --> 02:18:23.700
It was the Battle of Canton, one of the most
crucial battles of the entire conflict. The

02:18:23.700 --> 02:18:28.559
French and English were laying siege to the
city of Canton, also known as Guangzhou, to

02:18:28.560 --> 02:18:32.581
prove their military dominance and capture
an important Chinese government official.

02:18:32.580 --> 02:18:37.620
Lord Blackwood led the charge on horseback.
Every bullet seemed to find the heart of a

02:18:37.620 --> 02:18:44.160
foe. He was a true hero among men; a gentleman
warrior with class, refinement, and style.

02:18:44.160 --> 02:18:49.320
And it would be thanks to his expert leadership
and marksmanship on the field that the allied

02:18:49.320 --> 02:18:52.080
European forces won the battle decisively.

02:18:52.080 --> 02:18:56.460
Lord Theodore Thomas Blackwood is a name that
deserves to be counted among Lord

02:18:56.460 --> 02:19:02.399
Horatio Nelson, Sir Francis Bacon, and Sir
Walter Raleigh. In addition to being a skilled

02:19:02.399 --> 02:19:08.099
and honorable fighter, Lord Blackwood is an
consummate explorer, naturalist, and frontiersman.

02:19:08.100 --> 02:19:13.380
During his heyday, he traveled perhaps further
than any man across the known and unknown

02:19:13.380 --> 02:19:18.720
corners of the globe. He made scientific,
biological, and anthropological discoveries

02:19:18.720 --> 02:19:24.360
that should have reset the course of society
forever. And yet, you won’t find any records

02:19:24.359 --> 02:19:29.399
in the history books of Lord Theodore Thomas
Blackwood. Nor will you find any grand oil

02:19:29.399 --> 02:19:32.399
paintings, or dedicated wings in British museums.

02:19:32.399 --> 02:19:38.939
This is because Lord Theodore Thomas Blackwood…
is a four and a half inch, telepathic neon

02:19:38.939 --> 02:19:45.899
sea slug. And he’s known to the SCP Foundation,
as SCP-1867.

02:19:45.899 --> 02:19:51.240
While he would never admit to it, Lord Blackwood
belongs to the species Nembrotha kubaryana,

02:19:51.240 --> 02:19:56.880
also known as the variable neon slug. He’s
kept in a standard aquarium in a Foundation

02:19:56.880 --> 02:20:02.880
containment site, and is physically no different
to any other member of his species. What makes

02:20:02.880 --> 02:20:09.300
Lord Blackwood unique is his powerful telepathic
abilities - specifically, the power to communicate

02:20:09.300 --> 02:20:15.060
by speaking directly into people’s minds.
And what’s more, he’s extremely talkative.

02:20:15.060 --> 02:20:22.140
But to what extent is anything that this anomalous
sea slug says true? Or is he just like SCP-082,

02:20:22.140 --> 02:20:26.161
Fernand the Cannibal - a creative and pathological
liar.

02:20:26.160 --> 02:20:30.599
It isn’t committed to record how exactly
the Foundation discovered Lord Blackwood.

02:20:30.600 --> 02:20:35.220
Perhaps a local aquarium worker worried they
were going insane when they heard the voice

02:20:35.220 --> 02:20:40.020
of a nineteenth century English nobleman ringing
in their ears whenever they were cleaning

02:20:40.020 --> 02:20:45.600
algae out of the tank. Maybe Lord Blackwood
was found by SCP Foundation divers, who are

02:20:45.600 --> 02:20:50.400
constantly combing the ocean for anomalous
creatures and activity. What we do know is

02:20:50.399 --> 02:20:55.979
that Lord Blackwood is an incredibly strange
and mysterious individual. He claims to have

02:20:55.979 --> 02:21:01.259
visited locations all around the world, and
encountered rare societies and creatures.

02:21:01.260 --> 02:21:06.000
The Foundation was skeptical about a number
of Lord Blackwood’s more outlandish claims,

02:21:06.000 --> 02:21:10.680
on account of him being a sea slug, but he
does appear to have the knowledge to back

02:21:10.680 --> 02:21:15.600
up his supposed experience. Interviews with
Lord Blackwood have shown that he’s extremely

02:21:15.600 --> 02:21:22.140
knowledgeable in the areas of geography, zoology,
botany, archaeology, anthropology and linguistics

02:21:22.140 --> 02:21:27.720
relating to his claimed regions of exploration,
as well as more esoteric fields such as obscure

02:21:27.720 --> 02:21:33.900
mythology, mysticism, and cryptozoology. In
other words, if Lord Blackwood hadn’t gone

02:21:33.899 --> 02:21:38.339
on his escapades around the globe throughout
history, how would he come to possess this

02:21:38.340 --> 02:21:39.480
wide variety of information?

02:21:39.479 --> 02:21:44.580
The Foundation was getting frustrated, and
began to probe further into the personal life

02:21:44.580 --> 02:21:50.399
of the most interesting gastropod in containment.
Lord Blackwood, under questioning, was always

02:21:50.399 --> 02:21:55.259
polite and amicable with Foundation staff.
He seemed to display no real knowledge of

02:21:55.260 --> 02:22:00.420
the fact that he himself was a sea slug - going
as far to accuse other people of being crazy

02:22:00.420 --> 02:22:04.440
or drunk when they brought the fact up to
him. While none of Lord Blackwood’s tall

02:22:04.439 --> 02:22:10.139
tales ever extend past the year 1910, he told
fanciful stories of exploring the Americas,

02:22:10.140 --> 02:22:13.980
and of his involvement in the Second Opium
War on the side of the English.

02:22:13.979 --> 02:22:19.200
Naturally, the Foundation wanted proof. When
they pressured Lord Blackwood on this, something

02:22:19.200 --> 02:22:24.300
even stranger happened: He gave it. The Lord
told his interviewers that he would happily

02:22:24.300 --> 02:22:28.740
donate his collection to them, if it gave
them cause to believe what he was saying.

02:22:28.740 --> 02:22:33.719
He gave the baffled Foundation researchers
the address of a cottage in England where

02:22:33.720 --> 02:22:38.820
they could find the secrets to his bizarre
and mysterious past, and local agents in the

02:22:38.819 --> 02:22:40.259
area followed up on the information.

02:22:40.260 --> 02:22:46.260
Upon investigation, Foundation Field Agents
did indeed find the cottage that Lord Blackwood

02:22:46.260 --> 02:22:51.180
had specified. It was being maintained by
an extremely old woman. When questioned about

02:22:51.180 --> 02:22:55.020
her presence there, she said that she was
“keeping the house for Lord Blackwood”,

02:22:55.020 --> 02:23:01.320
and gave no more useful information. Incidentally,
it appeared that this singular purpose was

02:23:01.319 --> 02:23:06.179
all that this old woman was living for. She
abruptly passed away from heart failure five

02:23:06.180 --> 02:23:10.800
days after the Foundation commandeered the
cottage. Whether anything truly anomalous

02:23:10.800 --> 02:23:13.620
caused this, we still don’t know.

02:23:13.620 --> 02:23:18.059
At first, the cottage seemed normal, until
the Field Agents discovered a secret basement

02:23:18.060 --> 02:23:23.161
housing Lord Blackwood’s “collection.”
They were amazed at what they saw: The basement

02:23:23.160 --> 02:23:26.160
consisted of zoological and botanical specimens,&nbsp;

02:23:26.160 --> 02:23:29.399
over three thousand artifacts,&nbsp;
a library containing

02:23:29.399 --> 02:23:35.339
over five thousand items, and a functioning
1800s scientific laboratory. It took around

02:23:35.340 --> 02:23:39.840
three weeks for Foundation agents working
round the clock in shifts to remove all the

02:23:39.840 --> 02:23:45.540
items from Lord Blackwood’s mysterious collection,
and what they found raised even more questions.

02:23:45.540 --> 02:23:51.600
The collection included, but was by no means
limited to: 116 unknown species of plants,

02:23:51.600 --> 02:23:58.980
107 unknown species of insects, 28 unknown
species of lizards, 23 unknown species of

02:23:58.979 --> 02:24:05.639
fish, 14 unknown species of amphibians, 12
unknown species of mammals, Fossils pertaining

02:24:05.640 --> 02:24:10.860
to 8 unknown species of dinosaur, Fossils
pertaining to 12 unknown species of prehistoric

02:24:10.859 --> 02:24:17.580
mammal, and Artifacts belonging to 29 unknown
indigenous societies. That’s a lot of unknowns!

02:24:17.580 --> 02:24:22.920
But wait, there’s more! His collection also
contained a collection of seemingly unknown

02:24:22.920 --> 02:24:28.380
firearms, including three wide-bore muskets
marked as “Dr. B. T. Moth’s Effective

02:24:28.380 --> 02:24:33.720
Particle Destabilizers.” Detailed globes
of Mercury, Venus, Mars, and the Galilean

02:24:33.720 --> 02:24:39.600
moons, accompanied by notes detailing possible
paths of surface exploration. A heavily modified

02:24:39.600 --> 02:24:44.400
carriage, containing instruments of unknown
purpose. A note attached to the door reads

02:24:44.399 --> 02:24:49.259
“On the fritz. Speak with Henry.” And
a highly dangerous and seemingly anomalous

02:24:49.260 --> 02:24:54.180
machine that killed four Foundation Field
Agents before it was destroyed on site. And

02:24:54.180 --> 02:24:57.480
when questioned about this little fiasco,
Lord Blackwood responded:

02:24:57.479 --> 02:25:01.740
“I did warn you to be careful around my
collection. That bloody thing nearly took

02:25:01.740 --> 02:25:03.660
my head off back in ninety-seven when I found
it.”

02:25:03.660 --> 02:25:08.340
However, there was one thing recovered from
Lord Blackwood’s collection that was perhaps

02:25:08.340 --> 02:25:12.360
more interesting than all&nbsp;
the others: 35 hand-written&nbsp;

02:25:12.359 --> 02:25:15.000
journals containing recordings of events described

02:25:15.000 --> 02:25:20.460
by Lord Blackwood in his grandiose tall tales
to the Foundation researchers. The accounts

02:25:20.460 --> 02:25:24.780
are generally identical to the stories he
had told, save for some slight variations

02:25:24.780 --> 02:25:29.819
and exaggerations on the part of Blackwood
in the re-telling. Most interestingly of all,

02:25:29.819 --> 02:25:34.559
all of these journals have been dated to the
appropriate time period of the events described

02:25:34.560 --> 02:25:36.300
by Foundation scientists.

02:25:36.300 --> 02:25:40.920
While his stories are too numerous to all
be shared here, there’s one that perfectly

02:25:40.920 --> 02:25:47.100
sums them all up: Lord Blackwood’s account
of a possible encounter with SCP - 1000, also

02:25:47.100 --> 02:25:50.281
known as Bigfoot, in Seattle during the mid-1800s.

02:25:50.280 --> 02:25:55.080
Lord Blackwood, seeking to explore the so-called
“new world” of North America, embarked

02:25:55.080 --> 02:25:59.760
with an assistant and an indigenous American
guide to the Pacific Northwest, in search

02:25:59.760 --> 02:26:05.760
of the legendary Sasquatch. The trio was headed
for Mount Rainier, then known as Tahoma. During

02:26:05.760 --> 02:26:10.080
the journey, Lord Blackwood found a young
fox caught in a trap that had been set by

02:26:10.080 --> 02:26:15.120
a local tribe. He took sympathy on the animal
and freed it, allowing it to run away to safety.

02:26:15.120 --> 02:26:19.620
That night, he and his assistant met up with
the rest of his guide’s tribe, and they

02:26:19.620 --> 02:26:24.599
settled down for the evening. However, things
took a disastrous turn when the camp was raided

02:26:24.600 --> 02:26:29.940
by a rival tribe. Almost everyone was slaughtered
in the process, and Lord Blackwood and his

02:26:29.939 --> 02:26:35.639
two companions were hauled away by the enemy
tribe for a sinister purpose: Sacrifice to

02:26:35.640 --> 02:26:36.960
a violent local deity.

02:26:36.960 --> 02:26:42.180
As it turns out, the creature that this tribe
worshipped was the very same one Lord Blackwood

02:26:42.180 --> 02:26:48.360
and the others were trying to find: A particularly
large and aggressive Sasquatch. Each night,

02:26:48.359 --> 02:26:53.759
a different sacrifice was made to the Sasquatch.
The victim would be placed near a forest clearing

02:26:53.760 --> 02:26:58.260
while the tribe played a primal song, and
the Sasquatch would emerge from the trees

02:26:58.260 --> 02:27:04.080
to devour its prey. The first night it ate
the assistant, the next night it ate the guide.

02:27:04.080 --> 02:27:09.000
And then, it became time for the sacrifice
of Lord Blackwood himself.

02:27:09.000 --> 02:27:11.580
As Blackwood was presented for sacrifice,&nbsp;

02:27:11.580 --> 02:27:14.819
he accepted his fate. But&nbsp;
instead of the Sasquatch,

02:27:14.819 --> 02:27:21.059
a legion of woodland animals emerged from
the trees - foxes, elks, raccoons, and more

02:27:21.060 --> 02:27:25.980
- themselves painted with tribal symbols.
The animals seemed to be on Lord Blackwood’s

02:27:25.979 --> 02:27:30.059
side, and attacked the tribespeople who had
been holding him captive giving Blackwood

02:27:30.060 --> 02:27:34.980
the chance to flee into the forest during
the chaos. Later, these same animals would

02:27:34.979 --> 02:27:39.240
find Blackwood again, and present him with
the things his captors had stolen from him.

02:27:39.240 --> 02:27:44.700
An elder fox also gave him a letter, proclaiming
him a knight of their people now. He was allowed

02:27:44.700 --> 02:27:49.260
safe passage back to a nearby settlement,
at which point he wrote to his financiers

02:27:49.260 --> 02:27:53.880
back in England, explaining the situation
and asking for more money to perform further

02:27:53.880 --> 02:27:59.160
expeditions into the Tahoma region. The whole
incident had only increased his thirst for

02:27:59.160 --> 02:28:01.019
adventure and exploration.

02:28:01.020 --> 02:28:07.621
Whether this tale is actually true, or just
a bizarre, colonial fantasy from the pathological

02:28:07.620 --> 02:28:10.740
mind of a telepathic sea slug, we may never&nbsp;

02:28:10.740 --> 02:28:13.740
know - but it doesn’t make&nbsp;
it any less interesting.

02:28:13.740 --> 02:28:19.620
To this day, Lord Blackwood continues to be
a perplexing but fascinating anomaly. He may

02:28:19.620 --> 02:28:24.180
not be the most dangerous, and he may not
be the most useful, either, but there’s

02:28:24.180 --> 02:28:28.560
no denying that perhaps we’d all like to
sit next to his tank for a couple hours one

02:28:28.560 --> 02:28:32.400
day, and hear him spin a good yarn over a
warm cup of tea.

02:28:32.399 --> 02:28:37.559
There’s a quote that says “the beautiful
thing about learning is nobody can take it

02:28:37.560 --> 02:28:38.281
away from you.”

02:28:38.280 --> 02:28:43.380
But what good is learning if the knowledge
might hurt you, drive you mad, or even kill

02:28:43.380 --> 02:28:43.620
you?

02:28:43.620 --> 02:28:48.899
It just sits there in your mind, like a stick
of dynamite with an invisible fuse.

02:28:48.899 --> 02:28:50.639
It could blow at any moment.

02:28:50.640 --> 02:28:55.741
All it’d take is a careless slip of the
tongue, and you might turn into a talking

02:28:55.740 --> 02:28:56.760
home appliance.

02:28:56.760 --> 02:29:02.700
This is a conundrum faced by anyone dealing
with an Infohazard - a certain kind of anomaly

02:29:02.700 --> 02:29:05.280
often dealt with by the SCP Foundation.

02:29:05.280 --> 02:29:10.319
Before we get into some of the craziest examples
of infohazards and what they’ve done to

02:29:10.319 --> 02:29:14.759
people, because let’s face it, that’s
what you’re really here for, first we have

02:29:14.760 --> 02:29:21.120
to answer that big question everyone’s a
little afraid to ask: Just what is an Infohazard?

02:29:21.120 --> 02:29:27.120
And how does it differ from a far more common
type of SCP, the dreaded Cognitohazard?

02:29:27.120 --> 02:29:29.519
Well we’re glad you were finally brave enough
to ask.

02:29:29.520 --> 02:29:34.860
First, cognitohazards are anomalies that are
dangerous to perceive through one of the senses.

02:29:34.859 --> 02:29:41.280
A well known example is SCP-096, which is
actually a visual cognitohazard.

02:29:41.280 --> 02:29:43.979
You see its face, and you’re toast.

02:29:43.979 --> 02:29:45.479
It’s as simple as that.

02:29:45.479 --> 02:29:52.259
And cognitohazards exist for all of the other
senses too: hearing, taste, touch, even smell.

02:29:52.260 --> 02:29:54.840
Infohazards, on the other hand, are different.

02:29:54.840 --> 02:29:59.819
These anomalous effects are triggered when
you start trying to express or describe something

02:29:59.819 --> 02:30:06.240
about what you’ve perceived, and when you
do, things start to get real weird real fast.

02:30:06.240 --> 02:30:10.979
Maybe you’re trying to explain what you
just saw to family members, friends, or the

02:30:10.979 --> 02:30:11.160
police.

02:30:11.160 --> 02:30:16.080
Maybe you’re a member of SCP Foundation
staff, trying to write up a report, or a new

02:30:16.080 --> 02:30:16.800
experiment log.

02:30:16.800 --> 02:30:22.080
Or maybe you’re a YouTube channel, trying
to create entertaining yet informative breakdowns

02:30:22.080 --> 02:30:25.080
and explanations of anomalies from the SCP
Foundation.

02:30:25.080 --> 02:30:31.019
If any or all of these apply to you, then
Infohazards are going to be your worst enemy.

02:30:31.020 --> 02:30:36.720
But as we look at some of the strangest examples,
we’ll try our best to resist their effects.

02:30:36.720 --> 02:30:41.340
First, seeing as it’s so hot out, how about
we take a relaxing dip in the pool while we

02:30:41.340 --> 02:30:44.040
tell you all about SCP-1128.

02:30:44.040 --> 02:30:46.200
What is SCP-1128?

02:30:46.200 --> 02:30:48.059
Well, that’s a loaded question.

02:30:48.060 --> 02:30:53.880
Technically speaking, it’s a massive, predatory,
aquatic creature, but despite its huge size,

02:30:53.880 --> 02:30:57.000
the creature can hunt its prey in any body
of water.

02:30:57.000 --> 02:31:02.160
Whether you’re stepping in a puddle, relaxing
in the bath, or say, chilling out in the pool,

02:31:02.160 --> 02:31:07.620
SCP-1128 can track you down and potentially
eat you alive.

02:31:07.620 --> 02:31:12.840
In one particularly horrifying test, a D-Class
was drinking from a simple glass of water,

02:31:12.840 --> 02:31:17.580
when the aquatic predator emerged, yanked
them inside, and ate them.

02:31:17.580 --> 02:31:22.200
Okay, so maybe you’re feeling a little nervous
now, but don’t worry, you’re still safe.

02:31:22.200 --> 02:31:26.280
Some people have even survived their attacks
from SCP-1128.

02:31:26.280 --> 02:31:28.500
Well, their initial attacks anyway.

02:31:28.500 --> 02:31:34.620
The creature has a tendency to come back,
again and again, relentless in its ravenous

02:31:34.620 --> 02:31:36.180
hunger for human flesh.

02:31:36.180 --> 02:31:40.680
Whenever it attacks successfully, all that’s
left is some blood floating on the water.

02:31:40.680 --> 02:31:45.540
But again, please don’t worry too much about
this creature, we don’t have another 682

02:31:45.540 --> 02:31:46.319
on our hands.

02:31:46.319 --> 02:31:50.939
After all, it’s an infohazard, it can only
start hunting you if you receive a written

02:31:50.939 --> 02:31:52.740
or verbal description of the creature.

02:31:52.740 --> 02:31:56.519
Oh, or some kind of visual representation
of the creature, too.

02:31:56.520 --> 02:32:00.180
Actually, on second thought, you may want
to get out of the pool.

02:32:00.180 --> 02:32:01.320
Now.

02:32:01.319 --> 02:32:03.299
And put down that drink too.

02:32:03.300 --> 02:32:06.240
Instead, let us tell you a nice little story.

02:32:06.240 --> 02:32:10.439
You step into a bar, smelling of fine liquor
and rich mahogany.

02:32:10.439 --> 02:32:13.679
You even get a whiff of some fine, leather
bound book.

02:32:13.680 --> 02:32:18.540
You see us sitting at the bar, motiong for
you to come over, and you decide to approach.

02:32:18.540 --> 02:32:24.660
You’re intrigued by our winning smile, and
our vast knowledge of anomalies and SCP Foundation

02:32:24.660 --> 02:32:25.139
lore.

02:32:25.140 --> 02:32:27.540
You take a seat next to us and order a drink.

02:32:27.540 --> 02:32:30.540
Get something fancy, it’s on our tab after
all.

02:32:30.540 --> 02:32:31.560
Our treat.

02:32:31.560 --> 02:32:34.260
“What does this have to do with Infohazards?”
you ask.

02:32:35.399 --> 02:32:42.719
“That’s the thing about SCP-1893, kid,”
we say, our dulcet tones smoother than scotch.

02:32:42.720 --> 02:32:44.820
“You can never just talk about it.

02:32:44.819 --> 02:32:49.799
It’s an Infohazard that forces information
about it to be delivered like a story.

02:32:49.800 --> 02:32:53.520
That’s why we’re in this bar right now,
that’s the set up.

02:32:53.520 --> 02:32:57.781
It expresses actual information about itself
through the dialogue, see?”

02:32:57.780 --> 02:33:02.700
You nod, beginning to grasp the concept, as
the bartender serves you your drink.

02:33:02.700 --> 02:33:05.280
It’s been forever since you’ve been to
a bar.

02:33:05.280 --> 02:33:07.439
Feels good to be out again, honestly.

02:33:07.439 --> 02:33:13.200
You drink deeply, savoring the flavor, but
you almost choke when you see the man standing

02:33:13.200 --> 02:33:13.859
in the corner.

02:33:13.859 --> 02:33:19.559
He’s so large and so distinctive, it surprises
you that you hadn’t noticed him before now.

02:33:19.560 --> 02:33:24.960
He stands in the corner, a freakishly tall
and muscular guy - like a basketball player

02:33:24.960 --> 02:33:27.180
who decided to become a pro bodybuilder.

02:33:27.180 --> 02:33:32.701
His muscular arms are bulging out of his white
vest, and a pair of bull’s horns are tattooed

02:33:32.700 --> 02:33:37.139
across the top of his bald head, making him
look like the devil made flesh.

02:33:37.140 --> 02:33:42.781
He stares at you with a subdued kind of annoyance,
as if to say that you’re not in real danger

02:33:42.780 --> 02:33:48.120
quite yet, but if he wanted, he could grab
you and twist your head off like a bottlecap.

02:33:48.120 --> 02:33:52.080
“What’s with the huge guy?” you ask
us, more than a little concern in your voice.

02:33:52.080 --> 02:33:55.439
“Oh, him?” we reply with a smirk.

02:33:55.439 --> 02:33:57.059
“He comes with the anomaly.

02:33:57.060 --> 02:34:03.360
He appears in every SCP-1893 experience to
an extent, though his level of involvement

02:34:03.359 --> 02:34:04.019
varies.

02:34:04.020 --> 02:34:10.320
If SCP-1893 doesn’t perceive you as an annoyance
or a threat, then you’re good to go.

02:34:10.319 --> 02:34:15.780
But if 1893 starts to feel like you’re gonna
cause it some problems, then the guy with

02:34:15.780 --> 02:34:18.120
the horn tattoos is gonna intervene.

02:34:18.120 --> 02:34:19.500
Speaking of which…”

02:34:19.500 --> 02:34:25.290
You look up, and see that the giant man is
now standing next to you, brow furrowed in

02:34:25.290 --> 02:34:26.100
visible rage.

02:34:26.100 --> 02:34:31.320
He picks up your drink, and crushes the glass
in his hand without flinching, dripping booze

02:34:31.319 --> 02:34:32.700
and blood onto the counter.

02:34:32.700 --> 02:34:36.300
He snarls, “I think you’ve had enough,
buddy.

02:34:36.300 --> 02:34:39.720
Now it’s time for you to leave, or we’re
gonna have to get physical.

02:34:39.720 --> 02:34:40.440
Understand?”

02:34:40.439 --> 02:34:42.839
You don’t need to be told twice.

02:34:42.840 --> 02:34:47.880
You grab your hat, get up, and leave the bar,
abandoning us on our lonely stool.

02:34:47.880 --> 02:34:50.940
But our next Infohazard still awaits…

02:34:50.939 --> 02:34:52.259
You like poetry?

02:34:52.260 --> 02:34:54.480
Japanese poetry, yes?

02:34:55.200 --> 02:34:56.880
The humble haiku

02:34:56.880 --> 02:35:01.680
It’s dear Nine Three One
A unique infohazard

02:35:01.680 --> 02:35:03.900
It’s so poetic

02:35:03.899 --> 02:35:07.019
Though specifically
It takes the form of haiku

02:35:07.020 --> 02:35:08.520
So, what does that mean?

02:35:08.520 --> 02:35:12.300
A rigid structure
The first line, five syllables

02:35:12.300 --> 02:35:14.340
Then seven, then five

02:35:14.340 --> 02:35:18.180
We can’t talk about this
In ways other than haiku

02:35:18.180 --> 02:35:19.560
It is challenging

02:35:19.560 --> 02:35:23.640
Object class is safe
It is kept at Site-19

02:35:23.640 --> 02:35:25.560
Need third tier clearance

02:35:25.560 --> 02:35:27.600
So, what is this thing?

02:35:27.600 --> 02:35:31.800
SCP Nine Thirty-One
It is a rice bowl

02:35:31.800 --> 02:35:35.520
White, with a blue band,
And a crackled blue pattern

02:35:35.520 --> 02:35:37.440
All inside the bowl

02:35:37.439 --> 02:35:41.099
And we must confess
We took that one from the file

02:35:41.100 --> 02:35:42.900
Man, haikus are hard

02:35:42.899 --> 02:35:46.679
Three inches in height,
Four point five inches across.

02:35:46.680 --> 02:35:48.241
(Metric doesn’t fit)

02:35:48.240 --> 02:35:51.840
No makers’ marks found;
Suspected to have been made

02:35:51.840 --> 02:35:53.700
Late Nineteen Hundreds.

02:35:53.700 --> 02:35:57.300
Really makes you think
On the skill of these poets

02:35:57.300 --> 02:35:59.040
Sans anomalies

02:35:59.040 --> 02:36:03.120
Sure, it can’t kill you
But writing these drives you mad

02:36:03.120 --> 02:36:05.160
Curse Nine-Three-One

02:36:05.160 --> 02:36:09.059
Trapped in this rhyme scheme
Makes the Old Man’s Torture World

02:36:09.060 --> 02:36:12.840
Look like a resort
Okay let’s move on

02:36:12.840 --> 02:36:16.500
Other SCPs to see
We’re sick of Haiku

02:36:16.500 --> 02:36:18.180
Okay, back to normal.

02:36:18.180 --> 02:36:23.880
Time to shake off the structure of SCP-931,
and talk about another iconic infohazard:

02:36:23.880 --> 02:36:25.980
SCP-3007.

02:36:25.979 --> 02:36:31.439
This incurable infohazard is a lot less whimsical
than a rice bowl that forces you to write

02:36:31.439 --> 02:36:36.599
and speak in haiku, in fact, it’s literally
killed several people, and some in surprisingly

02:36:36.600 --> 02:36:37.741
gruesome ways.

02:36:37.740 --> 02:36:44.519
The main component of the Infohazard is known
as SCP-3007-1, this is an extremely vivid

02:36:44.520 --> 02:36:51.300
anomalous hallucination that affects those
under the 3007 umbrella, known as SCP-3007-2.

02:36:51.300 --> 02:36:55.260
To be afflicted with SCP-3007&nbsp;
is a truly horrifying&nbsp;

02:36:55.260 --> 02:36:56.880
and debilitating condition.

02:36:56.880 --> 02:37:02.640
The hallucinations occur an average of four
times a day, with each episode lasting for

02:37:02.640 --> 02:37:08.400
as long as an hour - and during these episodes,
the victims are at risk of grievous bodily

02:37:08.399 --> 02:37:10.139
harm, or even death.

02:37:10.140 --> 02:37:16.020
So the question now is: What exactly is the
SCP-3007-1 hallucination?

02:37:16.020 --> 02:37:21.000
To the people experiencing it, they appear
to be transported to a strange, alien world

02:37:21.000 --> 02:37:25.920
consisting of a huge number of white towers
or pillars, stretching into the sky.

02:37:25.920 --> 02:37:32.100
SCP-3007-2 specimens are trapped on a series
of bridges, incredibly far off the ground,

02:37:32.100 --> 02:37:34.260
that connect these various structures.

02:37:34.260 --> 02:37:38.640
This anomalous area is known as SCP-3007-3.

02:37:38.640 --> 02:37:44.281
It’s important to remember that people transported
to this world still remain, physically, in

02:37:44.280 --> 02:37:44.639
our own.

02:37:44.640 --> 02:37:50.940
However, any damage sustained with SCP-3007-3
will carry over into our own reality.

02:37:50.939 --> 02:37:56.339
To give one particularly gruesome example,
some people fall from the precarious bridges

02:37:56.340 --> 02:37:59.940
and tumble to their deaths in SCP-3007-3.

02:37:59.939 --> 02:38:05.339
Back in our reality, they suddenly explode
from the damage of an invisible high-speed

02:38:05.340 --> 02:38:07.620
impact, killing them instantly.

02:38:07.620 --> 02:38:12.960
There’s much more to SCP-3007, enough that
it probably warrants its own explanation,

02:38:12.960 --> 02:38:18.420
and the SCP Foundation takes it extremely
seriously, believing that, if the infohazard

02:38:18.420 --> 02:38:23.640
is allowed to breach containment and become
contagious, it could result in an XK-Class

02:38:23.640 --> 02:38:25.260
End of the World Scenario.

02:38:25.260 --> 02:38:31.680
As a result, anyone found to be infected by
SCP-3007 is contained and summarily terminated

02:38:31.680 --> 02:38:33.600
to reduce the risk of it spreading.

02:38:33.600 --> 02:38:40.320
To make things even worse, there are also
concerns about SCP-3007-3 seeping into our

02:38:40.319 --> 02:38:47.819
reality, as those standing within a two-meter
range of SCP-3007-2 during a 3007-1 episode

02:38:47.819 --> 02:38:52.139
can actually hear the sounds from the terrifying
hallucinatory reality.

02:38:52.140 --> 02:38:55.380
Okay, that was a little scary.

02:38:55.380 --> 02:38:59.160
How about instead of talking about falling
to your death without falling at all, we talk

02:38:59.160 --> 02:39:00.120
about a nice movie.

02:39:00.120 --> 02:39:04.859
Goncharov, by Martin Scorsese, one of the
best gangster movies of all time.

02:39:04.859 --> 02:39:07.080
What, you’ve never heard of Goncharov?

02:39:07.080 --> 02:39:11.460
It’s got everything - action, suspense,
romance, a mountain of black thorns, on which

02:39:11.460 --> 02:39:13.620
lives a dark tyrant of terrible and unknowable
power.

02:39:13.620 --> 02:39:15.780
You’re sure you haven’t seen Goncharov?

02:39:15.780 --> 02:39:20.519
Well, here’s the thing, all signs point
to movies like Goncharov and many others simply

02:39:20.520 --> 02:39:21.480
not existing.

02:39:21.479 --> 02:39:26.519
This comes as a result of&nbsp;
SCP-2747, an infohazardous&nbsp;

02:39:26.520 --> 02:39:28.440
phenomenon that causes people to talk about

02:39:28.439 --> 02:39:30.540
works of fiction that don’t exist.

02:39:30.540 --> 02:39:36.300
These works often feature commonalities, like
an ethereal or disturbing tone, ambiguity,

02:39:36.300 --> 02:39:40.020
black thorns, and a sinister,&nbsp;
mysterious antagonist.

02:39:40.020 --> 02:39:46.260
The Foundation is doing all they can to hunt
down and suppress SCP-2747, but it’s proving

02:39:46.260 --> 02:39:48.000
more difficult than they’d imagined.

02:39:48.000 --> 02:39:52.319
Currently, the leading hypothesis is that
these tales may have actually existed once,

02:39:52.319 --> 02:39:57.479
but were erased from reality, leaving only
the residue of memory and the odd scrap of

02:39:57.479 --> 02:39:58.259
evidence around.

02:39:58.260 --> 02:40:05.040
Many researchers speculate that the various
pieces that form SCP-2747 are anafabula, pieces

02:40:05.040 --> 02:40:09.359
of fiction accidentally composed with the
perfect elements to cause them to quite literally

02:40:09.359 --> 02:40:11.280
erase themselves over time.

02:40:11.280 --> 02:40:16.620
Now the greatest concern that the Foundation
has about these anafabulas is that they might

02:40:16.620 --> 02:40:21.000
actually be one, and their reality is on the
precipice of collapse.

02:40:21.000 --> 02:40:27.120
But we really don’t have time to unpack
that right now, and like SCP-3007, a full

02:40:27.120 --> 02:40:31.680
explanation of this anomaly would take some
time and is probably best tackled on its own.

02:40:31.680 --> 02:40:34.620
But there you have it, folks: Infohazards.

02:40:34.620 --> 02:40:39.420
They say that knowing is half the battle,
but in this case, it’s the whole battle,

02:40:39.420 --> 02:40:41.819
and if you know, you lose!

02:40:41.819 --> 02:40:46.500
Not really a battle at all come to think of
it… more of a trap.

02:40:46.500 --> 02:40:51.720
But whether it’s a vicious mega-fish, a
strangely buff man with bull tattoos, a poetic

02:40:51.720 --> 02:40:57.840
rice bowl, or a nightmarish ordeal of daily
hallucinations, there’s no doubt that Infohazards

02:40:57.840 --> 02:41:02.340
are some of the most strange and fascinating
anomalies that the Foundation has to offer.

02:41:02.340 --> 02:41:09.840
Oh, and of course, how could we forget the
most well-known Infohazard of all: SCP-2521.

02:41:09.840 --> 02:41:13.260
This entity is so infohazardous&nbsp;
that its Foundation&nbsp;

02:41:13.260 --> 02:41:15.600
file entry is written in pictograms.

02:41:15.600 --> 02:41:21.540
This is because, whenever information is recorded
about this entity, it manifests and steals

02:41:21.540 --> 02:41:21.780
it.

02:41:21.780 --> 02:41:24.059
If you write it down, it’ll take the paper.

02:41:24.060 --> 02:41:27.661
If you make a note of it on a computer, it’ll
take the computer.

02:41:27.660 --> 02:41:32.040
And of course, if you talk about it, it’ll-
Oh no, not again!

02:41:38.640 --> 02:41:38.701
Ahhhh!

02:41:38.700 --> 02:41:43.200
Phew, that was a close one, but I’m ok,
for now at least.

02:41:43.200 --> 02:41:49.620
Agent Carla Mendoza was one of the best field
agents that Site 41 had ever seen.

02:41:49.620 --> 02:41:55.019
She was professional, cool under pressure,
and when the situation demanded it, she could

02:41:55.020 --> 02:41:56.520
be a straight-up badass.

02:41:56.520 --> 02:42:01.920
During a Chaos Insurgency raid on the Site,
she’d single handedly killed four different

02:42:01.920 --> 02:42:05.580
insurgents - the last one with her bare hands.

02:42:05.580 --> 02:42:10.439
During containment breaches, she’d always
be the first one charging into the fray, her

02:42:10.439 --> 02:42:13.559
Foundation standard-issue Beretta drawn and
ready to fire.

02:42:13.560 --> 02:42:18.900
Agent Mendoza was so devoted to the job that
she took up the Site Director’s offer to

02:42:18.899 --> 02:42:24.359
start living onsite, so she could always be
there to help if an emergency situation unfolded.

02:42:24.359 --> 02:42:30.359
After all, when it all hits the fan, you want
someone as utterly unshakeable as Agent Mendoza

02:42:30.359 --> 02:42:31.200
on your side.

02:42:31.200 --> 02:42:35.939
The job had thrown the worst of the worst
at her, and she’d never even flinched.

02:42:35.939 --> 02:42:39.779
So surely, nothing could scare Agent Mendoza,
right?

02:42:39.780 --> 02:42:40.500
Right?

02:42:40.500 --> 02:42:45.720
After a long day of kicking ass, taking names,
and filling in the properly mandated amount

02:42:45.720 --> 02:42:51.540
of SCP Foundation debriefing paperwork, Agent
Mendoza retired to her Site 41 quarters.

02:42:51.540 --> 02:42:57.180
She felt exhausted and sweaty, so before heading
to bed to watch some wonderful SCP Explained

02:42:57.180 --> 02:43:01.260
videos on her phone, she decided to take a
quick shower.

02:43:01.260 --> 02:43:04.020
The last thing she expected&nbsp;
was for this particular&nbsp;

02:43:04.020 --> 02:43:08.281
shower to become...well, let’s say “Hitchcockian.”

02:43:08.280 --> 02:43:12.840
The water was running, hot and clean, filling
the air with steam.

02:43:12.840 --> 02:43:18.600
Agent Mendoza was lathering up her hair when
she first heard the noise: Heavy, wheezing

02:43:18.600 --> 02:43:21.960
breaths coming from just behind the shower
curtain.

02:43:21.960 --> 02:43:27.480
The second she heard it, Agent Mendoza felt
a kind of brutal, crushing anxiety that she’d

02:43:27.479 --> 02:43:28.740
never experienced before.

02:43:28.740 --> 02:43:33.719
Like a hand was reaching into her chest, and
squeezing her heart.

02:43:33.720 --> 02:43:38.340
The self-defense training that’d been encoded
into her muscle memory over years of working

02:43:38.340 --> 02:43:40.080
at the Foundation kicked into effect.

02:43:40.080 --> 02:43:46.080
In a blind panic, she struck out at the shower
curtain, causing it to sway outwards - and

02:43:46.080 --> 02:43:49.559
land directly on the face of Mendoza’s wheezing
voyeur.

02:43:49.560 --> 02:43:56.040
Who or whatever it was, it was standing right
there, less than a meter away from the shower.

02:43:56.040 --> 02:43:59.640
That wheezing carved into Mendoza’s ears
like a butcher’s knife.

02:43:59.640 --> 02:44:02.640
What an awful, monstrous sound.

02:44:02.640 --> 02:44:07.860
And despite the fact that the shower curtain
obscured its face, she could still somehow

02:44:07.859 --> 02:44:13.139
see it, the way a defenseless animal can sense
an approaching predator without ever locking

02:44:13.140 --> 02:44:18.060
eyes on it - and just somehow know that it’s
too late for them to escape now.

02:44:18.060 --> 02:44:23.460
Every training session, every achievement,
every piece of battle-hardening experience

02:44:23.460 --> 02:44:27.660
- it all evaporated in the presence of that
thing.

02:44:27.660 --> 02:44:31.380
Mendoza was so terrified, she might as well
have been a child.

02:44:31.380 --> 02:44:37.319
The monster just stood there beyond the curtain,
its raw, fleshy face parted into a freakishly

02:44:37.319 --> 02:44:39.120
wide, yellow-toothed grin.

02:44:39.120 --> 02:44:44.760
She didn’t know how, but on some deep, primal
level, she was aware that if this thing got

02:44:44.760 --> 02:44:49.140
its hands on her, something horrific beyond
description would happen to her.

02:44:49.140 --> 02:44:53.220
She was too terrified to even move a muscle
in its presence.

02:44:53.220 --> 02:44:58.741
She remained like that, standing in the shower
and sobbing quietly, for the next three solid

02:44:58.740 --> 02:45:01.740
hours until the creature finally disappeared.

02:45:01.740 --> 02:45:06.420
When her colleagues found her, she’d experienced
moderate scalding wounds from the hot water

02:45:06.420 --> 02:45:07.260
of the shower.

02:45:07.260 --> 02:45:12.060
It took another several hours for Agent Mendoza
to compose herself enough to share her story.

02:45:12.060 --> 02:45:17.481
A couple of days later, Tim Ellis, a junior-level
filing clerk, was found trapped in a Site

02:45:17.480 --> 02:45:18.660
41 supply closet.

02:45:18.660 --> 02:45:24.240
He’d urinated in his Foundation-issue slacks,
and was in a state of borderline catatonia.

02:45:24.240 --> 02:45:29.219
When his superiors asked him why he’d been
spending two hours in a supply closet on company

02:45:29.220 --> 02:45:34.140
time, he reported that it was because a monster
had appeared outside the door when he was

02:45:34.140 --> 02:45:36.000
searching for a replacement stapler.

02:45:36.000 --> 02:45:41.520
Despite never actually opening the door to
see what was outside or call for help - Mr.

02:45:41.520 --> 02:45:45.900
Ellis said that he felt as though he would
have had a heart attack if he actually opened

02:45:45.899 --> 02:45:49.920
that accursed door - he was able to provide
a clear description of the monster.

02:45:49.920 --> 02:45:53.399
He said it was tall and&nbsp;
emaciated, with reddish-brown&nbsp;

02:45:53.399 --> 02:45:56.280
skin that made it seem almost burnt or rotten.

02:45:56.280 --> 02:46:01.920
While it stood there and waited beyond the
supply closet door, it let out the most awful

02:46:01.920 --> 02:46:05.760
wheezing noise, like an old, rusty Iron Lung.

02:46:05.760 --> 02:46:12.120
But the image that Ellis seemed most fixated
on was the monster’s face, or lack thereof:

02:46:12.120 --> 02:46:18.180
Just a huge, grinning mouth that covered up
its entire head, stocked with an arsenal of

02:46:18.180 --> 02:46:19.500
massive, yellow teeth.

02:46:19.500 --> 02:46:22.680
Ellis was visibly shivering as he talked about
it.

02:46:22.680 --> 02:46:29.460
Two incidents are an unpleasant coincidence,
but three are a bonafide pattern, and it didn’t

02:46:29.460 --> 02:46:35.340
take long for more sightings of this strange
new anomaly - dubbed SCP-303, or The Doorman

02:46:35.340 --> 02:46:37.440
- to pop up across the site.

02:46:37.439 --> 02:46:42.479
It earned that name by always appearing behind
some kind of doorway, or at least a movable

02:46:42.479 --> 02:46:45.839
divider, in the case of Agent Mendoza’s
shower curtain.

02:46:45.840 --> 02:46:51.120
Whenever it appeared outside a doorway, nearby
Foundation personnel would report being struck

02:46:51.120 --> 02:46:55.800
with a sudden paralyzing terror that made
engaging with the creature impossible.

02:46:55.800 --> 02:47:00.660
Attempts to call for help were also often
stifled, as the very presence of the Doorman

02:47:00.660 --> 02:47:03.059
causes disruptions to electrical equipment.

02:47:03.060 --> 02:47:08.460
Whenever The Doorman manifests in your proximity,
it’s safe to say that it’ll be commanding

02:47:08.460 --> 02:47:10.859
your absolute, undivided attention.

02:47:10.859 --> 02:47:16.380
This was a particularly frightening case for
the SCP Foundation because it was one of the

02:47:16.380 --> 02:47:19.440
few anomalies bringing the fight directly
to them.

02:47:19.439 --> 02:47:25.379
Most sentient anomalous beings would do anything
to avoid getting captured by the SCP Foundation

02:47:25.380 --> 02:47:30.540
and contained in one of their high-security
sites, full of experienced researchers and

02:47:30.540 --> 02:47:34.439
state-of-the-art equipment designed specifically
to neutralize their effects.

02:47:34.439 --> 02:47:40.080
The Doorman, however, just seemed to take
this as a challenge, turning even the most

02:47:40.080 --> 02:47:44.580
hardcore personnel on the site into gibbering
wrecks with its mere presence.

02:47:44.580 --> 02:47:48.000
But The Doorman was just getting started.

02:47:48.000 --> 02:47:51.000
Agent Henderson had a frightening encounter
in the break room.

02:47:51.000 --> 02:47:55.560
He was pulling a long shift, and just wanted
to grab some coffee creamer from the cabinet.

02:47:55.560 --> 02:48:00.241
However, as he approached the cabinet, he
heard the telltale wheezing, and that terrible,

02:48:00.240 --> 02:48:02.819
overwhelming terror set in once more.

02:48:02.819 --> 02:48:09.240
The Doorman was sitting inside the cabinet
in the fetal position, he just knew it.

02:48:09.240 --> 02:48:14.639
Could this thing really just appear anywhere
it pleased, and keep people in or out until

02:48:14.640 --> 02:48:17.580
it decided to dematerialize and torment somebody
else?

02:48:17.580 --> 02:48:22.859
When the creature finally dematerialized and
the cabinet was examined, the coffee creamer

02:48:22.859 --> 02:48:26.759
was found to be missing, leaving Agent Henderson
distraught.

02:48:26.760 --> 02:48:32.100
This was the first recorded instance of The
Doorman stealing a physical item, but it would

02:48:32.100 --> 02:48:33.360
be far from the last.

02:48:33.359 --> 02:48:38.040
Henderson wondered whether the creature that’d
just humiliated him was sitting somewhere

02:48:38.040 --> 02:48:43.800
else now, sipping from a warm cup of joe with
its big, freakish mouth and laughing at him.

02:48:43.800 --> 02:48:50.040
But a few incidents after this, things would
become considerably more serious: The Doorman

02:48:50.040 --> 02:48:52.140
was about to take its first life.

02:48:52.140 --> 02:48:56.940
Well, it isn’t really that simple, if you
want to get into the semantics of the thing.

02:48:56.939 --> 02:49:01.919
When the body of Dr. Barker was found inside
the 2nd-floor storage room after a spree of

02:49:01.920 --> 02:49:07.440
SCP-303 incidents, the question was naturally
posed as to whether The Doorman had gotten

02:49:07.439 --> 02:49:11.099
more dangerous and finally directly attacked
one of its victims.

02:49:11.100 --> 02:49:12.300
Not quite.

02:49:12.300 --> 02:49:17.580
There had only been one way in and out of
the storage room: A secured decompression

02:49:17.580 --> 02:49:23.040
chamber, and the Doorman had appeared inside
this chamber while Dr. Barker was in the storage

02:49:23.040 --> 02:49:28.260
room, effectively trapping him inside with
the sheer terror it causes in its victims.

02:49:28.260 --> 02:49:33.180
He was trapped in the room for a grand total
of five days, at which point he finally died

02:49:33.180 --> 02:49:37.500
of dehydration, and the Doorman demanifested
shortly afterward.

02:49:37.500 --> 02:49:40.439
The staff of Site 41 scaled&nbsp;
up their countermeasure&nbsp;

02:49:40.439 --> 02:49:43.319
efforts, hoping to discover more about and

02:49:43.319 --> 02:49:46.259
perhaps even trap and contain the infamous
Doorman.

02:49:46.260 --> 02:49:52.980
Dr. Burroughs, Researcher Matthews, four members
of security personnel, and four D-Class operatives

02:49:52.979 --> 02:49:58.259
formed a kind of strike team, ready for quick
dispatches whenever The Doorman happened to

02:49:58.260 --> 02:49:58.800
manifest.

02:49:58.800 --> 02:50:03.480
It wasn’t long before the creature appeared
in a room on the first floor, but the team

02:50:03.479 --> 02:50:08.280
quickly intercepted its location, ready and
eager to gather more data on the mysterious

02:50:08.280 --> 02:50:10.979
being that’d been terrorizing all of them
for weeks.

02:50:10.979 --> 02:50:15.839
Dr. Burroughs ordered one of the D-Classes
to open the door and look inside, but the

02:50:15.840 --> 02:50:17.460
D-Class refused out of fear.

02:50:17.460 --> 02:50:22.260
The doctor told him that if he didn’t open
the door, he’d be transferred to SCP-682

02:50:22.260 --> 02:50:22.800
duty.

02:50:22.800 --> 02:50:26.580
The D-Class frantically shook his head and
said, “I’d rather take my chances with

02:50:26.580 --> 02:50:27.780
the reptile than go in there.”

02:50:27.780 --> 02:50:29.580
The doctor was getting frustrated.

02:50:29.580 --> 02:50:34.080
He told the D-Class that if he didn’t open
the door immediately, he’d be terminated

02:50:34.080 --> 02:50:35.519
right there on the spot.

02:50:35.520 --> 02:50:40.440
The D-Class still refused, saying that he’d
take death over what the Doorman would do

02:50:40.439 --> 02:50:42.359
to him if he stepped inside.

02:50:42.359 --> 02:50:46.620
Without hesitation, Dr. Burroughs ordered
one of the security officers to shoot the

02:50:46.620 --> 02:50:47.760
D-Class then and there.

02:50:47.760 --> 02:50:49.500
The shot was fired.

02:50:49.500 --> 02:50:51.240
The D-Class was terminated.

02:50:51.240 --> 02:50:55.979
Dr. Burroughs then ordered a female D-Class
who’d just witnessed this callous execution

02:50:55.979 --> 02:50:59.639
to open the door, or the same abrupt death
would befall her.

02:50:59.640 --> 02:51:04.500
She still refused, then began to describe
the awful things she believed The Doorman

02:51:04.500 --> 02:51:06.300
would do to her if she went inside.

02:51:06.300 --> 02:51:09.840
Researcher Matthews was visibly shaken by
the descriptions.

02:51:09.840 --> 02:51:13.620
Dr. Burroughs decided not to terminate this
D-Class immediately.

02:51:13.620 --> 02:51:18.840
He instead wanted to see just how much pressure
the Doorman’s anomalous fear-based resistance

02:51:18.840 --> 02:51:20.100
mechanisms could take.

02:51:20.100 --> 02:51:25.260
Another D-Class was given a combat knife and
also given the order to cut the female D-Class

02:51:25.260 --> 02:51:28.020
with it every time she refused an order to
go inside.

02:51:28.020 --> 02:51:33.541
After two hours of repeated asking from Dr.
Burroughs, the female D-Class dropped dead

02:51:33.540 --> 02:51:34.500
from blood loss.

02:51:34.500 --> 02:51:38.160
At no point did she ever attempt to open the
door.

02:51:38.160 --> 02:51:43.500
It seemed that, in all cases for those in
the thrall of the Doorman’s anomalous effects,

02:51:43.500 --> 02:51:47.939
death is a truly preferable alternative to
ever facing it head-on.

02:51:47.939 --> 02:51:53.099
It’s worth mentioning that these tests were
conducted back in the 1970s, before the formation

02:51:53.100 --> 02:51:55.500
of the Foundation’s Ethics Committee, which&nbsp;

02:51:55.500 --> 02:51:58.200
explains why their methods&nbsp;
feel a little needlessly

02:51:58.200 --> 02:51:58.679
cruel.

02:51:58.680 --> 02:52:03.660
Since then, The Doorman has fully commandeered
the second-floor storage room, the same one

02:52:03.660 --> 02:52:05.580
where it caused Dr. Barker’s death.

02:52:05.580 --> 02:52:09.359
It only ever leaves the room to steal more
items from around the site.

02:52:09.359 --> 02:52:14.399
These items have included a cryotube, three
sets of standard Foundation surgical equipment,

02:52:14.399 --> 02:52:18.000
two D-Class research&nbsp;
cadavers, one gasoline-powered&nbsp;

02:52:18.000 --> 02:52:20.100
generator, a variety of chemicals from the

02:52:20.100 --> 02:52:25.380
chemical storage areas, and of course, poor
Agent Henderson’s can of powdered coffee

02:52:25.380 --> 02:52:25.920
creamer.

02:52:25.920 --> 02:52:30.540
The reason for the Doorman taking an interest
in these particular items remains unknown,

02:52:30.540 --> 02:52:33.840
but we can only assume that nothing good can
come of it.

02:52:33.840 --> 02:52:38.520
And there you have it, folks, the strange,
frightening, and eerily inconclusive tale

02:52:38.520 --> 02:52:39.480
of The Doorman.

02:52:39.479 --> 02:52:43.979
All we can really say is that we’re awfully
glad he’s fixated on bothering Site 41,

02:52:43.979 --> 02:52:48.240
because who knows what would happen if he
widened his net to the rest of us?

02:52:48.240 --> 02:52:50.700
Thankfully, we won’t need to think about
that.

02:52:50.700 --> 02:52:51.840
Oh, that’s odd.

02:52:51.840 --> 02:52:52.920
Can you hear that?

02:52:52.920 --> 02:52:54.300
I thought I was imagining it.

02:52:54.300 --> 02:52:57.600
Though come to think of it, I can’t help
but feel a little uneasy right now.

02:52:57.600 --> 02:53:00.360
Do you ever get that feeling you’re being
watched?

02:53:00.359 --> 02:53:02.880
Wait...The door, there’s something behind
the door.

02:53:02.880 --> 02:53:03.960
Can you feel it?

02:53:03.960 --> 02:53:09.720
Can you feel its red flesh and rotten teeth
pressing up against it, breathing, waiting?

02:53:09.720 --> 02:53:12.180
Can you feel it staring at you without eyes?

02:53:12.180 --> 02:53:14.580
Looking deep into your very soul?

02:53:14.580 --> 02:53:15.120
No?

02:53:15.120 --> 02:53:16.140
Well, that’s good.

02:53:16.140 --> 02:53:17.880
But just stay cautious, okay?

02:53:17.880 --> 02:53:24.840
After all, life has many doors, and you never
know who or what will be waiting for you behind

02:53:24.840 --> 02:53:25.620
the next one...&nbsp;

02:53:25.620 --> 02:53:30.420
Growing up in a small Virginia town near the
mountains, right on the border of West Virginia,

02:53:30.420 --> 02:53:33.960
Zane heard all kinds of&nbsp;
stories from his grandmother.

02:53:33.960 --> 02:53:37.500
Tales of mountain lions who could transform
into ghostly women.

02:53:37.500 --> 02:53:42.840
The tailypo, a fluffy rodent-like creature
on an endless quest to get its tail back from

02:53:42.840 --> 02:53:44.040
the hunter who took it.

02:53:44.040 --> 02:53:48.840
The Mothman that appeared with glowing red
eyes to warn of impending tragedy.

02:53:48.840 --> 02:53:51.840
Most of all, she warned him about the deer.

02:53:51.840 --> 02:53:57.060
"Sometimes," she used to say, "when you're
out in the woods late at night, you'll see

02:53:57.060 --> 02:53:58.860
a deer acting a little bit funny.

02:53:58.859 --> 02:54:01.080
Maybe it's making strange sounds.

02:54:01.080 --> 02:54:03.479
Maybe it's standing up like a man.

02:54:03.479 --> 02:54:06.959
Maybe it's staring at you from the shadows
and won't look away.

02:54:06.960 --> 02:54:11.700
If you ever see one of these deer, promise
me you'll get away from it as fast as possible.

02:54:11.700 --> 02:54:15.779
Don't look at it, don't talk to it, just get
far, far away."

02:54:15.779 --> 02:54:17.519
He promised her every time.

02:54:17.520 --> 02:54:22.741
But, as he got older, he started to forget
his grandma's stories, letting them fade away

02:54:22.740 --> 02:54:25.559
with memories of the Easter Bunny and Santa
Claus.

02:54:25.560 --> 02:54:31.320
He didn't think about the stories again until
he was older, a junior in college, and embarking

02:54:31.319 --> 02:54:33.420
on a camping trip with his roommate, Josh.

02:54:33.420 --> 02:54:37.920
They were both staying with Zane's family
for the summer, and had been enjoying the

02:54:37.920 --> 02:54:39.480
sunshine and fresh air.

02:54:39.479 --> 02:54:44.040
They'd gone hiking, picked blackberries, and
gone fishing to their hearts' content.

02:54:44.040 --> 02:54:48.840
After a while, they got sick of sleeping in
the cramped house and decided to have a proper

02:54:48.840 --> 02:54:50.819
camping trip out in the mountains.

02:54:50.819 --> 02:54:55.979
Campsites were crowded this time of year,
but Zane knew a spot just isolated enough

02:54:55.979 --> 02:55:00.000
that they could kick back, enjoy nature, and
relax in peace.

02:55:00.000 --> 02:55:04.080
They packed their supplies and headed out
into the forest for a weekend they would never

02:55:04.080 --> 02:55:04.380
forget.

02:55:04.380 --> 02:55:09.540
By nightfall, Zane and Josh had pitched their
tents, built a fire, and were starting to

02:55:09.540 --> 02:55:10.140
make some dinner.

02:55:10.140 --> 02:55:15.420
They roasted hot dogs and heated cans of beans
over the fire, and decided to start telling

02:55:15.420 --> 02:55:17.279
some classic scary stories.

02:55:17.279 --> 02:55:22.559
Sitting by the crackling fire, listening to
the rustling leaves, snapping twigs, and the

02:55:22.560 --> 02:55:27.360
chittering of animals all around, Zane couldn't
help but remember the stories he had almost

02:55:27.359 --> 02:55:28.080
forgotten.

02:55:28.080 --> 02:55:34.140
All of the strange, inexplicable things that
came out after the sun went down and the forest

02:55:34.140 --> 02:55:34.980
went quiet.

02:55:34.979 --> 02:55:39.719
He thought he could hear the footsteps of
something walking by their campsite, circling

02:55:39.720 --> 02:55:39.960
them.

02:55:39.960 --> 02:55:42.240
But it was probably just his imagination.

02:55:42.240 --> 02:55:47.519
As Josh told stories about babysitters stalked
by killers and drivers picking up ghostly

02:55:47.520 --> 02:55:50.940
hitchhikers, Zane was thinking about the deer.

02:55:50.939 --> 02:55:56.519
He shuddered but shook it off, and after some
more stories and a few too many s'mores, the

02:55:56.520 --> 02:55:58.621
two friends decided to get some sleep.

02:55:58.620 --> 02:56:03.000
After several hours, Zane woke to the sound
of Josh unzipping his tent.

02:56:03.000 --> 02:56:07.500
He sat up, ready to yell at his friend for
waking him up, but the sight of Josh's pale,

02:56:07.500 --> 02:56:09.300
frightened face stopped him.

02:56:09.300 --> 02:56:11.880
"There's something here..." was all Josh could
say.

02:56:11.880 --> 02:56:14.940
His hands, Zane noticed, were shaking.

02:56:14.939 --> 02:56:16.620
"Hey man, it's okay.

02:56:16.620 --> 02:56:19.500
Let's check it out," Zane patted Josh on the
shoulder.

02:56:19.500 --> 02:56:24.359
He was pretty sure his friend just wasn't
used to camping in actual nature, but reached

02:56:24.359 --> 02:56:25.979
for his hunting knife just in case.

02:56:25.979 --> 02:56:30.899
He grabbed a flashlight, and switched it on,
following Josh out into the darkness.

02:56:30.899 --> 02:56:36.179
He swept the beam across the clearing, and
it illuminated a pair of orange eyes staring

02:56:36.180 --> 02:56:38.880
directly at him from behind a nearby tree.

02:56:38.880 --> 02:56:42.960
"What the..." he approached the shape, trying
to get a clear look at it.

02:56:42.960 --> 02:56:46.380
As it became more illuminated, his stomach
dropped.

02:56:46.380 --> 02:56:50.100
It was a deer, but something was...wrong with
it.

02:56:50.100 --> 02:56:55.440
Its mouth was wide open, its jaw working up
and down like it was trying to make a sound,

02:56:55.439 --> 02:56:57.000
but nothing came out.

02:56:57.000 --> 02:56:59.040
But that wasn't the worst part.

02:56:59.040 --> 02:57:05.160
As the flashlight beam illuminated the animal's
body, Zane realized that, somehow, its head

02:57:05.160 --> 02:57:06.599
was on backwards.

02:57:06.600 --> 02:57:09.720
"What the-" Josh appeared behind him, gasping.

02:57:09.720 --> 02:57:10.620
"Shh!"

02:57:10.620 --> 02:57:12.420
Zane shushed him intensely.

02:57:12.420 --> 02:57:14.819
He suddenly remembered his grandmother's warnings.

02:57:14.819 --> 02:57:15.719
"You know what?

02:57:15.720 --> 02:57:16.741
I don't feel so great.

02:57:16.740 --> 02:57:18.779
I think we should go back to the car and head
to my place."

02:57:18.779 --> 02:57:22.859
He gave Josh a look, shaking his head as if
to say "don't say another word."

02:57:22.859 --> 02:57:27.359
By the glow of their flashlights, the two
packed up their campsite, all under the gaze

02:57:27.359 --> 02:57:28.679
of the misshapen deer.

02:57:28.680 --> 02:57:34.320
They drove home in silence, Josh only speaking
once to ask: "What was that thing?"

02:57:34.319 --> 02:57:35.639
Zane shook his head.

02:57:35.640 --> 02:57:36.661
"I don't know.

02:57:36.660 --> 02:57:38.220
But it wasn't a deer."

02:57:38.220 --> 02:57:40.680
They crept back into the house, and went to
bed.

02:57:40.680 --> 02:57:43.380
They knew they would never speak of tonight
ever again.

02:57:43.380 --> 02:57:48.840
As Zane began to drift off to sleep, his last
conscious thought was to glance out the window.

02:57:48.840 --> 02:57:52.860
There, in the yard not five feet away, was
a deer.

02:57:52.859 --> 02:57:53.939
Watching.

02:57:53.939 --> 02:58:00.419
He didn't know it, but that night Zane encountered
an instance of SCP-6448.

02:58:00.420 --> 02:58:07.200
SCP-6448 is an anomalous species of creatures
that appear to belong to the Cervidae family,

02:58:07.200 --> 02:58:09.479
nicknamed the "Not Deer."

02:58:09.479 --> 02:58:12.479
They are highly intelligent&nbsp;
and can be distinguished&nbsp;

02:58:12.479 --> 02:58:15.419
from ordinary deer by unusual behavior and

02:58:15.420 --> 02:58:16.500
physical deformities.

02:58:16.500 --> 02:58:21.779
Some of these have included: legs that bend
backwards, the eyes of animals other than

02:58:21.779 --> 02:58:28.439
deer, forward-facing eyes, jerky movements,
lack of fear toward humans, and walking on

02:58:28.439 --> 02:58:29.580
two hind legs.

02:58:29.580 --> 02:58:37.260
Most notably, and most frightening, SCP-6448
instances will watch and stalk humans, for

02:58:37.260 --> 02:58:39.360
a duration of hours or even days.

02:58:39.359 --> 02:58:44.819
They will follow humans home, and steal items
from their domains including weapons, food,

02:58:44.819 --> 02:58:46.679
and other personal items.

02:58:46.680 --> 02:58:51.480
They are most frequently found in the deep
woods at night, when a person is completely

02:58:51.479 --> 02:58:51.779
alone.

02:58:51.779 --> 02:58:58.259
If someone encounters an instance of SCP-6448,
if they acknowledge any of the creature's

02:58:58.260 --> 02:59:00.300
anomalous traits, it will attack.

02:59:00.300 --> 02:59:05.880
In order to limit the loss of life and ensure
that SCP Foundation employees exercise the

02:59:05.880 --> 02:59:12.420
utmost caution when dealing with SCP-6448,
the Cryptozoology Division issued the following

02:59:12.420 --> 02:59:13.020
guidelines:

02:59:13.020 --> 02:59:17.701
"If you notice a deer that seems “off”,
look away and ignore it.

02:59:17.700 --> 02:59:20.700
If it knows that you’ve noticed it, it’s
too late.

02:59:20.700 --> 02:59:26.220
If you hear your name, whistling, or something
else in the woods calling for you, don’t

02:59:26.220 --> 02:59:27.241
acknowledge it.

02:59:27.240 --> 02:59:33.840
Never acknowledge it exists, don’t respond,
don’t go looking for it, don’t call back

02:59:33.840 --> 02:59:34.200
to it.

02:59:34.200 --> 02:59:38.279
If you’re walking at night and you feel
something breathing on your neck or whispering

02:59:38.279 --> 02:59:42.540
behind you, the key to your safety is pretending
that everything is normal.

02:59:42.540 --> 02:59:46.260
Your survival is dependant on your ignorance."

02:59:46.260 --> 02:59:51.420
Whatever SCP-6448 is, they&nbsp;
appear to be intelligent&nbsp;

02:59:51.420 --> 02:59:54.120
enough to understand when they are being studied,

02:59:54.120 --> 02:59:56.460
and they don't seem to like it very much.

02:59:56.460 --> 03:00:04.980
On January 11, 1994, a group of three SCP-6448
instances broke into Site-41 in North Carolina,

03:00:04.979 --> 03:00:08.819
using a tunnel they had carved over a long
period of time.

03:00:08.819 --> 03:00:11.700
At that time, there was an&nbsp;
instance in containment,&nbsp;

03:00:11.700 --> 03:00:14.399
but in all of the chaos of the breach, the

03:00:14.399 --> 03:00:15.540
specimen was lost.

03:00:15.540 --> 03:00:22.140
Every time an instance was captured and contained
near SCP-6448's habitat, it would later escape

03:00:22.140 --> 03:00:23.880
via similar tunnels.

03:00:23.880 --> 03:00:31.080
SCP-6448 was officially classified by the
SCP Foundation in 1980, but those from the

03:00:31.080 --> 03:00:36.240
Appalachian region have known about these
strange creatures since at least 1947.

03:00:36.240 --> 03:00:42.660
From folktales and campfire stories to secondhand
and even firsthand encounters, the locals

03:00:42.660 --> 03:00:48.000
are well aware of the Not Deer's existence,
and are largely familiar with the precautions

03:00:48.000 --> 03:00:49.500
necessary to avoid them.

03:00:49.500 --> 03:00:55.319
Though many of the civilians that encounter
SCP-6448 avoid notifying the authorities,

03:00:55.319 --> 03:01:01.019
there have been several recorded 911 calls
involving the Not Deer since 2000.

03:01:01.020 --> 03:01:03.541
The following is a log of those calls:

03:01:03.540 --> 03:01:05.640
February 1, 2000:

03:01:05.640 --> 03:01:11.220
"Victim (aged 41, female) dialed emergency
services after hearing their name being called

03:01:11.220 --> 03:01:12.720
from the woods near their home.

03:01:12.720 --> 03:01:17.520
The victim recounts the vocalization being
likened to a scream in a voice that they do

03:01:17.520 --> 03:01:21.600
not recognize and requested assistance in
locating the source.

03:01:21.600 --> 03:01:26.040
Emergency personnel requested the subject
place their phone on the floor outside the

03:01:26.040 --> 03:01:28.019
home to listen for the alleged sounds.

03:01:28.020 --> 03:01:33.840
After 2 minutes, a vocalization was heard
that was calling to the subject by name, emanating

03:01:33.840 --> 03:01:35.040
from the nearby forest.

03:01:35.040 --> 03:01:35.340
&lrm;

03:01:35.340 --> 03:01:39.960
The subject was instructed to investigate
the disturbance themselves and keep services

03:01:39.960 --> 03:01:41.640
updated on the situation.

03:01:41.640 --> 03:01:47.100
The victim then begins to walk into the woodland,
getting about 50 meters into the underbrush

03:01:47.100 --> 03:01:48.900
before inexplicably stopping.

03:01:48.899 --> 03:01:53.580
They claim there to be a noticeably large
deer standing in the way of the path.

03:01:53.580 --> 03:01:57.300
She begins to walk closer, though states it
does not move.

03:01:57.300 --> 03:02:00.840
Subject diverts from the path and begins walking
in a different direction.

03:02:00.840 --> 03:02:04.800
After 30 minutes, no source of the voice is
determined.

03:02:04.800 --> 03:02:06.960
The caller returns to their residence."

03:02:06.960 --> 03:02:09.300
June 13, 2002:

03:02:09.300 --> 03:02:14.100
"Victim (aged 28, male) calls 911 regarding
a home break-in.

03:02:14.100 --> 03:02:16.741
The caller notes numerous items to be missing&nbsp;

03:02:16.740 --> 03:02:19.500
from their residence and&nbsp;
requests an investigation.

03:02:19.500 --> 03:02:25.979
Operators dispatch two investigators to visit
the home and pertain a potential perpetrator.

03:02:25.979 --> 03:02:32.279
The pair note that, based on earlier CCTV
images, all cutlery, sharp objects, firearms,

03:02:32.279 --> 03:02:37.019
lightbulbs, and a single copy of the novel
‘The Day After Roswell’ are missing.

03:02:37.020 --> 03:02:41.940
Also noted is that there is a complete lack
of any fingerprints at the scene, with no

03:02:41.939 --> 03:02:43.979
doors or windows having been broken into.

03:02:43.979 --> 03:02:49.859
Analysis of the home’s CCTV footage revealed
there to be a two hour period of missing film,

03:02:49.859 --> 03:02:55.620
with the exception of a single frame containing
a Cervus nippon on its hind legs, reaching

03:02:55.620 --> 03:02:56.340
towards the camera.

03:02:56.340 --> 03:02:59.520
Its frontal hooves have been warped to resemble
fingers.

03:02:59.520 --> 03:03:03.121
No footage of the entity exiting the home
was discovered."

03:03:03.120 --> 03:03:05.640
November 19, 2005:

03:03:05.640 --> 03:03:10.560
"A cattle farmer (aged 54, male) reported
to local authorities the sudden disappearance

03:03:10.560 --> 03:03:13.440
of over 30% of his largest herd.

03:03:13.439 --> 03:03:18.359
Response teams searched the nearby area for
4 hours though found no trace of the cattle.

03:03:18.359 --> 03:03:23.279
The victim was recommended to set up trail
cameras and note any unusual activity overnight.

03:03:23.279 --> 03:03:29.639
At 01:11 AM, two SCP-6448 are seen walking
through the field before fleeing.

03:03:29.640 --> 03:03:34.680
One places an object into the ground, later
discovered to be a single fork.

03:03:34.680 --> 03:03:39.900
A week after this discovery, 200 discarded
bovine hooves appear at the location."

03:03:39.899 --> 03:03:42.420
March 4, 2009:

03:03:42.420 --> 03:03:48.240
"Victim (age unknown, gender unknown) dials
911 to request assistance from animal services.

03:03:48.240 --> 03:03:53.819
The victim is standing within a forest in
front of a Cervus elaphus, which is violently

03:03:53.819 --> 03:03:54.599
contorting.

03:03:54.600 --> 03:03:58.800
The victim attempts to state "You better get
a vet or something, I don't think it's well"

03:03:58.800 --> 03:04:02.340
before a piercing screech is heard and the
line falls silent.

03:04:02.340 --> 03:04:06.840
Recovered footage depicts the aforementioned
animal squirming, seemingly in pain.

03:04:06.840 --> 03:04:12.480
A viscous churning is audible as a black mass
erupts out of the instance, and the video

03:04:12.479 --> 03:04:13.919
turns to static."

03:04:13.920 --> 03:04:16.020
October 11, 2012:

03:04:16.020 --> 03:04:21.720
"Victim (aged 23, male) is a junior wildlife
officer at Cherokee National Forest, Tennessee.

03:04:21.720 --> 03:04:27.480
They radio their supervisor in the early evening
regarding a herd of Odocoileus virginianus

03:04:27.479 --> 03:04:28.919
within the reserve.

03:04:28.920 --> 03:04:34.140
Supposedly, there is a single animal that,
upon first glance, appears average, though

03:04:34.140 --> 03:04:36.720
possesses divergent attributes, including&nbsp;

03:04:36.720 --> 03:04:40.200
backwards joints, enlarged&nbsp;
abdomen, and forward-facing

03:04:40.200 --> 03:04:40.559
eyes.

03:04:40.560 --> 03:04:45.540
Upon stating this, a distant whistle is audible,
and the victim stumbles slightly.

03:04:45.540 --> 03:04:49.140
They begin to say “What the he- did it just
whistle at me?”

03:04:49.140 --> 03:04:52.440
before the sound of hooves rapidly getting
closer is heard.

03:04:52.439 --> 03:04:57.059
Notably, the hoof steps did not sound to be
in the traditional gallop of a cervid."

03:04:57.060 --> 03:04:59.340
October 12, 2012:

03:04:59.340 --> 03:05:04.140
"The former victim’s supervisor calls authorities
following the victim’s absence from the

03:05:04.140 --> 03:05:05.100
reserve night shift.

03:05:05.100 --> 03:05:07.680
Following this, their radio begins to crackle.

03:05:07.680 --> 03:05:12.772
The victim’s voice can be heard on the other
end, and he requests the supervisor’s attention.

03:05:12.771 --> 03:05:17.099
&lrm; &lrm; He calls regarding a herd of Odocoileus
virginianus within the reserve.

03:05:17.100 --> 03:05:22.560
They claim there is a single animal that upon
first glance appears average, though possesses

03:05:22.560 --> 03:05:28.081
divergent attributes including backwards joints,
enlarged abdomen and forward facing eyes.

03:05:28.080 --> 03:05:33.479
Suspecting the creature to be a rare genetic
malformation, the victim requests their supervisor

03:05:33.479 --> 03:05:34.620
to come to the location.

03:05:34.620 --> 03:05:38.340
The supervisor questions the victim about
what happened the night previous.

03:05:38.340 --> 03:05:40.020
There is no reply.

03:05:40.020 --> 03:05:45.060
Upon the supervisor’s and law enforcement’s
arrival at the site, a herd of approximately

03:05:45.060 --> 03:05:47.581
80 Odocoileus virginianus was present.

03:05:47.580 --> 03:05:52.319
A single entity is in the field’s center
and appears to be standing separate from the

03:05:52.319 --> 03:05:52.920
rest of the group.

03:05:52.920 --> 03:05:56.460
It flees the scene upon realizing the law
enforcement’s presence.

03:05:56.460 --> 03:05:59.700
Where it formerly stood laid a standard two-way
radio."

03:05:59.700 --> 03:06:02.220
April 8, 2016:

03:06:02.220 --> 03:06:07.620
“Victim (aged 35, female) dials 911 using
a satellite phone, distressed.

03:06:07.620 --> 03:06:11.880
They state that they are in [REDACTED] County
Woods and are being followed.

03:06:11.880 --> 03:06:17.220
She claims that, despite seeing no one for
the duration of her hike, she “feels as

03:06:17.220 --> 03:06:21.720
if she’s being watched” and has heard
someone walking behind her at various points

03:06:21.720 --> 03:06:22.320
in the trip.

03:06:22.319 --> 03:06:24.660
The victim is unable to&nbsp;
give an adequate description&nbsp;

03:06:24.660 --> 03:06:27.300
of their location, but knows the route to

03:06:27.300 --> 03:06:28.500
return to her residence.

03:06:28.500 --> 03:06:32.939
Operators request the victim to return to
a point wherein she can provide a sufficient

03:06:32.939 --> 03:06:34.679
geographic description of her position.

03:06:34.680 --> 03:06:39.180
&lrm; The victim remains on the line for the
duration of the hike back to a readily used

03:06:39.180 --> 03:06:40.741
portion of the wilderness trail.

03:06:40.740 --> 03:06:44.279
Along the journey, various unnatural sounds
can be heard.

03:06:44.279 --> 03:06:49.380
These include footsteps, rockslides, coughing,
whispering, and whistling.

03:06:49.380 --> 03:06:54.960
Nearing the main trail, all woodland noises,
such as birds and wind, cease suddenly, and

03:06:54.960 --> 03:06:59.520
the victim states she can see a malformed
deer carcass coated in a thick layer of black

03:06:59.520 --> 03:06:59.940
slime.

03:06:59.939 --> 03:07:03.120
At this time, human screams can be heard in
the distance.

03:07:03.120 --> 03:07:07.140
Operators request the victim continue and
ignore other stimuli.

03:07:07.140 --> 03:07:13.680
Agents embedded in local law enforcement,
suspecting SCP-6448 involvement, notify Gamma-4

03:07:13.680 --> 03:07:14.640
to the situation.

03:07:14.640 --> 03:07:18.120
20 minutes later, the victim returns to the
main trail.

03:07:18.120 --> 03:07:23.939
Gamma-4, now operating the 911 call, informs
the victim not to respond to any further unusual

03:07:23.939 --> 03:07:26.759
activity and briefly outlines Cervus Protocol.

03:07:26.760 --> 03:07:31.560
For the duration of the victim’s journey
to her home, two sets of breathing are audible.

03:07:31.560 --> 03:07:35.820
The victim successfully returns to her residence
and shuts the door behind her.

03:07:35.819 --> 03:07:42.000
Now out of sight from SCP-6448, agents inquire
at the victim’s address, and the victim

03:07:42.000 --> 03:07:43.140
promptly complies.

03:07:43.140 --> 03:07:47.580
Operatives instruct the victim to have possession
of all firearms and weapons on the premises

03:07:47.580 --> 03:07:51.479
and to barricade herself inside a safe space
with one exit point.

03:07:51.479 --> 03:07:56.639
The victim swiftly begins grabbing all available
weapons and throwing them inside a wardrobe.

03:07:56.640 --> 03:07:59.340
It is at this time that there is a knock on
the front door.

03:07:59.340 --> 03:08:04.200
The victim does not respond and continues
to hoard sharp objects from kitchen drawers.

03:08:04.200 --> 03:08:09.000
The knocking becomes more violent as the handle
is jostled and shaken incessantly.

03:08:09.000 --> 03:08:13.740
A voice on the other side repeats the phrase
“Hello, it is me.

03:08:13.740 --> 03:08:15.479
Hello, let me in.”

03:08:15.479 --> 03:08:18.479
in a calm manner as the door begins to shake.

03:08:18.479 --> 03:08:22.139
The victim retreats to her wardrobe, armed
with a small firearm.

03:08:22.140 --> 03:08:27.420
Upon sealing herself in the space, the knocking
ceases, and footsteps can be heard becoming

03:08:27.420 --> 03:08:28.020
further away.

03:08:28.020 --> 03:08:31.621
The sound of galloping is audible as the front
door caves in.

03:08:31.620 --> 03:08:34.559
Hoof steps can now be heard inside the home.

03:08:34.560 --> 03:08:38.400
The entity continues to repeat “Hello, it
is me.

03:08:38.399 --> 03:08:40.200
Hello, let me in.”

03:08:40.200 --> 03:08:42.059
as it searches the small building.

03:08:42.060 --> 03:08:45.840
A bright light flashes overhead, seemingly
circling the house.

03:08:45.840 --> 03:08:48.420
Eventually, the entity enters the victim’s
bedroom.

03:08:48.420 --> 03:08:54.359
Through a small slit in the wardrobe door,
the victim can see a Cervus canadensis standing

03:08:54.359 --> 03:08:56.580
on its hind legs and surveying the room.

03:08:56.580 --> 03:09:02.220
Its movements are crooked and stiff, seeming
to struggle to stand in a bipedal fashion.

03:09:02.220 --> 03:09:07.380
It slouches down to a quadrupedal crouch,
similar to the stance of an arachnid.

03:09:07.380 --> 03:09:11.700
It inhales heavily, and its head locks on
the view of the wardrobe.

03:09:11.700 --> 03:09:13.920
It is noted as possessing human eyes.

03:09:13.920 --> 03:09:16.740
It scampers towards the subject and opens
the door.

03:09:16.740 --> 03:09:18.660
A single gunshot is heard.

03:09:18.660 --> 03:09:23.760
Responders found no trace of either SCP-6448
or the victim."

03:09:23.760 --> 03:09:29.700
Containment of SCP-6448 is focused on the
investigation of any deer exhibiting anomalous

03:09:29.700 --> 03:09:32.279
traits in and around the Appalachian area.

03:09:32.279 --> 03:09:39.000
Any civilian sightings of SCP-6888 are to
be handled by Mobile Task Force Gamma-4, or

03:09:39.000 --> 03:09:40.260
the "Green Stags".

03:09:40.260 --> 03:09:46.560
Any possible deaths resulting from SCP-6448
will be blamed on hiking accidents, and any

03:09:46.560 --> 03:09:50.100
reported sightings can be explained away with
Chronic Wasting Disease.

03:09:50.100 --> 03:09:56.460
CWD, occasionally referred to as "zombie deer
disease" is a prion disease affecting members

03:09:56.460 --> 03:09:57.720
of the Cervidae family.

03:09:57.720 --> 03:10:02.700
Symptoms of the illness include loss of motor
function control and damage to decision making,

03:10:02.700 --> 03:10:06.300
as well as gradual degradation of all mental
faculties.

03:10:06.300 --> 03:10:09.060
It is one hundred percent fatal.

03:10:09.060 --> 03:10:14.640
However, though the disease does exist, most
recorded cases of it in the Appalachian region

03:10:14.640 --> 03:10:19.080
can actually be attributed to instances of
SCP-6448.

03:10:19.080 --> 03:10:26.160
Any captured instances of SCP-6448 should
be transported to Site-44 for the Cryptozoology

03:10:26.160 --> 03:10:28.260
Division's containment and study.

03:10:28.260 --> 03:10:35.100
On November 29, 2019, they finally got their
chance to bring a Not Deer into custody.

03:10:35.100 --> 03:10:42.360
The Green Stags were able to capture an instance
of SCP-6448 with help from MTF Nu-7, "Hammer

03:10:42.359 --> 03:10:46.979
Down", and their heavy vehicles division,
as well as some experimental shock rifles.

03:10:46.979 --> 03:10:52.500
One Not Deer was knocked unconscious in the
conflict, and its body was loaded onto an

03:10:52.500 --> 03:10:56.939
armored helicopter and flown straight to Site-44
in Essex, England.

03:10:56.939 --> 03:11:02.099
At the site, it was then placed in a reinforced
steel containment cell, and heavily sedated.

03:11:02.100 --> 03:11:04.741
This entire process went off without a hitch.

03:11:04.740 --> 03:11:10.679
As the entity began to regain consciousness,
Cryptozoology Specialist F. Ozz watched it

03:11:10.680 --> 03:11:14.460
through a one-way glass window and attempted
to speak to it through the intercom.

03:11:14.460 --> 03:11:18.840
"Greetings, SCP-6448," Researcher Ozz began.

03:11:18.840 --> 03:11:22.920
At the sound of his voice, the creature jumped
to its feet, staring at the intercom.

03:11:22.920 --> 03:11:24.540
"Can you understand me?

03:11:24.540 --> 03:11:27.840
We've seen your genus speak English just fine
in the past."

03:11:27.840 --> 03:11:32.640
The animal did not answer, but began licking
one of its legs and behaving as if it were

03:11:32.640 --> 03:11:33.661
an ordinary deer.

03:11:33.660 --> 03:11:35.880
Researcher Ozz sighed impatiently.

03:11:35.880 --> 03:11:37.800
"Please, we know your secret."

03:11:37.800 --> 03:11:42.720
The Not Deer stopped what it was doing, freezing
completely still as it listened to his words.

03:11:42.720 --> 03:11:45.540
"Admittedly, it wasn't exactly well kept.

03:11:45.540 --> 03:11:49.620
If you'd just look at yourself for more than
a few seconds, it is very clear that you're

03:11:49.620 --> 03:11:50.819
not...normal."

03:11:50.819 --> 03:11:56.099
At this, the creature, which had been facing
away from the window, swiveled its neck 180

03:11:56.100 --> 03:11:59.340
degrees, breaking its own spine with an audible
crack.

03:11:59.340 --> 03:12:03.779
It stared, unblinking, at the window and directly
at Researcher Ozz.

03:12:03.779 --> 03:12:07.319
Ozz turned to the containment staff, suddenly
anxious.

03:12:07.319 --> 03:12:09.240
"I thought you said this was one-way?"

03:12:09.240 --> 03:12:14.219
The staff assured him that it was, and there
was no way the Not Deer could see him.

03:12:14.220 --> 03:12:17.100
Still, its eyes were locked directly on his
face.

03:12:17.100 --> 03:12:20.880
He shook off the sense of unease and continued
his line of questioning.

03:12:20.880 --> 03:12:23.460
"Are you something imitating deer?

03:12:23.460 --> 03:12:28.439
It is clear that, if so, you possess basic
anatomical knowledge of them, though details

03:12:28.439 --> 03:12:29.639
are clearly faulty.

03:12:29.640 --> 03:12:32.220
In fact, a better question would be...how?

03:12:32.220 --> 03:12:34.980
If, in fact, you are not what you pretend
to be."

03:12:34.979 --> 03:12:39.419
The Not Deer opened its mouth at this, revealing
unusually sharp teeth.

03:12:39.420 --> 03:12:44.340
It moved its jaw as if attempting to speak,
but only a choking sound came out.

03:12:45.479 --> 03:12:46.919
"Shall we move on?"

03:12:46.920 --> 03:12:48.120
Ozz asked.

03:12:48.120 --> 03:12:50.939
"What I'm more concerned with here is why
you take our people.

03:12:50.939 --> 03:12:52.500
Is it a vendetta?

03:12:52.500 --> 03:12:53.399
Spite?

03:12:53.399 --> 03:12:53.939
Food?"

03:12:53.939 --> 03:12:56.700
For the first time in the interview, the Not
Deer blinked.

03:12:56.700 --> 03:13:00.300
It was an unnatural movement,&nbsp;
forced and deliberate,&nbsp;

03:13:00.300 --> 03:13:02.460
like the creature was attempting to engage

03:13:02.460 --> 03:13:07.680
in an ordinary behavior rather than actually
experiencing an involuntary impulse.

03:13:07.680 --> 03:13:11.400
"Responding is mandatory," Researcher Ozz
prompted.

03:13:11.399 --> 03:13:12.899
The creature did not react.

03:13:12.899 --> 03:13:16.679
"If you will not comply," Ozz's tone grew
stern, frustrated.

03:13:16.680 --> 03:13:18.900
"Maybe you'd like to see your brand new&nbsp;&nbsp;

03:13:18.899 --> 03:13:20.040
containment
cell."

03:13:20.040 --> 03:13:21.960
At last, the entity spoke.

03:13:21.960 --> 03:13:28.560
"R-Rasaerch.

03:13:28.560 --> 03:13:30.360
Research."

03:13:30.359 --> 03:13:33.599
Its voice resembled a distorted version of
Ozz's.

03:13:33.600 --> 03:13:34.621
"Research?

03:13:34.620 --> 03:13:36.180
What kind of..."

03:13:36.180 --> 03:13:38.400
Ozz wasn't able to finish his question.

03:13:38.399 --> 03:13:45.059
"July 7, 1947," the creature said, before
ramming into the one-way glass and cracking

03:13:45.060 --> 03:13:45.180
it.

03:13:45.180 --> 03:13:50.280
As Ozz stumbled backward from the force, the
creature collapsed on the ground, seizing

03:13:50.279 --> 03:13:51.540
and screaming as its abdomen.

03:13:51.540 --> 03:13:52.979
"Get the Stags in here now!"

03:13:52.979 --> 03:13:55.379
Ozz cried out, but it was too late.

03:13:55.380 --> 03:14:00.480
A black mass of something shiny and tendriled
leaped out of the Not Deer, scuttling around

03:14:00.479 --> 03:14:04.919
the cell before shattering the window and
leaving the empty shell of a deer behind.

03:14:04.920 --> 03:14:10.800
The Site-44 Breach System activated and attempted
to initiate emergency containment protocols,

03:14:10.800 --> 03:14:15.840
but the mysterious black mass escaped its
sector, made its way toward the main exit,

03:14:15.840 --> 03:14:21.000
broke through the glass on the front exit
door, and vanished into the shrubbery outside.

03:14:21.000 --> 03:14:24.359
The escaped anomaly could not be found and
recontained.

03:14:24.359 --> 03:14:28.679
Ever since this incident, there have been
a record-breaking number of Chronic Wasting

03:14:28.680 --> 03:14:31.440
Disease cases identified&nbsp;
in deer in the surrounding&nbsp;

03:14:31.439 --> 03:14:34.200
area, as well as an unprecedented increase

03:14:34.200 --> 03:14:35.819
in UFO reports.

03:14:35.819 --> 03:14:41.099
Further research is currently ongoing, but
it is unknown whether we will ever truly know

03:14:41.100 --> 03:14:42.300
what these creatures are.

03:14:42.300 --> 03:14:59.279
Only one thing is for certain: they are definitely
not deer.

